{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs","id":207567,"title":"Lunars, Breeding Projects and Lost Eggs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-24T15:03:17-07:00","id":207567,"title":"Lunars, Breeding Projects and Lost Eggs","content":"Seeing as Lunars have the best tools Creation-side to; locate, collect, and breed the Lost Eggs into a might host to bring down the Realm - one wonders why not? Beastmen are a thing that is used and Lunars are the unparalleled masters of all things, &quot;breed that supersoldier&quot;. With the Lunar connection to the land/Gaia and their history both breeding beastmen and being curators of the Age of Dreams Dragonblooded House Armies it seems something they would do. Fight the Realm with their own host of Dragonbloods - laugh mightily at the Sidereals and their pawns as they throw their own upon the field. What are thoughts? It seems PC's often collect 1-2 lost eggs over the course of a short game to be trusted seconds and the like - what says the forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:14:04-07:00","id":207589,"title":"","content":"yes, i always tough why didint the Lunars go all Bene Gesserit and created their own host of DB","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:15:24-07:00","id":207593,"title":"","content":"As with many army-breeding strategies, there are two problems:<br /> 1. Pregnancies and child-raising take time.<br /> 2. How do you control your army of supermen?<br /> <br /> Presumably no lunar has found a solution to both problems that is within their resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 07-24-2014, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:23:33-07:00","id":207596,"title":"","content":"Because expecting Dragon-Blooded, even outcaste lacking the institutional training and logistical support of either the Scarlet Empire or the Seventh Legion, to just fall in line with your plots is likely to result in...a number of complications. They're still Exalted, after all, with larger-than-life goals, agendas, and passions. It's not necessarily an easy sell to convince them to just hang out somewhere and breed rather than pursuing their personal goals, especially if the Lunar isn't offering to help them with those.* On top of the fact that virtually every civilization is &quot;aware&quot; that Lunars are a breed of Anathema, given the spread of Immaculate teachings (even if your society doesn't follow the Immaculate Faith to the extent of the Realm, it's hard to just set aside millennia of stories of heart-drinking demons that wear the skins of men and beasts).<br /> <br /> And I don't think Lunars can just restore the Breeding 5-6 blood purity of the pre-Usurpation time when most (non-PC) outcaste will probably lack Breeding entirely...hell, I don't think even DBs can really replicate that level of blood purity without strict eugenics regimens, a lack of non-DB sexual partners, and infinite time shenanigans. Even then probably not because not everybody will care about someone's grand ole plot especially if it means they have to give up their mortal wife, or are forced to pair up and breed with an opposite-sex DB when they're homosexual, etc.<br /> <br /> Hell, outcastes have good reasons for joining up with the Realm if they're not born there or turned over by their communities (i.e. Paragon and An-Teng at least have a policy of giving discovered DBs to the Realm, at least in part because of Realm policies): they automatically get status, probably training, and likely to get a good job and income. It's a pretty sweet deal for them.<br /> <br /> *I am approaching this question from a narrative perspective, not discussing the implications of 2e social combat convincing them to do so, because that's more interesting to me than having an argument about the bad mechanics associated with infinite brainwashing lasers and UMI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:30:43-07:00","id":207597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207593#post207593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with many army-breeding strategies, there are two problems:<br /> 1. Pregnancies take time.<br /> 2. How do you control your army of supermen?<br /> <br /> Presumably no lunar has found a solution to both problems that is within their resources.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Lunars have already controlled an army of supermen, during the First Age, and the Solar Deliberative broke that. Certainly, no need to tell the Threshold children about any of that. So, I'd say that not only does the Silver Pact have the ability to control the supermen (they are highly skilled at such things as well as having the benefit of historical precedent) but skilled at such things with thousands of years to hone that capability and their technique before Project Wyldhand and other catastrophic failings in public support for the Solar government imploded that influence by association.<br /> <br /> In regard to pregnancies - that is an &quot;issue&quot; with the ever popular Beastmen. An issue that has done nothing to discourage its use and seems to still be in vouge as of the 3E Lunar fiction. Most Lunar Elder have them either directly or by association (Leviathan being all pining away and pure - using his pupils beastmen). Lunars have means to speed pregnancies and they are not overly worried about the wait in Core. Lunar Elders have had at least 800 years of stable hand sitting to take part in such a project.<br /> <br /> If there *is* anything, it would be a stigma against Dragonbloods as a whole due to past experiences. Lunar Elders holding a grudge and burying all that knowledge deep and sitting on it. But, really, I don't see Lunars as lacking pragmatism to that degree and the results would speak for themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:35:59-07:00","id":207602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207596#post207596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because expecting Dragon-Blooded, even outcaste lacking the institutional training and logistical support of either the Scarlet Empire or the Seventh Legion, to just fall in line with your plots is likely to result in...a number of complications.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Realm can just get them to fall in line with its plots? This is how it works in Core. Lost Eggs are collected all the time from the Threshold and there is no issue there when the Realm does it or Lookshy. I believe Yurgen Kaneko is attributed to having several Lost Eggs within his host. Is it just an issue with Lunars have fingers in that cookie jar? Sidereals have fingers all up in that cookie jar, long fingers reaching all the way down from Heaven. Surely it would be easier for Lunars to mess with all that - what with those Lost Eggs in their back yards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:37:10-07:00","id":207603,"title":"","content":"This is happening in my current game. A Lunar NPC named Makisa Dragon-Tamer has been building up a nation to support a breeding population of Dragon-Blooded for the last several centuries. A lot of people in the Thousand Streams River think that she's suicidal or insane, but her association with several powerful older Lunars is keeping her safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:39:25-07:00","id":207605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207593#post207593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you control your army of supermen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Godzilla charms.<br /> <br /> Or, you can just tell them the truth, that most other Dragon-Blooded in Creation are pawns being used by your enemies, and let them decide what they think about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:52:03-07:00","id":207613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207602#post207602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Realm can just get them to fall in line with its plots? This is how it works in Core. Lost Eggs are collected all the time from the Threshold and there is no issue there when the Realm does it or Lookshy. I believe Yurgen Kaneko is attributed to having several Lost Eggs within his host. Is it just an issue with Lunars have fingers in that cookie jar? Sidereals have fingers all up in that cookie jar, long fingers reaching all the way down from Heaven. Surely it would be easier for Lunars to mess with all that - what with those Lost Eggs in their back yards?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some differences there, between the Realm and other powers fostering Lost Eggs. Not just Lunars. And certainly this is a generalization. Any individual Lost Egg could choose to sign up with a Solar warlord, or a Lunar prince, or whatever, if the individual connections are there. I'm talking generally, why many Lost Eggs would see the Realm as the best possible deal for them.<br /> <br /> An outcaste Dragon-Blood taken to the Realm is now among thousands of &quot;her own people.&quot; She will attend a prestigious institution with centuries of experience training Dragon-Bloods. She is worshiped as an intercessor between mortals and Heaven. Many laws flat-out do not apply to her, or what would result in severe punishment for a mortal will be a slap on the wrist for her. If she gets through school, she'll either have a good (if entry-level) job and all the benefits that come with it, or become a monk (and be trained to not care about worldly pursuits to the same degree). If she goes to the legions she'll probably be provided with (state own) artifact weapons and armor; if she goes to the Heptagram, she'll come out a sorcerer (probably), etc. And they'll benefit from the training in skills and enlightenment (represented by Charm and Essence training) of other Dragon-Bloods who know how to foster and teach one of their own optimally. However they will probably have to give up a lot of their own personal plots - if you go to the Realm, you probably won't be able to get revenge on that slaver in Harborhead who kidnapped your mother. Eventually you might get back there, and when you do you'll be in a much better position to kick some ass, but that is definitely going to be delayed if you go to the Realm and work your way up in its institutions. And of course, unless you're adopted by a Great House, you'll only ever go so far.<br /> <br /> An outcaste Dragon-Blood signing on with a Lunar is not signing on with an institution of Lunars. Her Lunar mentor may have friends who really hate Dragon-Bloods. Her mentor may be in control of lands and armies, but likely will not have support equivalent to the Manses, organizations, and armories of the Blessed Isle. There will be an understanding that if the Realm looks too close, her Lunar mentor will become a Wyld Hunt target. You may be more able to pursue your personal agenda--or you might not, depending on how much you're entangled with your mentor's stuff and how much they need you around; presumably they will try to convince you not to go run off to deal with the aforementioned slaver when they're counting on you as a force multiplier in whatever way. Sure, you may be taught sorcery and esoteric martial arts and may command an army in your mentor's name, but you probably don't have access to the ancient Dragon-Blooded arsenals like the Realm would offer, you probably have no shot at getting a good arranged marriage that gives you financial and political benefits (in the Realm, there's always a chance), etc.<br /> <br /> So for a Lunar, or the Bull, or whoever to have Lost Eggs, those Lost Eggs want to be there for some reason. Maybe their mentor saved their life; maybe their mentor was the only parent they knew; maybe their mentor paid them a couple times and they stayed on for consistent money; maybe they're from a remote community and want to stay and protect it because they're invested in it; maybe they lived in a satrapy and have absolutely no interest in working for The Man (figuratively) who's kept a boot on the nation's neck for 500 years, whatever. I'm not saying those aren't perfectly valid reasons to give the bird to the Realm and be off on your own. What I am saying is that when asked &quot;do you want to go to a place where you're treated like a living god,&quot; most people--<i>especially</i> people who have lived kinda shitty lives until Exaltation--are going to say &quot;fuck yes!&quot;<br /> <br /> This is entirely ignoring the satrapies who flat-out handover newly-Exalted DBs (who are usually teenagers, mind) to the Realm. In those cases, the new Exalt probably has no real way to oppose being taken and indoctrinated. Even having grown up in a satrapy, as a vassal to the Realm, suddenly becoming one of those people who runs the show versus just some peasant...it's awful tempting to go and seize the destiny that the Immaculates have preached you're entitled to as a DB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-24-2014, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:53:40-07:00","id":207615,"title":"","content":"The real reason? Because Lunars don't do stuff. Or because they have a pathological hatred of Dragon-Blooded. Or because the Lunars all reverted into animal mentalities and hid. Or they ran into the Wyld and became Fair Folk allies (or enemies, or wardens). The real problem is that Lunars never had a theme, or a firm idea, and the breeding programs is just one idea thrown at the wall that at least stuck a little bit. None of it is terribly well thought out, and most people are just grasping at straws to try to figure out where Lunars fit in a world that was never designed for them (that's where the outsider theme came from). <br /> <br /> In reality, a Lunar could do that no problem. At least, with no more problem than with the other breeding programs they have. It is WAY harder to make Beastmen than to make Dragon-Blooded. And why not Dragon-Blooded beastmen? They'd be no less loyal than in the First Age.<br /> <br /> Here's the real answer to why they wouldn't have done it: The Realm might have noticed, and then the Realm would have absorbed it, and then the Lunars would have had to run away. If they didn't run away, they would have had a major effect in Creation, and that's just not how they roll anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:03:35-07:00","id":207621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207615#post207615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is WAY harder to make Beastmen than to make Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's true. If you want to breed a lot of DBs, you need DB parents with pure blood whose pure blood give their children a higher chance of Exalting. Breeding in more blood purity to consistently get a baby who Exalts itself is going to take time, especially with outcaste &quot;stock&quot; that has thin blood to start. And keeping in mind each potential DB is an investment of at least 12-20 years before you might start to see payoff (since DB Exaltations start around puberty and higher-Breeding tends to make them Exalt younger). The Breeding Background and ranks are a pure OOC meta-construct to put easy reference numbers on something much more complicated and mystical and harder to quantify in-setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207615#post207615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they didn't run away, they would have had a major effect in Creation, and that's just not how they roll anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, bad fluff is bad. To me this discussion is most interesting if you excise the &quot;Lunars are dumb and have done nothing for 2000 years&quot; stuff even if you don't fill in the hole of nothing being done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:15:22-07:00","id":207637,"title":"","content":"For all we know, many Lunars actually have done this. For all we know, there are several powerful Lunar empires of Dragon-Blooded in Creation. People always seem to forgot that what is described in the books is not supposed to be anything more than a fraction of what actually exists in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:16:08-07:00","id":207638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207613#post207613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An outcaste Dragon-Blood taken to the Realm is now among thousands of &quot;her own people.&quot; She will attend a prestigious institution with centuries of experience training Dragon-Bloods. She is worshiped as an intercessor between mortals and Heaven. Many laws flat-out do not apply to her, or what would result in severe punishment for a mortal will be a slap on the wrist for her. .</div> </div> </div> </div>People in the Threshold don't know if Solars are really demons, don't know if half the fancy of the Realm is true, don't know if Heaven exists or if it's just a buncha terrestrial court elementals running the show, many don't even know enough to understand or relate to these examples. I would agree to this if we were talking about people from the inner sea where Realm propaganda is strong. I would agree a bit further out if the character has high lore/occult ratings. Most persons I'm talking about, people from the Threshold, none of that would be the case. The same airy promises any power could offer them - all probably equally accepted. A Realm BD's promise is worth nothing more than a Lunar's promise, and probably less with Appearance Excel/New Friend Aroma and other fairly potent Lunar social tricks.<br /> <br /> As far as laying out everything on the table - it's not a job interview. These guys get snapped up when found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-24-2014, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:21:51-07:00","id":207641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as Lunars have the best tools Creation-side to; locate, collect, and breed the Lost Eggs into a might host to bring down the Realm</div> </div> </div> </div> I see no such thing; please elaborate further. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are the unparalleled masters of all things, &quot;breed that supersoldier&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or maybe not...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:28:07-07:00","id":207646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">People always seem to forgot that what is written in the books is not supposed to be anything more than a fraction of what actually exists in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div> The unspecified corners of Creation aren't supposed to contain things that radically revvaluate the assumed international power dynamics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:30:40-07:00","id":207649,"title":"","content":"Sorry Isator Levi, I've learned not to play this game with you. Maybe another poster in this thread will bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:31:41-07:00","id":207650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207638#post207638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People in the Threshold don't know if Solars are really demons, don't know if half the fancy of the Realm is true, don't know if Heaven exists or if it's just a buncha terrestrial court elementals running the show, many don't even know enough to understand or relate to these examples. I would agree to this if we were talking about people from the inner sea where Realm propaganda is strong. I would agree a bit further out if the character has high lore/occult ratings. Most persons I'm talking about, people from the Threshold, none of that would be the case. The same airy promises any power could offer them - all probably equally accepted. A Realm BD's promise is worth nothing more than a Lunar's promise, and probably less with Appearance Excel/New Friend Aroma and other fairly potent Lunar social tricks.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, I'm mostly talking about places where the Realm either has satrapies at best or regional influence at least. I'm not sure this stuff applies much in the River Province because I don't think Lookshy looks for recruits (but will take them) and a DB can do pretty OK for themselves in Nexus, Great Forks, and other places. Outside of those areas it's likely to me that a DB is going to act like any other Exalt: either taking over his home community or venturing forth for adventure and maybe joining up with other powers as their whims and goals dictate.<br /> <br /> Not going to get into how Lunar Charm mechanics might skew this because of how seriously bad 2e's social mechanics are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207638#post207638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as laying out everything on the table - it's not a job interview. These guys get snapped up when found.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. DBs are more than a commodity, they're Exalted. It's not like buying a wagon of timber. Sure a power might snap them up but there's not a real good way to keep them snapped up if they want to leave. Give them all the bennies you like, it may not be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-24-2014, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T16:36:56-07:00","id":207674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207646#post207646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The unspecified corners of Creation aren't supposed to contain things that radically revvaluate the assumed international power dynamics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you've played Exalted yet, have you? It isn't just the corners. We're told in the 2e core book that everything written in all the books amounts to only a small fraction of Creation. The <b>vast</b> majority is unknown, which means, yeah, there is room for a lot of interesting and powerful peoples and states, and STs love filling it up with them. A few non-Realm, non-Lookshy Dragon-Blooded states don't necessarily change the shape of Creation anyway, especially if they're way out on the edge of the world where Lunar power holds sway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-24-2014, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T17:09:15-07:00","id":207737,"title":"","content":"also there are Linthia DB and no one has a problem with that, so why not some Lunar DB","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T17:40:05-07:00","id":207750,"title":"","content":"This is just a special case of the questions &quot;why aren't the Dragon-Blooded the elite of every large society?&quot; and &quot;why is the proportion of Dragon-Blooded in the world so low?&quot;<br /> <br /> There are a number of answers you can give to those questions, but they're likely to hold for this as well (while not ruling out particular cases.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3457-matthias","name":"Matthias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T17:54:13-07:00","id":207758,"title":"","content":"All right, so, long answer (as best as I understand it):<br /> <br /> At the end of the First Age, if there was any sizable number of Dragon Blooded who retained loyalty to the Solars and Lunars (considering that grievances are supposed to have been widespread, and the Sidereals had been working for some time to set the course of their attitudes), they would have been basically fully destroyed in the establishment of the Shogunate; under the circumstances, it seems as though an end to fighting that would signify a transition of authority wouldn't be possible until they were.<br /> <br /> So then you've got the Shogunate itself, where the Dragon Blooded have established their hegemony, and endeavor to incorporate all of their number into it; there isn't really a social category comparable to Lost Eggs or Outcastes around at the time, everybody is part of the widespread institutions of the Shogunate. At the same time, the Terrestrials are developing their idea of their own inherent spiritual superiority and demonising the Lunars, at the same time as the failing infrastructure is causing increasingly oppressive policies; a lot of Lunars are going to experience the Dragon Blooded first in terms of a life of subjugation beneath them, and of being brutally hunted and ostracised following their Second Breath, and pretty much any Dragon Blood is going to possess a position greater than what Lunars could give them by default, even without viewing Lunars in terms of terrifying monsters who threaten their dominion. There's a lack of opprtunities for Lunars to use Dragon Blooded there, and a lot of bad blood that might make the prospect undesirable besides. This does not mean that there aren't occasional clandestine (and maybe even the extremely rare overt) occasions of alliance between Terrestrials and Lunars; the Shogunate is heavily factionalised, and that makes for marriages of opportunity. It's still a distinct thing from the idea of Lunars raising their own competing groups of Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Then you get to the Age of Sorrows, and that's likely the point where things are most possible but least useful. The numbers of Dragon Blooded and their assets have been gutted; that means that the majority of remaining ones of power all close ranks in the centre (partially for the sake of defence against the scary Lunar Anathema), while the ones who are within reach are scattered and comparatively weak. Centuries of stories about real or imagined atrocities on both sides will have accumulated a lot of weight; a lot of Outcaste Dragon Blooded are still coming up with the social perspective that Lunars are terrifying things and a danger to the safety and stability of the world in general, as well as the sanctity of their enlightened souls, while many Lunars still have issues with the existence of the Terrestrials as a general thing, or at least with the actions that the current crop have perpetrated against them and theirs (or at least form expectations of there being low viability in using them based on such experiences). That's not to say that no Lunars have some measure of power over (or other relationship) with any Outcastes; part of the point of Outcastes is that they're so widespread they find their way into virtually any line of employment (just look at Minton's latest blog post). But it's a bit of an uphill battle, on both sides, not just for overcoming practical barriers or biases between the involved parties, but in the responses of their peer groups (for the sake of argument, imagine how a Lunar who's trying to use Terrestrials loses the support of Leviathan; more concretely how Outcastes associated with Anathema are rather problematic for the Realm).<br /> <br /> Building your own little competitive dynasty of Terrestrials as a Lunar? Virtually impossible; Outcastes are too widely distributed (incidentally, the most common cause of Outcastes grouping together is when a bunch unite around fulfilling the social expectation that they kill Lunars) and their bloodlines are too weak. You'd probably have to gather up a sizable portion of the Outcastes in an entire Direction just to have a good base to start with, and it would still likely take decades or centuries of careful cultivation to start meaningfully increasing their numbers; the Scarlet Dynasty has far superior breeding, and even they seem to carry assumptions that this generally requires carefully selected matches based on collating and comparing numerous factors going several generations back through the family line. If it was as easy as all that, more <i>Dragon Blooded</i> would be trying it for their own benefits, as well as certain management resources like spiritual regiments, dietary information, gynecological knowledge and staff, as well as a sophisticated infrastructure for raising the offspring. Some Lunars might be willing to invest the effort, resources and time required to build up a consistently viable bloodline to reign over, but that's likely to be further compounded by the negative attention it will accumulate, not just from the Realm and other Lunars, but other provincial powers who dislike the idea of a local sept of expanding and self-perpetuating Exalts taking up space. I'd work in an idea for a Lunar who's coming to the fruition of a <i>loooong</i> term project to produce a local bloodline capable of birthing larger numbers of Exalted, but where that part is still on the horizon.<br /> <br /> Besides, such a group still wouldn't quite be competitive with the Scarlet Dynasty; the Exalted of the Realm are richer, more deeply embedded in a highly sophisticated economic, political and military apparatus, and still have better equipment than your local crop does. The value of whatever such subject Dragon Blooded could damage in the Realm is probably not often commensurate with what it would have cost you to build them up; not compared to much cheaper, more easily replenished mortals whom you can clog the Realm's gears up with over a long period of time.<br /> <br /> Beastfolk, in comparison, are super easy; you get (or be) a person and animal to have sex in a suitable area, which then grows like any population of people. Beastfolk aren't even especially useful; I really think the main value they have to Lunars is being a populace they know Realm-run society will marginalize, as well as having cultural aesthetic values that makes it really easy for Lunars to form cults of personality. Tactically speaking, they're not much more useful than any other group of mortals the Lunars might use to tie up Realm military resources while all their cool shit gets broken.<br /> <br /> They're certainly not an indication that Lunars have any particular distinctive or impressive capacity to breed human beings, because again, it's super easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T18:59:39-07:00","id":207800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207674#post207674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you've played Exalted yet, have you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want you to answer this question, Levi. If you expect other people to argue with you, it's only fair that you answer a question once in a while. Have you ever played Exalted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207758#post207758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building your own little competitive dynasty of Terrestrials as a Lunar? Virtually impossible; Outcastes are too widely distributed (incidentally, the most common cause of Outcastes grouping together is when a bunch unite around fulfilling the social expectation that they kill Lunars) and their bloodlines are too weak. You'd probably have to gather up a sizable portion of the Outcastes in an entire Direction just to have a good base to start with, and it would still likely take decades or centuries of careful cultivation to start meaningfully increasing their numbers; the Scarlet Dynasty has far superior breeding, and even they seem to carry assumptions that this generally requires carefully selected matches based on collating and comparing numerous factors going several generations back through the family line. If it was as easy as all that, more <i>Dragon Blooded</i> would be trying it for their own benefits, as well as certain management resources like spiritual regiments, dietary information, gynecological knowledge and staff, as well as a sophisticated infrastructure for raising the offspring. Some Lunars might be willing to invest the effort, resources and time required to build up a consistently viable bloodline to reign over, but that's likely to be further compounded by the negative attention it will accumulate, not just from the Realm and other Lunars, but other provincial powers who dislike the idea of a local sept of expanding and self-perpetuating Exalts taking up space. I'd work in an idea for a Lunar who's coming to the fruition of a <i>loooong</i> term project to produce a local bloodline capable of birthing larger numbers of Exalted, but where that part is still on the horizon.<br /> <br /> Beastfolk, in comparison, are super easy; you get (or be) a person and animal to have sex in a suitable area, which then grows like any population of people. Beastfolk aren't even especially useful; I really think the main value they have to Lunars is being a populace they know Realm-run society will marginalize, as well as having cultural aesthetic values that makes it really easy for Lunars to form cults of personality. Tactically speaking, they're not much more useful than any other group of mortals the Lunars might use to tie up Realm military resources while all their cool shit gets broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm playing a Lunar in two separate games at the moment who comes from a dynastic family. Any child of his, human or beastman, has a good chance of receiving the Exaltation of Mela. He could easily produce hundreds of Terrestrial Exalted without even needing a single drop of dragons' blood other than his own. And that's if I don't create charms for the purpose, building off of the existing Lunar breeding charms, which I would probably try to do if he ever embarked on such a task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-24-2014, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:19:01-07:00","id":207806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207800#post207800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm playing a Lunar in two separate games at the moment who comes from a dynastic family. Any child of his, human or beastman, has a good chance of receiving the Exaltation of Mela. He could easily produce hundreds of Terrestrial Exalted children without even needing a single drop of dragons' blood other than his own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how you figure there's &quot;a good chance&quot; your kids will be DBs. You're a Lunar. You don't have Breeding. If anything, your kids will be Half-Caste. Scroll of Errata spells out the rules for Breeding and chance deterring your child Exalting. I mean, if the ST just goes &quot;you're from a patrician family, your kids will definitely Exalt DB&quot; that's a whole other thing; not sure where your certainty comes from aside from that. Also like you're waiting over a decade, at least, for each kid to become old enough to maybe Exalt. Which most games don't typically give you unless everyone's cool with that kind of timeskip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-24-2014, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:23:30-07:00","id":207810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207637#post207637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all we know, many Lunars actually have done this. For all we know, there are several powerful Lunar empires of Dragon-Blooded in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>One already exists in Dzibilchan, Kingdom of the Crocodile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:24:44-07:00","id":207812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207800#post207800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm playing a Lunar in two separate games at the moment who comes from a dynastic family. Any child of his, human or beastman, has a good chance of receiving the Exaltation of Mela. He could easily produce hundreds of Terrestrial Exalted without even needing a single drop of dragons' blood other than his own. And that's if I don't create charms for the purpose, building off of the existing Lunar breeding charms, which I would probably try to do if he ever embarked on such a task.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a Lunar that has begun to take that path in honor of the Gens of the First Age. Awesome to hear I'm not alone!<br /> <br /> @Zelbinnean <br /> On Half castes - no one uses those, no one I've ever heard of. It takes decades or centuries to save Creation (even a Direction of it) - more game should span more time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-24-2014, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:26:36-07:00","id":207813,"title":"","content":"I don't honestly have a clue how the actual Breeding background would apply in situation - the character didn't start with one, being a Lunar, but presumably the strength of his dragons' blood is still what it would have been if he'd not Exalted. But yes, it would be a process taking decades, of course, and not every descendant would Exalt - not even most. But a Lunar can be patient, and he can have a lot of children if he really puts his mind (and a stamina excellency) to the task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:35:01-07:00","id":207828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207806#post207806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how you figure there's &quot;a good chance&quot; your kids will be DBs. You're a Lunar. You don't have Breeding. If anything, your kids will be Half-Caste. Scroll of Errata spells out the rules for Breeding and chance deterring your child Exalting. I mean, if the ST just goes &quot;you're from a patrician family, your kids will definitely Exalt DB&quot; that's a whole other thing; not sure where your certainty comes from aside from that. Also like you're waiting over a decade, at least, for each kid to become old enough to maybe Exalt. Which most games don't typically give you unless everyone's cool with that kind of timeskip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because in a game of long term plans you can make those time skips.<br /> And it make time some custom charms that fit within similar themes as the beast man breeding charms. but with those you can create your own army of dragon blooded doubly so if you have a manse with a Dragon's Nest in it. Using that you can breed up the chance purity of blood in the children and using a careful breeding program restore the lines to near first age level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:38:35-07:00","id":207829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207613#post207613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An outcaste Dragon-Blood signing on with a Lunar is not signing on with an institution of Lunars. Her Lunar mentor may have friends who really hate Dragon-Bloods. Her mentor may be in control of lands and armies, but likely will not have support equivalent to the Manses, organizations, and armories of the Blessed Isle. There will be an understanding that if the Realm looks too close, her Lunar mentor will become a Wyld Hunt target. You may be more able to pursue your personal agenda--or you might not,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. You might have a total moron trying to recruit you.<br /> <br /> A super soldier who can breed more super soldiers is a valuable asset. Well worth the investment of offering to help kill one slaver. If not simply abducting or luring in said slaver for your prospective recruit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:38:43-07:00","id":207830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207813#post207813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't honestly have a clue how the actual Breeding background would apply in situation - the character didn't start with one, being a Lunar, but presumably the strength of his dragons' blood is still what it would have been if he'd not Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Breeding background is how you determine if your child Exalts, and they added rules in the errata (like the ones that existed in 1e) so people could roll to see if their kid Exalts DB. That's what I'm referencing. Other Exalts aren't reference. Old rule was that Exalting Celestial burned out your Dragon's Blood. Helps prevent dumb shit like a half-Caste Lunar who's also Exalted as a DB or such nonsense.<br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;ST fiat it is!&quot; is fine if your group is fine with it, of course, I just thought you were referencing a rule to back up your assertions and character fluff. I think one patrician parent only means you have to roll a 1 on a d10 for your kid to Exalt (olds improve with DB parents etc).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207812#post207812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Half castes - no one uses those, no one I've ever heard of. It takes decades or centuries to save Creation (even a Direction of it) - more game should span more time.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;No one uses the rules&quot; isn't a real convincing reason to not refer to the rules that govern this particular thing. I mean sure, Half-Caste rules are absolutely terrible! But that's a whole different argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:42:14-07:00","id":207832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207806#post207806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how you figure there's &quot;a good chance&quot; your kids will be DBs. You're a Lunar. You don't have Breeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. If only you could turn into someone that does have breeding.<br /> <br /> Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:44:19-07:00","id":207833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207810#post207810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One already exists in Dzibilchan, Kingdom of the Crocodile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just leave this here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\"> http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:58:33-07:00","id":207839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207830#post207830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Breeding background is how you determine if your child Exalts, and they added rules in the errata (like the ones that existed in 1e) so people could roll to see if their kid Exalts DB. That's what I'm referencing. Other Exalts aren't reference. Old rule was that Exalting Celestial burned out your Dragon's Blood. Helps prevent dumb shit like a half-Caste Lunar who's also Exalted as a DB or such nonsense.<br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;ST fiat it is!&quot; is fine if your group is fine with it, of course, I just thought you were referencing a rule to back up your assertions and character fluff. I think one patrician parent only means you have to roll a 1 on a d10 for your kid to Exalt (olds improve with DB parents etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think of it as fluff. The character is a descendant of Mela. Both his siblings as well as his parents are Air Aspects. His blood is that of the Dragon of Strife. Therefore, his descendants would have a good chance of receiving her Grace. I'm not overly concerned with how the dice rolls would work. If I wanted to have kids and the ST decided I needed a Breeding background, presumably I'd be allowed to buy into it with XP, or I'd create some charms (in the nature of Terrestrial Bloodline Integration or Tiger-and-Seahorse Dynasty) to achieve the effect I wanted. A large part of any Exalted game is ST fiat; that's just the way it is when you're dealing with demigod PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-24-2014, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T22:00:35-07:00","id":207909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207839#post207839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think of it as fluff. The character is a descendant of Mela.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people are. His heritage in this matter, however, is so thin that it doesn't show.<br /> <br /> Also, raising Breeding is only accomplished through a potentially lethal ritual allowed only by an elder-level Dragon-Blooded Presence Charm, which requires the user to have either perfect Breeding or else they have to use it on themself until they do. Meaning that the few candidates capable of doing so could potentially kill themselves just getting built up to use it on others. It automatically kills mortals, and has no effect on Celestials, even if they do have the Terrestrial Heritage merit, This part of the rules system is structured and established, demigods or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T22:04:43-07:00","id":207912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207909#post207909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of people are. His heritage in this matter, however, is so thin that it doesn't show.<br /> <br /> Also, raising Breeding is only accomplished through a potentially lethal ritual allowed only by an elder-level Dragon-Blooded Presence Charm, which requires the user to have either perfect Breeding or else they have to use it on themself until they do. Meaning that the few candidates capable of doing so could potentially kill themselves just getting built up to use it on others. It automatically kills mortals, and has no effect on Celestials, even if they do have the Terrestrial Heritage merit, This part of the rules system is structured and established, demigods or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunars maintained the First Age Gens - they would have charms. Fluff is the best reason for a charm to exist - fits the story and lore better than even many written charms. Just cause it is not in a book means next to nothing, particularly for a splat like Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T00:24:08-07:00","id":207973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207758#post207758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...loses the support of Leviathan...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Had to laugh at this one. His support is, as it is, worth all of nothing. Has not been to a Silver Pact meeting in for like a thousand years. Leviathan is worst Lunar, Swims in Shadows and his Squid bro do everything in Luthe. Those two would be worth 10 Leviathans in any game I can think of. Leviathan's eyes are focused squarely in Luthe and he emotes and communicates nothing to the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> Lunars are far far too pragmatic to turn their backs on a tool or weapon as useful as the Dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T01:03:59-07:00","id":207991,"title":"","content":"Actually there are canonical beastman groups (direction book east, I think) that have dragon blooded and there were the crocodile men dragon blooded. I think there are two factors here: 1. doing this in a big way really gets you on the Siddies &quot;kill now&quot; list. The lunar behind the crocodile man project attracted no less a personage that Kejak after all. <br /> 2. It takes a long time. <br /> <br /> But equally, it should be eminantly doable. Lunars can summon neomah, they live for thousands of years, they have access to hidden redoubts in the Wyld, so they should be able to create armies of dragonblooded. The reason they don't is the same reason that the Realm, despite supposedly trying to incrase the numbers of DB, doesn't have hundreds of thousands-- in game fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T01:05:17-07:00","id":207993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207830#post207830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, &quot;ST fiat it is!&quot; is fine if your group is fine with it, of course, I just thought you were referencing a rule to back up your assertions and character fluff. I think one patrician parent only means you have to roll a 1 on a d10 for your kid to Exalt (olds improve with DB parents etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, TSk's patrician Lunar's children only have a 10% chance of Exalting as DBs if he sleeps with a regular mortal.<br /> <br /> All that means is that he needs to have <i>a lot more than ten children</i>. In terms of a monogamous marriage, that's pretty hard to pull off quickly without a spouse who's Exalted or divine, but I don't think Creation is a place where super-beings of any stripe put a heavy emphasis on marital monogamy, particularly those which have &quot;breeding program&quot; (however icky that is) as part of their schtick.<br /> <br /> To draw a parallel from real life, Genghis Khan apparently has sixteen million male descendants today; one would assume also an equal number of female descendants, but the testing is done on the Y-chromosome. He died 800 years ago, give or take, so that's 800 years to produce 32 million descendants. Pretty impressive for a dude who spent much of his childhood starving and homeless.<br /> <br /> Coincidentally, it's been approximately 800 years since the Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusade. Plenty of time for a Lunar with traces of DB blood to start seducing everyone of his/her/hir breeding-appropriate gender(s). Given that both Lunars and DBs fought to the end against the infinite hordes of the Wyld, it would be entirely possible for some few of them to overcome their respective prejudices, particularly if they wind up on the (new) border of Creation, still endangered by the remnants of Balor's forces.<br /> <br /> It's entirely fair to assume large Lunar-led kingdoms run into opposition from the Realm and the Sidereals, and that they usually lose, but denying the possibility of Lunar-DB team-ups or lineages is a fairly extremist position. I'm fairly sure 3E will show us a lot more of these situations, particularly with the large new Lunar kingdoms showing up (c.f. the Caul).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:49:56-07:00","id":208155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">His support is, as it is, worth all of nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a reason I prefaced the line with &quot;for the sake of argument&quot;; that whole post is made of broad suppositions of the depiction of characters and scenarios based on what we've been told about the portrayal of Lunars (and Dragon Blooded) in the new Edition. If there's going to be a point about how a significant reason that the Silver Pact maintains a measure of unity in destroying the Realm because of the personal vendettas of the most ancient Lunars, I imagine that requires all hands on deck. That doesn't even quite require one to fully drop the characterisation of Leviathan as a bit withdrawn and bitter; all he needs are assets that might draw other Lunars to him, and certain wants that can be leveraged for them. Associating with Terrestrials doesn't even need to be a thing of consequence with him, just a matter of choosing different paths down an adventure novel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:59:44-07:00","id":208158,"title":"","content":"Mostly, while I don't expect or particularly want a comprehensive ruling on how the breeding of Terrestrial Exalted works, I like to interpret the information as presented in First Edition in terms that produce rules based around preserving their interpersonal family dynamics and the limitations of their society, rather than have them disappear inside assumptions that it's possible and optimal to indiscriminately produce massive numbers of them, whether it be through ridiculous manses, or converting women into immobile brood sows who'll live for a thousand years and reproduce like rodents, or being a Celestial Exalt with notable breeding (or even just a Dragon Blooded man who prolifically has sex). Nothing based on gaming statistics. Nothing that dehumanises and depersonalizes the Terrestrial Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T05:20:33-07:00","id":208170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207603#post207603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is happening in my current game. A Lunar NPC named Makisa Dragon-Tamer has been building up a nation to support a breeding population of Dragon-Blooded for the last several centuries. A lot of people in the Thousand Streams River think that she's suicidal or insane, but her association with several powerful older Lunars is keeping her safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair to them, going by the title Dragon-Tamer probably isn't the wisest of moves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T06:14:10-07:00","id":208212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207909#post207909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, raising Breeding is only accomplished through a potentially lethal ritual allowed only by an elder-level Dragon-Blooded Presence Charm, which requires the user to have either perfect Breeding or else they have to use it on themself until they do. Meaning that the few candidates capable of doing so could potentially kill themselves just getting built up to use it on others. It automatically kills mortals, and has no effect on Celestials, even if they do have the Terrestrial Heritage merit, This part of the rules system is structured and established, demigods or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like how the Past Life Background is only available to Infernals. But I don't know a single ST who doesn't rule otherwise. I wasn't talking about 'raising breeding', anyway. As I said, his breeding should be the same as it would have been before Lunar Exaltation, which is excellent. The idea that Celestial Exaltation wipes away Breeding is, to me, kind of silly. I can understand why it might be put into the books, as a barrier to twinks, but it's the kind of thing responsible players and storytellers are better off just ignoring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T06:58:22-07:00","id":208255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207912#post207912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars maintained the First Age Gens - they would have charms. Fluff is the best reason for a charm to exist - fits the story and lore better than even many written charms. Just cause it is not in a book means next to nothing, particularly for a splat like Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars maintained the First Age Gens - I don't recall a statement to this effect, do you have a book reference?<br /> <br /> In any case I feel like &quot;make it more likely that my kid will Exalt DB&quot; is a valid theme for DB Charms, and wholly out of theme for Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208212#post208212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that Celestial Exaltation wipes away Breeding is, to me, kind of silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208212#post208212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">t it's the kind of thing responsible players and storytellers are better off just ignoring.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is treading into Rule Zero territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-25-2014, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:14:38-07:00","id":208281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208255#post208255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the blood of Gaia is not so weak that it flees before the touch of a mere god, even a god so great as Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:59:12-07:00","id":208319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208281#post208281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the blood of Gaia is not so weak that it flees before the touch of a mere god, even a god so great as Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the way you want to play it, so be it. That's a valid interpretation of the fluff, but I could just as well say &quot;the lunar essence that suffuses you upon Exaltation burns away all lesser spiritual energies&quot; - which is also why you can't be both an Exalt and a half-caste, or an Exalt and a godblood with charms. In either case, we're each just telling the stories we want to tell.<br /> <br /> I also have a metagame reason: Lunars can't breed a DB army because I don't <i>want</i> anyone - lunar or otherwise - to control an army of superbeings that consists largely of their children and/or grandchildren, unless they themselves are a terrible monster. As a corollary, I want to discourage making Lunars who are terrible monsters, and I <i>especially</i> want to discourage the idea that terrible monster Lunars are the archetypal Lunars.<br /> <br /> Again, telling the stories we want to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:12:25-07:00","id":208334,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm not sure if someone said that already (too many posts to read in such a short time :P) but I think the main reason the Lunars won't try to make &quot;their own army of Dragons&quot; is not some pathological hate or something like that- but the fact that they have seen how it failed. The Usurpation was the event when they saw how the weakest among the Exalted defeated their masters, the strongest among the Chosen. How could the Lunars make sure that history won't repeat itself, and that their own army won't turn against them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:30:41-07:00","id":208358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208212#post208212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just like how the Past Life Background is only available to Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not just like it. Breeding is a rather intrinsic trait of the Terrestrial Exaltation. Past Lives explicitly is the result of a Celestial Exaltation not being scrubbed between time empowering a legacy of heroes. Breeding requires a Terrestrial Exaltation. Please note that its mechanical effects include boosts to Essence pools, which is almost certainly something that you don't want to deal with piling onto other Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I don't know a single ST who doesn't rule otherwise. I wasn't talking about 'raising breeding', anyway. As I said, his breeding should be the same as it would have been before Lunar Exaltation, which is excellent. The idea that Celestial Exaltation wipes away Breeding is, to me, kind of silly. I can understand why it might be put into the books, as a barrier to twinks, but it's the kind of thing responsible players and storytellers are better off just ignoring. </div> </div> </div>Mortals don't get Breeding as a Background, so it technically doesn't wipe it away. You can get Terrestrial Heritage, and count as a well-bred patrician, or have no significant measure at all. That's the extent to which those who do not carry enough blood of the dragons to be Exalted carry the blood of the dragons. The Breeding Background denotes that you've taken after a powerful lineage of Terrestrial Exalted, by being, first and foremost, Terrestrial Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:34:38-07:00","id":208365,"title":"","content":"Having it skip a generation (ie the child of a mortal with two dragonblooded parents of reasonably high breeding) seems perfectly justifiable to me, So the idea of mortals with a terrestrial bloodline possessing &quot;phantom breeding&quot; that doesn't do anything but determine that of their offspring is a viable concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:05:41-07:00","id":208427,"title":"","content":"you know, in 3ed Breeding is going out the window, its going to give you some social bonus but it has nothing to do with the chances of a child to exalt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:14:29-07:00","id":208434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208427#post208427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know, in 3ed Breeding is going out the window, its going to give you some social bonus but it has nothing to do with the chances of a child to exalt</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that announcement somewhere, but that's good. Breeding was the most egregious &quot;must-buy Background&quot; for DBs due to the extra motes it provided. I assume that's also out the window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:21:18-07:00","id":208439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208319#post208319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have a metagame reason: Lunars can't breed a DB army because I don't <i>want</i> anyone - lunar or otherwise - to control an army of superbeings that consists largely of their children and/or grandchildren, unless they themselves are a terrible monster. As a corollary, I want to discourage making Lunars who are terrible monsters, and I <i>especially</i> want to discourage the idea that terrible monster Lunars are the archetypal Lunars.<br /> <br /> Again, telling the stories we want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Lunars are terrible monsters. Some Lunars do control armies of their offspring. Do Lunars like Ma-Ha-Suchi not exist in your games?<br /> <br /> And if someone in your game plays an ex-Dynastic Lunar, and he has a child, you do not allow that child any more chance of Terrestrial Exaltation even though it's a member of the Scarlet Dynasty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-25-2014, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:37:44-07:00","id":208446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208334#post208334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm not sure if someone said that already (too many posts to read in such a short time :P) but I think the main reason the Lunars won't try to make &quot;their own army of Dragons&quot; is not some pathological hate or something like that- but the fact that they have seen how it failed. The Usurpation was the event when they saw how the weakest among the Exalted defeated their masters, the strongest among the Chosen. How could the Lunars make sure that history won't repeat itself, and that their own army won't turn against them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lore really sells that as more the Solars and the Lunars just got taken down cause they were so close to them. Lunars are all about raising up powerful and self-sufficient societies that don't need a butt load of Solar maintained magictech and bs. Lunars should not be worried about rebellion through cause of their own error at this point in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:50:02-07:00","id":208453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208439#post208439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Lunars are terrible monsters. Some Lunars do control armies of their offspring. Do Lunars like Ma-Ha-Suchi not exist in your games?<br /> <br /> And if someone in your game plays an ex-Dynastic Lunar, and he has a child, you do not allow that child any more chance of Terrestrial Exaltation even though it's a member of the Scarlet Dynasty?</div> </div> </div> </div>They exist, but their narrative role (if they're mentioned at all) generally falls into one of three categories: they're either something to avoid, to kill at any cost, or to be an extremely dubious and untrustworthy ally. These characters are not role models and I'm not sure I'd want to play with anyone who felt inspired to follow their example.<br /> <br /> If someone in my group plays an Ex-Dynastic Lunar with a kid, and the kid isn't a half-caste, I'd give that child a chance of Terrestrial Exaltation in proportion to how much their Exaltation would be useful to the story. In the specific case of the player who wants 1000 baby dragons at their beck and call, we'd probably have to have a talk about their Motivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:51:05-07:00","id":208454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208439#post208439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if someone in your game plays an ex-Dynastic Lunar, and he has a child, you do not allow that child any more chance of Terrestrial Exaltation even though it's a member of the Scarlet Dynasty?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two schools of thought here which kind of mirror the biggest schools of thought for Exalted playstyle. Neither is right or wrong; they're merely different vectors for storytelling and approaches to the game.<br /> <br /> Simulationist: apply the rules, which in 2e are &quot;roll a die.&quot; Lunar might be counted as a patrician with good heritage for purposes of the roll, meaning the child will Exalt on a roll of 1, or 1-2 if the other parent is also a patrician of good heritage. In 1e, there was a table, I think in the Player's Guide, that spelled out the Breeding rolls for DBs, different results in Exalt-Exalt pairings based on the parents' Essence and the primacy of &quot;genetics&quot; if the parents were different kinds of Exalts but equal Essence (Solaroid &gt; Lunar = Sidereal &gt; DB). This is the rule, and it's based on random chance, but that's kind of realistic in the world? A well-bred patrician is still not a Dragon-Blood and even the most well-bred patrician doesn't have as much inherent &quot;genetic&quot; power within them as a &quot;mudblood&quot; Outcaste does, because the fact of the matter is the Outcaste Exalted DB, and the patrician didn't. Even coming from a long line of Dragon-Blooded, a patrician is still not a DB, meaning the Blood of the Dragons didn't catalyze within them to Exalt them Terrestrial, for whatever reason (being superseded by a Celestial Exaltation would do that). Honestly under the rules if you have a former-Realm patrician Lunar and a mortal having a child, that child is much more likely going to be a Lunar Half-Caste, especially if the Lunar is higher Essence.<br /> <br /> Narrativist: here the main question is &quot;how does the child's ultimately Exalting (or not) serve the story?&quot; Keeping in mind that this question won't be answered for over a decade in-game (I've rarely seen games go that long IC, though timeskips might happen I've only heard of it happening a handful of times; usually a game either successfully ends and this is played out inane epilogue, or dies and the question is never answered). Relevant concerns include: is it more compelling that the Lunar's child Exalts as a DB, or shows himself to be a Half-Caste? What's the player's preference? Even with the player's preference, what is the story the ST wants to explore? That would probably be a thing best discussed early in the game or at chargen, for the ST to have the idea in their head and be able to weave it into their overarching story. By this I mean that a player is free to tell the ST &quot;I would like my kid to ultimately be a DB&quot; but the player is not <i>entitled</i> to that outcome (no more than they are entitled to any plot-based outcome), and the outcome might narratively depend on other factors like the nature of the other parent even if there is not a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:56:25-07:00","id":208471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208453#post208453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They exist, but their narrative role (if they're mentioned at all) generally falls into one of three categories: they're either something to avoid, to kill at any cost, or to be an extremely dubious and untrustworthy ally. These characters are not role models and I'm not sure I'd want to play with anyone who felt inspired to follow their example.</div> </div> </div> </div>At what point did I say they were a role model?<br /> <br /> The question on this thread is why no Lunars have done this over the last 800 years. Some say it's impossible, to them I point to my Lunar dynast to show how possible it is. But my Lunar hasn't had any kids and isn't interested in kids, and if he was, he wouldn't be interested in breeding an army. I'm sure it's not a project that any Lunar in a game I run will undertake, either. But that doesn't make it impossible. If you say it's impossible, then you have to start censoring out the existence of Lunars like Ma-Ha-Suchi from your games, which I don't want to do either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208453#post208453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone in my group plays an Ex-Dynastic Lunar with a kid, and the kid isn't a half-caste, I'd give that child a chance of Terrestrial Exaltation in proportion to how much their Exaltation would be useful to the story..</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is probably what I would do. And if the player <i>wanted</i> a Terrestrial child I'd simply let them have one and treat them like any other NPC relative. I wouldn't tell them they can't, it's impossible, Lunar magic forbids it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:01:56-07:00","id":208473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208358#post208358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals don't get Breeding as a Background, so it technically doesn't wipe it away. You can get Terrestrial Heritage, and count as a well-bred patrician, or have no significant measure at all. That's the extent to which those who do not carry enough blood of the dragons to be Exalted carry the blood of the dragons. The Breeding Background denotes that you've taken after a powerful lineage of Terrestrial Exalted, by being, first and foremost, Terrestrial Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any rule that says a mortal dynast &quot;counts as a patrician&quot; for any purposes is a rule I'm comfortable ignoring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:05:23-07:00","id":208478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208473#post208473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any rule that says a mortal dynast &quot;counts as a patrician&quot; for any purposes is a rule I'm comfortable ignoring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's exactly what a patrician is. &quot;Patrician&quot; is shorthand for &quot;Dynastic Great House member who is not Exalted.&quot; It is supposed to be evocative of the patrician (i.e. nobility) class of the Roman Republic. This is kind of a Rule Zero Fallacy? It's cool if you want to ignore the rules, but when you're talking &quot;why has no Lunar in Creation done this,&quot; you're talking about the game, which in part necessitates talking about the rules. Also just because you ignore a rule doesn't mean that everyone or even most people will...<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about a narrative perspective, I typed this yesterday, didn't post it, but maybe it's relevant now:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207674#post207674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I don't think you've ever played a game of Exalted, have you? It's not just the corners. We're told in the 2e core book that everything detailed in all the books is only a small fraction of the entirety of Creation. A small fraction means the vast majority is undescribed. And yeah, that's room for a lot of nations, cultures and states, many of them unique, interesting and powerful. A few non-Realm, non-Lookshy Dragon-Blooded states doesn't necessarily change the shape of Creation anyway.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Such a place as you describe would have to be the corners of the Threshold far from Realm and/or Bronze Faction Sidereal scrutiny (just as a note; the All-Seeing Eye is presumed to be competent, and the Bronze Faction is presumed to have enough interest in the Realm to clandestinely tip them off to something of this nature if they discover it), or it would have to be supernaturally well-hidden (say, like the Caul in 3e). If the Realm were to learn about some new region that had a concentrated number of DBs in it, they would certainly move to try and either form an alliance or outright bring those DBs into their fold. I'm not necessarily talking war (though they might threaten if negotiations didn't go anywhere and they felt threatened somehow) but they'd certainly send spies, envoys, and lavish things to help convince the Lost Egg State that it's in their great interest to be supported by the largest DB nation in Creation. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u200b</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I mean, look at their response to a Circle of Solars doing shit they didn't like kind of far out there in the northern Threshold. When the Realm sees something it considers a big deal (like, say, a group of Anathema raising armies, or some just-discovered country that has a ton of DBs that have been bred for the past 800 years), their response is not...moderate. They could certainly go further if they tried int he Scavenger Lands, because Lookshy would probably prefer alliance over bringing them into the Legion structure, but Lookshy still doesn't like Anathema.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-25-2014, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:06:49-07:00","id":208479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208471#post208471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question on this thread is why no Lunars have done this over the last 800 years. Some say it's impossible, to them I point to my Lunar dynast to show how possible it is. But my Lunar hasn't had any kids and isn't interested in kids, and if he was, he wouldn't be interested in breeding an army. I'm sure it's not a project that any Lunar in a game I run will undertake, either. But that doesn't make it impossible. If you say it's impossible, then you have to start censoring out the existence of Lunars like Ma-Ha-Suchi from your games, which I don't want to do either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is impossible - I just said that I didn't want to play a game scenario where it could happen, or did happen. I can sort of handwave these circumstances by saying something like &quot;Well, the stars didn't align the right way in the last 800 years - we couldn't get a Lunar with good breeding AND the will to breed an army AND who didn't get killed AND was actually competent and had resources enough to pull it off&quot; - but if you're asking me to find an explicit or implicit justification or the lack of Lunar-Dragonblood armies in the fluff or the mechanics of 2E, I don't have anything for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:19:58-07:00","id":208492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208478#post208478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bronze Faction Sidereal scrutiny</div> </div> </div> </div>Bronze Faction, and the Realm for that matter, has little to no power in the Threshold. After the Contagion they pulled back to the Realm and have not been able to effectively police Lunars since. Lunars have Wyld Quests and such, and the #1 way Sidereals die is to Lunars when they do down to Creation bar none. Lunars are not cowering in their collective boots at Sidereals, and they do know about them, nor would they avoid any project in the Threshold for that reason. Ma Ha is totally proof of that, Leviathan is proof of that, the Hislanti League is proof of that, Tamuz is proof of Lunar cleverness, and for those willing to accept Halta - it's pretty O.P.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208478#post208478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernaturally well-hidden (say, like the Caul in 3e)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not hidden, there is a large Realm city on the island and it is more an issue of Lunar power that they can not deal with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-25-2014, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:21:07-07:00","id":208494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208478#post208478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's exactly what a patrician is. &quot;Patrician&quot; is shorthand for &quot;Dynastic Great House member who is not Exalted.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, patrician families and Dynastic families are separate. An un-Exalted dynast is still a dynast. And a patrician family would have to pay a fortune to have one of their children marry one. At least, that's the way it was in 2nd Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:22:04-07:00","id":208495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208427#post208427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know, in 3ed Breeding is going out the window, its going to give you some social bonus but it has nothing to do with the chances of a child to exalt</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't quite right. The social benefits are in, but what Breeding loses are the extra motes Zelbinnean was talking about that made it feel like a must-buy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e Breeding is probably going to be a fixed-cost Merit denoting good breeding, and conferring social advantages in Dynastic society and a greater likelihood of your kids Exalting. The 1e/2e Breeding Background, while it made sense as a setting expression given the importance of strong blood for the Dragon-Blooded... as a game element, it had all the problems of Generation and none of the benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:24:17-07:00","id":208497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208494#post208494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, patrician families and Dynastic families are separate. An un-Exalted dynast is still a dynast. And a patrician family would have to pay a fortune to have one of their children marry one. At least, that's the way it was in 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case I'm comfortable assuming that the Scroll of Errata wording boils down to a semantic issue equating &quot;patrician&quot; with &quot;non-DB Great House member,&quot; since &quot;Dynast&quot; is overwhelmingly used as shorthand for &quot;Realm DB&quot; in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:30:08-07:00","id":208500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208492#post208492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bronze Faction, and the Realm for that matter, has little to no power in the Threshold. After the Contagion they pulled back to the Realm and have not been able to effectively police Lunars since. Lunars have Wyld Quests and such, and the #1 way Sidereals die is to Lunars when they do down to Creation bar none. Lunars are not cowering in their collective boots at Sidereals, and they do know about them, nor would they avoid any project in the Threshold for that reason. Ma Ha is totally proof of that, Leviathan is proof of that, the Hislanti League is proof of that, Tamuz is proof of Lunar cleverness, and for those willing to accept Halta - it's pretty O.P.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, fair enough, I was thinking more that a single Lunar in societies (like Tamuz, Gerd Marrow-Eater, Ma-Ha-Suchi, Raksi, Rain Deathflyer and Silver Python each basically having their own sphere is influence) is going to be hard to find/notice first of all, but a Lunar surrounded by a small army of DBs they've been breeding is probably going to ping the Loom or whatever from Essence expenditure. But maybe if it's far enough away from the Isle they won't care. I'm trying to remember the circumstances where the Realm really started to care about the Bull; I know the Wyld Hunt is usually just opportunistic (i.e. glowing thing in a place, send the local garrisons to deal with it first and that usually works). I just can't remember what the bull did to draw the attention of the Legions aside from uniting the Icewalkers, but I recall it was big and involved Samea nuking shit with sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:34:59-07:00","id":208501,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the SoE, but in the 2e core, pag 44 it says: &quot;Patrician are considered nobles in the Realm because they are descendants of one of the Exalts of the Scarlet Dynasty.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:37:42-07:00","id":208502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208497#post208497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case I'm comfortable assuming that the Scroll of Errata wording boils down to a semantic issue equating &quot;patrician&quot; with &quot;non-DB Great House member,&quot; since &quot;Dynast&quot; is overwhelmingly used as shorthand for &quot;Realm DB&quot; in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could certainly have been written better.<br /> <br /> But yeah, even if you don't exalt, being a dynast means your blood is better than any patrician's. If two dynastic Dragon-Bloods marry and have three children, and only two of them Exalt, it's not a difference in blood that keeps the third from Exalting; it was just not his fate. but he remains a Sesus, or a Tepet. He might be married to a patrician, but if so, the patrician's parents will have to pay through the nose for the honor of marrying into the Scarlet Dynasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-25-2014, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:53:19-07:00","id":208528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208500#post208500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to remember the circumstances where the Realm really started to care about the Bull...but I recall it was big and involved Samea nuking shit with sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly flying an army a couple thousand miles using Celestial Circle Sorc. to attack Rokan-Jin which was a neighbor of the Linowan who they care a *lot* about. Even that mighta been ok, but Semea summoned like 2-3 Second Circle Demons during that conquest too...so really it's Samea they worry about not Yurgen. That the Tiger Warriors trashed the Realm Legion is worrisome but also super circumspect. I believe the books imply the Empress undermined the Tepet somehow there, cause the Realm shoulda won a battle in terms of man power vs man power.<br /> <br /> But ya, the Realm is more worried about Samea than Yurgan. Celestial Circle spells be bs yo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T12:06:29-07:00","id":208537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208528#post208528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly flying an army a couple thousand miles using Celestial Circle Sorc. to attack Rokan-Jin which was a neighbor of the Linowan who they care a *lot* about. Even that mighta been ok, but Semea summoned like 2-3 Second Circle Demons during that conquest too...so really it's Samea they worry about not Yurgen. That the Tiger Warriors trashed the Realm Legion is worrisome but also super circumspect. I believe the books imply the Empress undermined the Tepet somehow there, cause the Realm shoulda won a battle in terms of man power vs man power.<br /> <br /> But ya, the Realm is more worried about Samea than Yurgan. Celestial Circle spells be bs yo.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside I wonder how 3e is going to rejigger that fluff considering dev statements on significantly toning back long-distance sorcerous travel options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T12:16:26-07:00","id":208548,"title":"","content":"Hmm, at least one advantage I can see in Breeding being a fixed-cost Merit is that it disassociates the idea of its mechanical scale matching precisely to how good it's supposed to be in-character. So having the Merit means you have some nebulous quality of &quot;good breeding&quot; which is not only fairly complicated from inside the setting, but also means different things for different characters.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with the idea of Celestial Exalted having that Merit, and thus being able to have Dragon Blooded children, albeit only with any kind of reliability if they get involved in the usual Dynastic matchmaking, and not with assumptions that their greater lifespans or whatever necessarily make them superior at having large numbers of Exalted children, at least on any meaningful time scale (like, if you have a dozen or so Exalted children in one century, and repeat it several centuries later, by about a time when the prior batch have passed on, it doesn't make much difference). I don't think they should be able to game probabilities with anything like &quot;sure my bloodline is weak, but if only one percent of my children Exalt and I have 10,000 children, I'll get a hundred Exalts&quot;. I think the heredity should be a bit more mystical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T12:41:31-07:00","id":208571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208537#post208537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside I wonder how 3e is going to rejigger that fluff considering dev statements on significantly toning back long-distance sorcerous travel options.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would certainly make Lunars more potent. Harder to corner or contest something that takes a Peregrine Falcon form and cruises at ~65mph before speed enhancer charms, mutations, up and coming monster abilities (like Tyrant Lizards track prey in a direction deal). I suppose this makes me happy - in a lotta games its just sorcerous chariot everywhere. Which is frustrating cause the cloud and other transport spells are hugely inferior to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T13:30:15-07:00","id":208601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208548#post208548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they should be able to game probabilities with anything like &quot;sure my bloodline is weak, but if only one percent of my children Exalt and I have 10,000 children, I'll get a hundred Exalts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one suggested anything like that. Even treating my Lunar as a patrician, without charms or Breeding and with the lowest possible odds, it would be ten times more effective than that, 10% instead of 1%, and a thousand instead of a hundred. And I'd assume anyone who tried doing that would want to improve the odds somehow.<br /> <br /> Building up dynasties and creating empires is a legitimate thing people do in games. It's not something I'm interested in, and I've never played a game that took place over a sufficiently large stretch of time that it would even be possible, but if someone wanted to run and play a game like that, or had an NPC Lunar who embarked on such a project, I have absolutely no problem with them. And Makisa Dragon-Tamer sounds awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T14:46:24-07:00","id":208705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207597#post207597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars have already controlled an army of supermen, during the First Age</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>commanded</i> a super army.<br /> <br /> That is an entirely different beast than <i>controlling</i> a super army. To command an army merely requires the army's consent to be commanded. To control an army means having the power to make their consent irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted cannot make Terrestrial Exalted irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T14:49:09-07:00","id":208706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208705#post208705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>commanded</i> a super army.<br /> <br /> That is an entirely different beast than <i>controlling</i> a super army. To command an army merely requires the army's consent to be commanded. To control an army means having the power to make their consent irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted cannot make Terrestrial Exalted irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Command is a better word, sorry. However, Sidereals *do* control them. So if anyone makes Dragonbloods irrelevant, its the Sidereals, where in they are just cat's-paws and unwitting lackeys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T14:59:22-07:00","id":208732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208706#post208706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Command is a better word, sorry. However, Sidereals *do* control them. So if anyone makes Dragonbloods irrelevant, its the Sidereals, where in they are just cat's-paws and unwitting lackeys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not accurate. Sidereals don't control DBs, they manipulate them. There is a difference. If anyone in recent history has <i>controlled</i> DBs, it was the Scarlet Empress. Who herself was not controlled by Sidereals, but was instead a party to a beneficial arrangement with the Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T15:15:42-07:00","id":208750,"title":"","content":"My two cents if anyone wants it. I would never have a problem with a PC having this as a goal. I'll throw obstacles in the way, of course. I will put limits on what the Lunar can do directly, such as no adopting a DB form and making babies. I count that as an essence power, and you don't get those from taking the form. I know that might seem unfair, because the Lunar CAN pass on traits, but I would consider this an expression of the Exaltation itself, and the Lunar doesn't actually get that. <br /> <br /> My biggest concern is that my campaign wouldn't run long enough for that to happen. I would gladly let the PC in, but I would warn him up front that the campaign timeline might end long before his plan comes to fruition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T15:25:05-07:00","id":208760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208732#post208732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not accurate. Sidereals don't control DBs, they manipulate them. There is a difference. If anyone in recent history has <i>controlled</i> DBs, it was the Scarlet Empress. Who herself was not controlled by Sidereals, but was instead a party to a beneficial arrangement with the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>No difference in respect to the Moonsilver Doomtrain's meaning. Doing another's bidding without ever knowing, over hundreds of years, just dancing to those strings...still sidelines Dragonbloods and their victories.<br /> <br /> Zel, I have a question. Been on these forums for years, and I have to wonder, why can people support every faction but Lunars. I mean really, if Lunars are so worthless and destined to fail - to have no meaningful connections to anything in the game (go play in the Wyld) why even include them. If they are not meant to fight their enemies the Sidereals (but be victims forever), if they are not meant to make something or sway Dragonbloods (who have been swayed by Solars and Sidereals over thousands of years), if they are not meant to be the strong second who questions and even overturns his commanders words when he is wrong (rather than a bonded suplicant) - what do you want them to do? Do you really want them to sit in the Boardermarches playing with Fairfolk, having no influence on the game, till the PC Circle goes off and kills some Eldar Lunar in a raid and takes his loot?<br /> <br /> What is your grand vision for Lunars Zel? Do they have none? Are they the one splat afforded no great destiny, story or protections?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Also, the Scarlet Empress was created by the Sidereals. She has no influence or interest in Heaven. She wants to bring Dragonblooded rule to the edges of Creation (not that she made any gains there). She brings stability to the Realm, just by being who she is, she has served the Sidereals. Why would they change anything. Even then, they council her and manipulate others in the Dynastic structure. The Sidereals very much control the Realm. Whenever she steps away for vacation, they could easily move in under a destiny and become her, killing the &quot;usurper&quot; when it/she returned.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208705#post208705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">[1]</span> Lunar Exalted cannot make Terrestrial Exalted irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two wrongs does not make a right, just frustrates me that everything else does just this<sup>[1]</sup> to Lunars. That even the players oppress them. I remember not so long ago when the Doomtrain carried the banner of Lunars high. I want to see that fire again, passions burning, mighty billows of smoke painting the horizon *sigh* truly we are in an Age of Sorrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-25-2014, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T15:51:39-07:00","id":208782,"title":"","content":"I was wondering when we'd get around to this again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T15:53:04-07:00","id":208783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208760#post208760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No difference in respect to the Moonsilver Doomtrain's meaning. Doing another's bidding without ever knowing, over hundreds of years, just dancing to those strings...still sidelines Dragonbloods and their victories.</div> </div> </div> </div>From one perspective, sure. From another, no, the individual glory and deeds of Dragon-Blooded forging an empire over the past 700 years is not diminished simply because someone else benefited from them doing so or because Scarlet got some institutional support from Heaven when she started. The conquests of the now-satrapies are DB victories. I wouldn't read Sidereal interference into any of those victories (unless that's part of the story you're telling - in which case go nuts!)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208760#post208760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zel, I have a question. Been on these forums for years, and I have to wonder, why can people support every faction but Lunars. I mean really, if Lunars are so worthless and destined to fail - to have no meaningful connections to anything in the game (go play in the Wyld) why even include them. If they are not meant to fight their enemies the Sidereals (but be victims forever), if they are not meant to make something or sway Dragonbloods (who have been swayed by Solars and Sidereals over thousands of years), if they are not meant to be the strong second who questions and even overturns his commanders words when he is wrong (rather than a bonded suplicant) - what do you want them to do? Do you really want them to sit in the Boardermarches playing with Fairfolk, having no influence on the game, till the PC Circle goes off and kills some Eldar Lunar in a raid and takes his loot?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the big problem with Lunars is they no more belong to a relevant unified faction than Solars do, but people want to insist that they do. This stems from their last-minute inclusion as a PC splat in 1e when they were intended to be barbarian antagonists, but that narrowness doesn't make for a lot of PC options. The 1e Silver Pact was trying to evoke the Garou Nation from OWoD Werewolf. So in 2e they tried to distance themselves from the &quot;boring barbarians playing boring barbarian stories&quot; vibe <i>explicitly supported in the 1e splatbook ST chapter</i>, and instead got &quot;Stewardship&quot; as a theme, paired with fluff saying &quot;yeah they all ran and hid in the Wyld for 2000 years and do nothing else.&quot; Which is an inherent dumb contradiction. So now you have &quot;shapeshifting Stewards,&quot; except the question becomes &quot;how can you steward the things you should care about if you can slip off into the night at any time as a mouse and abandon them?&quot;<br /> <br /> For some reason, Solars = Lords worked well in their themes and charms. Just like Sidereals = Viziers and Dragon-Blooded = Soldiers. Lunars = Stewards never really did, because on the most important level, the Lord is also the Steward of his domain and people. Hence Stewards were redundant with Lords, and didn't explore that different a thematic space, so we got Silver Solars instead. Silver Solars, with worse mechanics and stuck in a boring organizational faction structure (seriously, there's a &quot;fight the Wyld&quot; faction, which is something all Lunars would do so they have a faction inside the organization that does the same jobs as the organization?) <br /> <br /> I don't support Lunars as a united faction because the Silver Pact doesn't make that much sense, and the 2e factions inside of it make even less sense aside from the Crossroads Society (and the TSR comes across as a stupid hobby that will never really do anything big and cool that actually affects the setting).I would support the stories of individual Lunars in a heartbeat, just like the stories of individual Solars, Sidereals, etc. The difference being that Solars have no overarching faction, while (most) Sidereals, DBs, Abyssals, Alchemicals, and (in 2e) GSPs belong to a large faction (Bureau of Destiny, Hell, the Realm, Loosky) or a small faction that shares general overarching goals with other small factions (the Deathlords, the Divisions of the Bureau of Destiny). Lunars have a large faction with no overarching policy except &quot;survive,&quot; composed of smaller factions that are frequently both irrelevant or ineffectual. There's no fun in actually being a part of the Silver Pact. This is a separate issue from 2 editions portraying the Lunars as uselessly sitting around forever or masturbating to societies they set up and ultimately abandon that don't seem to make any big waves ever.<br /> <br /> I had thought about a Lunar-Sidereal War during mid-2e as a way to spice up the terrible Lunar fluff but hadn't thought much about implementation, but it seems someone on 3e also had these ideas and is running with them in a cool way. I like the idea of a 700-year cold war (or 2000 year cold war since the end of the First Age, whichever). Now the TSR societies could actually serve as catspaws to the Lunars in the same ways that the DBs have their satrapies and the Sidereals use some of the DBs. i'm hoping this is how it shapes out for 3e because as it stands the TSR has no purpose, where it might have a cool niche role to fill with the Caul and a more active Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> The problem with Lunars is that they're thematically muddled. &quot;Animal Exalted&quot; is very restrictive and evokes both thoughts of furries and a specific play style hearkening to Changing Breeds in OWoD. &quot;Steward Exalted&quot; turned into &quot;Silver Solar,&quot; i.e. &quot;similar effects as Solars, but more expensive and with higher prereqs as a cheap way to balance them against Solars.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208760#post208760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Scarlet Empress was created by the Sidereals. She has no influence or interest in Heaven. She wants to bring Dragonblooded rule to the edges of Creation (not that she made any gains there). She brings stability to the Realm, just by being who she is, she has served the Sidereals. Why would they change anything. Even then, they council her and manipulate others in the Dynastic structure. The Sidereals very much control the Realm. Whenever she steps away for vacation, they could easily move in under a destiny and become her, killing the &quot;usurper&quot; when it/she returned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like this idea nor do I agree with it. She doesn't serve the Sidereals. She's not Chejop's little proxy, even if he could kill her pretty easy. If Chejop had killed the Empress after the end of the Contagion, what then? He couldn't rally the DBs - they followed the Empress in part because she was now a huge heroic figure, and in part because she had the power of the Sword of Creation. Chejop in an RD couldn't rally them to him, nor would he inherit the Sword, so he struck a deal that was good for both of them. A Sidereal advisor controls the Realm only insofar as they influence an actual Dynast of high standing, because the Realm respects hierarchy and high standing. The Sidereals will be relatively powerless to stop a Realm Civil War, no matter which side they throw their weight behind, in part because the Sidereals are not unified and some of them would benefit from a Civil War even as others freak out about it, and in part because Sidereal powers make them better advisors than god-kings. Also insofar as she has &quot;not made any gains&quot; to control Creation - I'd say controlling the Blessed Isle and the shores of most of the Inner Sea is pretty good. Maybe not 700 years good, but not terrible.<br /> <br /> I find it interesting you're looking for someone to go to bat for Lunars while trying to minimize everything DBs have done and could do as &quot;just a byproduct of Sidereal puppetry.&quot; Am I misinterpreting that or missing something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:01:16-07:00","id":208790,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to say again that I think most people's complaints about Lunars can be addressed with a gentle reminder that we don't, actually, know what the vast majority of Creation is like. All the stuff that is detailed in all the books only encompasses, explicitly, a small fraction of Creation. The majority, entire continents of it, are left out of the books. So, you want a more powerful Silver Pact? Have one in your game. Think Lunars should have done more than you're aware of throughout Creation's history? Well, they probably have. Do we really need it all to be spelled out for us in such detail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:02:05-07:00","id":208791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one suggested anything like that. Even treating my Lunar as a patrician, without charms or Breeding and with the lowest possible odds, it would be ten times more effective than that, 10% instead of 1%, and a thousand instead of a hundred.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's funny, at the beginning of this I was hoping it was going to mean &quot;nobody suggested that&quot; to mean my extrapolation was ungrounded, meaning I had a significant falling sensation when it instead turned into a perverse kind of &quot;you didn't take your extrapolation far enough&quot;. Suffice to say, no, no I do not think the minimal breeding of one's Exalt and lack of discernment in a partner should lead to a thousand Dragon Blooded. I don't think it should lead to five Dragon Blooded. I don't think the inheritance of the Terrestrial Exaltation should be a statistical thing where you can overcome poor breeding by sheer brute forcing it. I find it neither consistent with the portrayal of the setting, nor generally good for attitudes towards the Dragon Blooded. I don't even care about how it gels with the gameplay statistics for Terrestrial inheritance; at best, I'd say that attempting to scale scenarios up like that, in a manner that that extremely simplistic math is clearly not designed to deal with (because seriously, rolling a single d10 has to have the weakest argument to be a simulation of the setting behind it of anything in the game) is at least as bad as trying to make dice pools in excess of twenty produce a consistent system or setting. No character gets to produce a decent number of Dragon Blooded children if they're not playing the same game as the Scarlet Dynasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:02:43-07:00","id":208793,"title":"","content":"One could easily play out that Scarlet was offed by the Sidereals for some reason in their own games - maybe she was starting to mess with stuff bigger than the Salt Gods. Be more fun to me than *spoiler*. But ya, I see a lot of your points. I suppose it's just been a long time that Lunars have sucked and going to be a while longer yet - and don't really understand why people cling to the lore of Lunars sucking rather than allowing them to change lore to be interesting (borrowing from 3E even or if you will). I mean sitting in Creation 2000 years - that's so much time to build some sort of power structure or network. Even 800 years, cause I'm very willing to accept the Shogunate as some scary bs.<br /> <br /> Thanks for sparing the time and words for me Zel, it is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:07:26-07:00","id":208798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">we don't, actually, know what the vast majority of Creation is like.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not true. Or, more accurately, it's not entirely relevant, because there are still logical constraints on what you can actually put into those blank spaces. The game is based on a degree of anthropological and economic awareness that clashes against assumptions of putting in significant things that don't impact anything surrounding them. Given values of &quot;a more powerful Silver Pact&quot; would be inconsistant with the setting asumptions of the hegemony of the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:12:28-07:00","id":208801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208790#post208790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you want a more powerful Silver Pact? Have one in your game. Think Lunars should have done more than you're aware of throughout Creation's history? Well, they probably have. Do we really need to have everything spelled out for us in exhaustive detail?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, 2e tried &quot;spell everything out&quot; with some subjects and it was bad.<br /> <br /> That said it would nice to have a couple examples of cool shit the Silver Pact successfully did (even if it's been wiped off the map), or a couple Lunars with actual big epic histories (even if they're dead now). Examples are not spelling everything out. Examples in the canon material are necessary to believe that such things might be possible though; the setting basically says &quot;welp Lunars have sucked for 2000 years&quot; it it becomes harder to believe the (homemade) stories of the ones who did cool shit without dismissing them as either aberrant or wishful thinking that they happened in a setting that goes out of its way to say &quot;that can't/didn't happen.&quot; It's especially painful to see the lack of these things over a 2000 year post-First Age period with Lunars, when those things are clearly present in both Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded and have been present from the very beginning. It comes across as sloppy implementation of Lunars at best or deliberate omission of them having Cool Historic Shit to Point At at worst that is right there in the book to inspire players and STs alike.<br /> <br /> Basically yes, I could probably invent cool stuff but some examples of existing cool stuff (that my plots could plug in to and my players could take an interest in) are not just nice, they're necessary. And we have none of them.<br /> <br /> It's a similar problem as with the Deathlords. Your table can have any reason why they haven't destroyed Creation with their canon write-ups. The white-room setting, however, does not provide a plausible reason why they haven't done more, because the mechanical system (in which the Deathlord stats were written) undermines the setting that the system is supposed to facilitate playing in. So you either have bullshit paper-thin excuses (problematic) or no valid reason to support your thesis (problematic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:13:09-07:00","id":208802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208791#post208791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's funny, at the beginning of this I was hoping it was going to mean &quot;nobody suggested that&quot; to mean my extrapolation was ungrounded, meaning I had a significant falling sensation when it instead turned into a perverse kind of &quot;you didn't take your extrapolation far enough&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually what I meant was you didn't seriously address the issue. You just distorted my example into a caricature of yiffing 10,000 mortals to produce 100 Exalts, when you know that's not what I was suggesting at all. That's always your method.. Trying to discuss anything with you is a game of clarifying and re-clarifying while you constantly seek to distort whatever is said for maximum ridicule and refuse to seriously answer any questions put to you.<br /> <br /> And that reminds me,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207674#post207674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you've played Exalted yet, have you?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=207800#post207800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want you to answer this question, Levi. If you expect other people to argue with you, it's only fair that you answer a question once in a while. Have you ever played Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't played Exalted, have you, Levi? 3000 posts on this forum, gods know how many on other forums, most of them arguing with people or making fun of their opinions, telling them how to play a game, but you've never actually played it, have you? Almost everyone else on this forum is here to talk about a game they enjoy playing. But are you even interested in playing? Or is it, to you, just something to argue about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-26-2014, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:26:03-07:00","id":208815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208793#post208793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for sparing the time and words for me Zel, it is appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quite welcome. And there are reasons for the endemic problems to Lunars that go back so far that it's not surprising many of them were carried forward.<br /> <br /> Some reading on the subject that I believe to be accurate, from Holden:<br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:the-lunar-factions\" target=\"_blank\">The Lunar Factions</a><br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:fixing-the-lunars\" target=\"_blank\">Fixing the Lunars</a><br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history\" target=\"_blank\">Troubled Lunar History</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:28:53-07:00","id":208818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208802#post208802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have never played Exalted, have you, Levi? 3000 posts on this forum, gods know how many on other forums, most of them arguing with people or making fun of their opinions, telling them how to play a game, but you've never actually played it, have you? Almost everyone else on this forum is here to talk about a game they enjoy playing. But are you even interested in playing? Or is it, to you, just something to argue about?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in the Exalted forum. Assuming that someone hasn't played the game is, quite honestly, one of the more terrible assumptions of bad faith one can make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:33:16-07:00","id":208822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208802#post208802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You have never played Exalted, have you, Levi? 3000 posts on this forum, gods know how many on other forums, most of them arguing with people or making fun of their opinions, telling them how to play a game, but you've never actually played it, have you? Almost everyone else on this forum is here to talk about a game they enjoy playing. But are you even interested in playing? Or is it, to you, just something to argue about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you care?<br /> <br /> Why should <i>anyone</i> care?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:38:19-07:00","id":208826,"title":"","content":"Although I know for a fact it's actually true about at least one person on here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:39:20-07:00","id":208828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208706#post208706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Command is a better word, sorry. However, Sidereals *do* control them. So if anyone makes Dragonbloods irrelevant, its the Sidereals, where in they are just cat's-paws and unwitting lackeys.</div> </div> </div> </div>In<i> Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded,</i> the relationship between Chejop Kejak and the Mouth of Peace is presented in an ambivalent manner: Kejak influences the successive Mouths, but sometimes they prove resistant or stubborn and take decisions he does not want them to. When this happens, he tries to outmanoeuvre them, but sometimes this proves impossible. When a Mouth of Peace is too out of his control... he shrugs and waits for the next one to come along, hoping they will be more malleable.<br /> <br /> This is an interesting portrayal. It shows that while Sidereals influence Dragon-Blooded society, they do not control it - individual people and discrete moments in history can fall out of their control. They work with that, because they don't really have a choice and because they can live thousand of years, so they can afford to take a long-term view and accept losses and setbacks along the way. <br /> <br /> Then came<i> Exalted: the Sidereals.</i> In this book's intro fiction, the Mouth of Peace is described as a pitiable, &quot;poor creature&quot; &quot;addled&quot; by the &quot;sorceries worked on her mind,&quot; basically a puppet for Chejop Kejak with no free will. That was a change in tone - and perhaps it set a new vision for the Sidereal/Dragon-Blooded relationship across the game line.<br /> <br /> I think the first depiction was more interesting. There are too few Sidereals - too few Gold Faction members - too few elders. They can't control Dynastic society, much less &quot;the Dragon-Blooded&quot; as a whole. For most of the time following the Usurpation, the Dragon-Blooded where in a state of constant warfare against both themselves and the enemies of Creation; there was nothing to control there. And when the Terrestrial Host was finally (partly) unified... it was under the control of a single Dragon-Blooded woman who could and would afford to tell off the Sidereals if they got delusions of controlling her.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals have been trying to influence and guide along Dragon-Blooded societies for centuries. They have met success and failure, but they've never been fully in control. Hell - some Dragon-Bloods are even aware of their existence, Arcane Fate notwithstanding. What they have most control over is their religion; the Immaculate Order is their tool, but even there they have issues (see the Mouth of Peace above). Dynastic society as a whole? Yeah, right.<br /> <br /> And that's not even getting into Outcastes. <br /> <br /> Mnemon's undercover Sidereal mentor almost <i>died</i> when she Exalted in a fit of anger against him, and she was a child. These are not people you can manipulate at your leisure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:47:52-07:00","id":208857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208818#post208818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're in the Exalted forum. Assuming that someone hasn't played the game is, quite honestly, one of the more terrible assumptions of bad faith one can make.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my knowledge he's never once posted anything about any character he's ever played, anything that's ever happened in a game, etc. And he does not answer the question when it's asked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208822#post208822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you care?<br /> <br /> Why should <i>anyone</i> care?</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, I shouldn't. But it's exasperating to constantly be told I'm playing a game wrong by someone who's never played it and has no interest in playing it. Especially when the same person isn't willing to honestly say whether he has or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:48:29-07:00","id":208858,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that an extremely simple way to reconcile this is by framing it in the same terms as why the Third Edition Silver Pact isn't generally trying to go in for Realm-style empire building or acquiring competing arsenals of First Age prodigies: that there general policy is to not try to compete with the Realm and Sidereals in their own arena (one where they already have a significant head start and several intrinsic advantages), instead using various forms of sabotage to remove the advantages of the enemy in a manner that also makes the world into an arena that favours them.<br /> <br /> I imagine that many Lunars don't quite see themselves as in a better position to harness the power of a group of Dragon Blooded than the empire that rules the world that is governed by a whole bunch of Dragon Blooded. I can just imagine the scenario in which a bunch of Terrestrials look to defend their Lunar forebear against a Wyld Hunt, and then get that shocking moment where the attackers turn out to look just like them, and ask probing questions, and it all leads to an unfortunate falling out. Also Dynasts pay better.<br /> <br /> Like, in the current cultural hegemony of Creation &quot;Lost Eggs&quot; serve as a rather sizable proportion of where the officers that secure Realm military superiority come from. I don't think it's much of a stretch to see most Lunars as wanting there to be a lot less Lost Eggs in the world. Their efforts towards that purpose could even be taken as part of why the Realm has a lot fewer legions than it used to. Again, it's not really a matter of &quot;we'll just have our own Outcastes that we keep away from them&quot;, because the Realm can generally make better use of Dragon Blooded, and have more to offer them. Dragon Blooded who seem under the influence of a Lunar Anathema might actually receive priority in recruitment for the Razor and Coin, or are otherwise targeted for rapid elimination (I'll remind again that people with the potential to be Dragon Blooded are fairly easily identified at the point where they have all the vulnerabilities of a three-week old child).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:53:39-07:00","id":208861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208828#post208828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In<i> Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded,</i> the relationship between Chejop Kejak and the Mouth of Peace is presented in an ambivalent manner: Kejak influences the successive Mouths, but sometimes they prove resistant or stubborn and take decisions he does not want them to. When this happens, he tries to outmanoeuvre them, but sometimes this proves impossible. When a Mouth of Peace is too out of his control... he shrugs and waits for the next one to come along, hoping they will be more malleable.<br /> <br /> This is an interesting portrayal. It shows that while Sidereals influence Dragon-Blooded society, they do not control it - individual people and discrete moments in history can fall out of their control. They work with that, because they don't really have a choice and because they can live thousand of years, so they can afford to take a long-term view and accept losses and setbacks along the way.<br /> <br /> Then came<i> Exalted: the Sidereals.</i> In this book's intro fiction, the Mouth of Peace is described as a pitiable, &quot;poor creature&quot; &quot;addled&quot; by the &quot;sorceries worked on her mind,&quot; basically a puppet for Chejop Kejak with no free will. That was a change in tone - and perhaps it set a new vision for the Sidereal/Dragon-Blooded relationship across the game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be an example of the splat-slant that was so prevalent in 1e because of its prevalence in OWoD (basically, fiction and stuff in a book for a particular splat was writhed as biased in support of that splat or to make it more interesting; later books tried to present information without that bias).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208828#post208828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mnemon's undercover Sidereal mentor almost <i>died</i> when she Exalted in a fit of anger against him, and she was a child. These are not people you can manipulate at your leisure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, where is that from? It's fairly obvious that that is problematic in its own right!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:58:23-07:00","id":208881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208861#post208861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, where is that from? It's fairly obvious that that is problematic in its own right!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from her writeup in Scroll of Exalts. In a sparring match, she nearly killed a Sidereal with sheer force of will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T17:01:27-07:00","id":208885,"title":"","content":"Well, the moment of Exaltation has always been portrayed as a kind of transcendent experience where you can achieve things you otherwise couldn't. When the Bull of the North Exalts, his anima <i>dissolves </i>ghosts. And when Mnemon Exalts...<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspect Book: Earth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Letter from Stone to Chejop Kejak RY 381<br /> <br /> Honored sir, the child Exalted two days ago. I would have written you earlier, but I have been tending my wounds. I was witness to the child\u2019s Exaltation \u2014 and almost victim to it. It was violent, which was not surprising, but the power she commanded as she touched her Essence was extraordinary. She used advanced Charms, managing to strike me several times before exhausting herself. The most alarming thing about the encounter after she had expended her Essence was that her force of will \u2014 not magic, sir, merely her will \u2014 had her manage to throw a knife at me as I left the room. This was not Essence. It was mere tenacity. I did not see it coming, to my shame. I saw her Exaltation and expected it, but the final attack was a surprise.<br /> <br /> After her attack, I found it necessary to remove myself from her view to get to safety. If she had enough consciousness left after expending her Essence to keep attacking, she is truly a dangerous girl. She knows without a doubt that I am a Sidereal now. I feel your insistence on my disguise was a wise one. I will be able to watch the child later with my true face, and she will be none the wiser.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T17:13:35-07:00","id":208890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208858#post208858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that an extremely simple way to reconcile this is by framing it in the same terms as why the Third Edition Silver Pact isn't generally trying to go in for Realm-style empire building or acquiring competing arsenals of First Age prodigies: that there general policy is to not try to compete with the Realm and Sidereals in their own arena (one where they already have a significant head start and several intrinsic advantages), instead using various forms of sabotage to remove the advantages of the enemy in a manner that also makes the world into an arena that favours them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in a RPG that will span a year or more of your time - building things, growth, and constructive action is going to be more fun and speak louder for your character than the 300 manses you've imploded. It also casts Lunars firmly as bad guys, always destroying stuff, no matter how valiant they make it sound in their fictions. I think doing that would be a very dangerous course for reconfirming Lunars as raid bosses and bad guys. Even the Deathlords and Deathknights build things, a lot of things, and they are about the antithesis of being. Some characters (like Changing Moons played like Nights) could get what they want out of such a thing, but making it splat wide would be terrible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208885#post208885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the moment of Exaltation has always been portrayed as a kind of transcendent experience where you can achieve things you otherwise couldn't. When the Bull of the North Exalts, his anima <i>dissolves </i>ghosts. And when Mnemon Exalts...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is sooooo bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-25-2014, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T17:47:36-07:00","id":208908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208858#post208858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that many Lunars don't quite see themselves as in a better position to harness the power of a group of Dragon Blooded than the empire that rules the world that is governed by a whole bunch of Dragon Blooded. I can just imagine the scenario in which a bunch of Terrestrials look to defend their Lunar forebear against a Wyld Hunt, and then get that shocking moment where the attackers turn out to look just like them, and ask probing questions, and it all leads to an unfortunate falling out. Also Dynasts pay better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're naturally going to betray your family and your people to the Realm and stab your Lunar ancestor in the back when you learn for the first time that other Dragon-Bloods - shockingly - look like you. Which your Lunar never told you, for some reason. And which you didn't know, because you've had no contact with any Dragon-Bloods before that moment. And because they can pay you better than Lunars can, because Lunars don't have money I guess.<br /> <br /> But when Solar Captain Dace shows up, you naturally forsake the Realm and go over to his side because don't you know? The sun-kings deserve your obedience. Not like<i> Lunars.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T17:55:34-07:00","id":208913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208890#post208890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is sooooo bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually find it very appropriate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:03:05-07:00","id":208921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208908#post208908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because you're naturally going to betray your family and your people to the Realm and stab your Lunar ancestor in the back when you learn for the first time that other Dragon-Bloods - shockingly - look like you. Which your Lunar never told you, for some reason. And which you didn't know, because you've had no contact with any Dragon-Bloods before that moment. And because they can pay you better than Lunars can, because Lunars don't have money I guess.<br /> <br /> But when Solar Captain Dace shows up, you naturally forsake the Realm and go over to his side because don't you know? The sun-kings deserve your obedience. Not like<i> Lunars.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Solars are new kids on the block, and anything bad they did is a distant legend. Lunars have been about, active, and intent on killing Dragon-Blooded since the days of the Shogunate. There's a rather huge mountain of bad blood there, likely down to the smallest and most innocuous folk tale spawned from their fifteen centuries-and-counting guerrilla campaign. Meanwhile, the wealth that the Lunars might have accumulated typically gets used in the same capacity, and that's if they've bothered to take anything of the sort when they burned down the enemy's base and trashed the most valuable items (First Age magical relics).<br /> <br /> Dace managed to win Risa over because he operates free of baggage like &quot;remember the time that Ma-Ha-Suchi killed all of those outcastes and decorated his lair with their skulls?&quot; No one wants to end up as a decorative skull around the Nameless Lair, and you can never be sure that a shapeshifter might not be Ma-Ha-Suchi, so there's that as a serious complication to any relationship, above and beyond Anathema propaganda. As the final straw, even the Solars might think of Lunars as monstrous. Such is the consequence of their activities while the Solars were out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:10:44-07:00","id":208927,"title":"","content":"Lies, it was his giant glow-sword and shiny bald head. Risa likes the Yul Brynner look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:19:59-07:00","id":208934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208927#post208927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when Solar Captain Dace shows up, you naturally forsake the Realm and go over to his side because don't you know? The sun-kings deserve your obedience. Not like<i> Lunars.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Totally agree with you. I don't get how people can be so blind.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the links Zelbinnean,they were most insightful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:20:49-07:00","id":208937,"title":"","content":"The fact that he handily killed her superior officer in front of her eyes probably had something to do with it, to tell the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:23:54-07:00","id":208941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208937#post208937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that he handily killed her superior officer in front of her eyes probably had something to do with it, to tell the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Welp a Lunar could do that - then take the form of the superior officer. Nothing stunning in that performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:27:49-07:00","id":208942,"title":"","content":"A Lunar would have eaten her superior officer in front of her. Then taken his form.<br /> <br /> What? What's the matter, Risa? Something wrong? You don't look well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:30:02-07:00","id":208943,"title":"","content":"Hey now, that's Havesh the Vanisher's shtick!<br /> <br /> Somehow it doesn't get him a lot of friends...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:34:14-07:00","id":208948,"title":"","content":"You know what? Forget the rest of it, this part:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208921#post208921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, the wealth that the Lunars might have accumulated typically gets used in the same capacity, and that's if they've bothered to take anything of the sort when they burned down the enemy's base and trashed the most valuable items (First Age magical relics).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they do this? Why would they <i>not</i> take the wealth and relics instead of smashing them? Are they too stupid to bring a <i>bag</i> with them when they raid places full of artifacts? Could they not perhaps use some of those beastmen they are supposedly so good at churning out to carry their luggage?<br /> <br /> Lunars are consistently presented as idiots, the Dumb Brute Exalted. They don't know how to build anything, they don't have any real talents besides &quot;break stuff&quot;, &quot;fuck stuff&quot;, or &quot;turn into things to either get to places to break stuff at or to fuck stuff&quot;, and they don't have any kind of plan for what they do next after breaking all of the stuff. The closest thing they've ever had to a constructive idea, the Thousand Streams River, is a joke of a plan that has no chance whatsoever of working. Why <i>should</i> we want to play them or associate with them as anything but raid bosses to be killed if they're this stupid and pointlessly destructive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:46:47-07:00","id":208954,"title":"","content":"The Lunars are good at building stuff. I mean, they don't particularly have a big overarching theme of &quot;great builders,&quot; but neither do Dragon-Bloods or Sidereals.<br /> <br /> They don't particularly <i>want</i> to build stuff most of the time, because it usually ends in them being ousted by Dragon-Blooded forces who then turn this infastructure to their advantage. So they favor installations that can be quickly destroyed or taken with them when they need to leave.<br /> <br /> They also have the issue that they don't have access to nearly as much 'prerequisite groundwork' - for instance, they tend to be unable to create the stable, entrenched societies that give rise to cultural elites from whom they could draw elite engineers, architects, or scientists that they could then put to work on building Manses or creating Artifacts, or to durably secure large deposits of jade.<br /> <br /> What's important to remember is that none of this is due to an inherent brutisheness inherent to the Lunars' natures - it is due to being constantly hounded and persecuted by the most powerful empire in the world. <br /> <br /> Lunars would certainly love to stop and build their Lunar version of the Heptagram. The Wyld Hunt won't let them. <br /> <br /> Though note, this portrayal is getting caveats and nuances in Third Edition. The Caul, people!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T18:51:56-07:00","id":208957,"title":"","content":"Well they've created what is arguably the greatest culture in Creation, Halta.<br /> <br /> It always seems strange to me that the people who complain Lunars haven't done anything impressive are often the same people who complain Halta is too amazing and powerful and must be taken down a peg.<br /> <br /> And getting back to the point I made before about how little we know about Creation, I see no reason to think there aren't half a dozen other Haltas scattered around the edge of Creation, have been for centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:21:52-07:00","id":208985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208948#post208948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why <i>should</i> we want to play them or associate with them as anything but raid bosses to be killed if they're this stupid and pointlessly destructive?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff certainly does not give you any reasons. As I've said: yes, you can make up your own reasons, but it's nice to feel like they were included in planning the setting and have things to show in the history to support that idea, rather than tacked on at the 11th hour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208934#post208934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the links Zelbinnean,they were most insightful.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quite welcome!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208957#post208957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they've created what is arguably the greatest culture in Creation, Halta.</div> </div> </div> </div>lol jeez omg lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-25-2014, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:28:31-07:00","id":208988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208985#post208985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lol jeez omg lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Because an enormous, prosperous, powerful, tolerant and relatively advanced multi-species civilization is not an achievement?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208985#post208985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fluff certainly does not give you any reasons. As I've said: yes, you can make up your own reasons, but it's nice to feel like they were included in planning the setting and have things to show in the history to support that idea, rather than tacked on at the 11th hour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree there should be more, and supposedly we'll see more of that in the next edition. The 'barbarian' thing makes me somewhat apprehensive about the whole thing, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:31:29-07:00","id":208989,"title":"","content":"There is that part where Haltan society is partly based on the cultural acceptation that anyone who touches the ground is fair game to be devoured by soul-sucking vampire fairies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:34:40-07:00","id":208991,"title":"","content":"But seriously, how easy is it to touch the ground in Halta? Even if you fall, you have to hit like 30 billion branches before you get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:35:36-07:00","id":208992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208988#post208988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because an enormous, prosperous, powerful, tolerant and relatively advanced multi-species civilization is not an achievement?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because Halta's write-up is.....pretty bad (that what I heard anyway).<br /> <br /> Eh, there seem to be not a lot of rage posts about Halta like I hope it to be, this is some from SufficentVelocity forum.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;We can work with the Fae and come out winning, we have animal companions with human intelligence that count as citizens , we are among the longest running Lunar project without influence by the realm , and we throw prisoners to the Rakasha while still smelling like roses. Oh and we control nearly a quarter of a Direction without manpower that would be necessary for this even by the wonky standards of Exalteds interaction with maps while living in treehouses.&quot; </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, it's better than that. They control an area the size of the Realm <i>without access to the ground</i>. Anyone who knows anything whatsoever about the dependence of a large society on agriculture will instantly, <i>instantly</i> call bullshit on that one.<br /> <br /> And then yes, they're a super special snowflake barbarian culture who live in trees but have advanced bureaucracy and high rates of literacy and good health and they're liberal and accepting of beastmen and they have gods and First Age Lunars on their side and the Linowa are fighting them with Realm aid so they're (one of) the LONE UNDERDOG(s) STANDING UP AGAINST THE REALM, and...<br /> <br /> ... it's nauseatingly Mary Sueish, frankly. Not to mention completely fucking stupid. At <i>best</i>, you should have disparate groups of &quot;Haltan tribes&quot; in the same way that you have &quot;Amazonian tribes&quot; - no unification, just a common environment, with thaumaturgic wards on their villages (often but not always arboreal, because that makes them easier to defend even when the wards don't work) that make them fairly safe from the raksha bands native to the area. They're not at <i>war</i> with Linowa as a whole, because there is no whole, but the tribes near the Linowan border attack them and are attacked in turn, and while they're less advanced they have guerilla supremacy in the forest - rather like the US in Vietnam. There should certainly be none of the &quot;enlightened and accepting&quot;, &quot;talking animals&quot;, &quot;high literacy&quot;, &quot;advanced bureaucracy&quot; crap going on (though beastmen are, frankly, their own problem), because that's just Mary Sue on top of Mary Sue.<br /> <br /> And hey, with the monopolity that is Halta broken, there's space to look at real-life historical &quot;high latitude forested cultures&quot; - parts of Russia, Sweden-Norway-Finland, maybe bits of Canada, the northern-most bits of Japan, etc - and put a few kingdoms and realistic societies down in that region. Ones that, you know, <i>don't suck</i>. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Aleph! The Haltans have friends in the forest who gather especially nutritious nuts and moss for them; they don't have to do agricul--ha ha ha ha ha, I can't even finish that sentence with a straight face. Fuck Halta. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-25-2014, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:37:46-07:00","id":208993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208988#post208988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I agree there should be more, and supposedly we'll see more of that in the next edition. The 'barbarian' thing makes me somewhat apprehensive about the whole thing, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had seen comments about how you can be a huge pampered social dilettante duelist from Port Calin and still completely fit the Lunar aesthetic. I'm excited for that. 2e did allow that, but 2e Charms were bland as hell and i am hoping for not bland Lunar Charms. I am more excited because while Conan axe-and-sandal is cool, it can be very hard to fit in to a story that doesn't revolve around the edge of civilization and its themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208988#post208988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because an enormous, prosperous, powerful, tolerant and relatively advanced multi-species civilization is not an achievement?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just feel like Halta has always been waaaaaaaay too pointedly twee to fit into Creation. I won't even reference the map - the size of both Halta and Linowan is just unrealistically embarrassing for whoever designed it and it's a known thing that it will be reigned in to something reasonably-sized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:43:15-07:00","id":208996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208992#post208992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's because Halta's write-up is.....pretty bad (that what I heard anyway).<br /> <br /> Eh, there seem to be not a lot of rage posts about Halta like I hope it to be, this is some from SufficentVelocity forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there, you see? &quot;The Lunar empire of Halta is too big, too prosperous, too enlightened and tolerant and in every way too successful.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then, later: &quot;Lunars never do anything! Where are all the successful Lunar empires? Rage!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:45:29-07:00","id":208997,"title":"","content":"I think the Haslanti League is an alltogether better and more interesting take at the Lunar's own brand of culture-building.<br /> <br /> But then, the Haslanti are just the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:48:17-07:00","id":208999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208996#post208996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there, you see? &quot;The Lunar empire of Halta is too big, too prosperous, too enlightened and tolerant and in every way too successful.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then, later: &quot;Lunars never do anything! Where are all the successful Lunar empires? Rage!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>See also: &quot;a nation founded by 2 Lunars over a relatively short period of time is extremely big, prosperous, enlightened and tolerant (inexplicably, being basically forest barbarians)...wait why do we have maybe 8 things like this across Creation when we have 300 Lunars?&quot;<br /> <br /> This is part of the overarching problem with Lunars. DBs mostly have 1 big place and 1 medium-sized but powerful place to point to. Sids are bureaucrats; this is known. For the number of Lunars, there isn't enough...and for what there is, a lot of it isn't good or is effectively 2000 years of revenge porn or moping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-25-2014, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:48:19-07:00","id":209000,"title":"","content":"Halta was promising back in Scavenger Sons. Then a lot of material got tacked on. Being retconned into a Lunar affair did it no favors. If Lunars stay involved with Halta in EX3, I'm guessing it would only be in the capacity of trying to get the Realm to send in and thus waste valuable, irreplacable relics of the First Age. To make the Scarlet Empire's support of the Linowan costly beyond comprehension. This would have the side benefit of the Linowan getting cool, impressive toys so that they're actually a credible threat to Halta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:53:15-07:00","id":209003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208999#post208999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See also: &quot;a nation founded by 2 Lunars over a relatively short period of time is extremely big, prosperous, enlightened and tolerant (inexplicably, being basically forest barbarians)...wait why do we have maybe 8 things like this across Creation when we have 300 Lunars?&quot;<br /> <br /> This is part of the overarching problem with Lunars. DBs mostly have 1 big place and 1 medium-sized but powerful place to point to. Sids are bureaucrats; this is known. For the number of Lunars, there isn't enough...and for what there is, a lot of it isn't good or is effectively 2000 years of revenge porn or moping.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is just funny to me, though - the one really cool, unequivocally successful Lunar-led civilization, one which could theoretically compete with the Realm for most enlightened culture in Creation, and of course everyone on the forums wants it destroyed.<br /> <br /> I do like the League, too. But I also like Halta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T21:05:18-07:00","id":209005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209003#post209003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is just funny to me, though - the one really cool, unequivocally successful Lunar-led civilization, one which could theoretically compete with the Realm for most enlightened culture in Creation, and of course everyone on the forums wants it destroyed.<br /> <br /> I do like the League, too. But I also like Halta.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't billed as a Lunar project from the start. That was added in a kind of panic late into 1e, much like with the Haslanti. The trend continued into 2e with the retconning of the Delzahn into a product of Tamuz's gynophobia, which was created for that edition as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T21:12:50-07:00","id":209010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209003#post209003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is just funny to me, though - the one really cool, unequivocally successful Lunar-led civilization, one which could theoretically compete with the Realm for most enlightened culture in Creation, and of course everyone on the forums wants it destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>For reasons other than it being founded by a pair of lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> You see, its too nice. Creation can't have nice places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T21:21:55-07:00","id":209015,"title":"","content":"I played a Haltan character traveling in the Scavvy Lands once. He found the cities unfortunately kind of grubby, bleak, uncivilized places. And also strangely two-dimensional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T21:46:12-07:00","id":209025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208881#post208881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's from her writeup in Scroll of Exalts. In a sparring match, she nearly killed a Sidereal with sheer force of will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's also in Caste Book: Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T21:55:40-07:00","id":209028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208954#post208954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars are good at building stuff. I mean, they don't particularly have a big overarching theme of &quot;great builders,&quot; but neither do Dragon-Bloods or Sidereals.<br /> <br /> They don't particularly <i>want</i> to build stuff most of the time, because it usually ends in them being ousted by Dragon-Blooded forces who then turn this infastructure to their advantage. So they favor installations that can be quickly destroyed or taken with them when they need to leave.<br /> <br /> They also have the issue that they don't have access to nearly as much 'prerequisite groundwork' - for instance, they tend to be unable to create the stable, entrenched societies that give rise to cultural elites from whom they could draw elite engineers, architects, or scientists that they could then put to work on building Manses or creating Artifacts, or to durably secure large deposits of jade.<br /> <br /> What's important to remember is that none of this is due to an inherent brutisheness inherent to the Lunars' natures - it is due to being constantly hounded and persecuted by the most powerful empire in the world.<br /> <br /> Lunars would certainly love to stop and build their Lunar version of the Heptagram. The Wyld Hunt won't let them.<br /> <br /> Though note, this portrayal is getting caveats and nuances in Third Edition. The Caul, people!</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, both the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal are regularly portrayed as being the builders of organizations, and the caretakers of organizations. Lunars in 1E were all about tearing stuff down. In 2E, they were a little more nuanced, in which they tear stuff down, and then teach people to be free and live independently. A few try to build up societies, but some are incompetent like that Tiger in the West, and others are extremely competent, and manipulate from the Shadows, like Sidereals. Others make beastmen tribes and lead them. <br /> <br /> I really wish it was different, but the general Lunar theme is tearing stuff down, and breaking stuff down, and hiding mystic secrets away so people can't get them. There are a couple of exceptions... but they aren't exactly filling. Lunars need some work. Lunars need to have been doing something other than building barbarian tribes since the 1st Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T05:00:39-07:00","id":209268,"title":"","content":"I imagine people would prefer Lunar dominions that possess a shred of credibility in the setting, and possibly also a bit of a... broader appeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T07:09:36-07:00","id":209293,"title":"","content":"Please tell me more about things that lack a shred of credibility, Levi. What was the experience of playing or running Halta like for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T07:11:28-07:00","id":209294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208908#post208908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when Solar Captain Dace shows up, you naturally forsake the Realm and go over to his side because don't you know? The sun-kings deserve your obedience. Not like<i> Lunars.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> We really need a better example of a Dragon-Blooded choosing to work for a Solar.<br /> Risa comes across as so incredibly brainwashed in Caste Book Dawn and then Scroll of Exalts gave her a meat puppet Motivation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T07:20:08-07:00","id":209297,"title":"","content":"The first novel presents her pretty well, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T07:28:35-07:00","id":209301,"title":"","content":"The 3e direction for Lunars will be what it will be, reading the last few pages, with the Lunars, I feel like my preference for how the operate, and why they don't accumulate as much stuff (manses, weapons, libraries), generally, *could* potentially be about mobility and flexibility, rather than sabotage or terrorism or an eventual advantage in a stone age world or persecution, as such. <br /> <br /> Mobility is a major advantage, whole peoples being able to migrate to where the enemy is weakest, to migrate and disperse in the face of threats. Mobility makes sense as well, when I think about how the Lunars could operate in the Threshold, moving around as patterns of Fair Folk assault on the world change, as new resources to gather and trade back into the world emerge from the Wyld, Creation's ecology and human culture.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that, when comparing the Dragonblooded and Lunars, I feel like it might be worth saying that the majority of people in the Dragonblooded and Lunar cultures are not productive. They mostly produce what they themselves use, or they extract from others what they want. It is only a fraction within the Dragonblooded society that really build, and that fraction only because they are not as mobile as the Lunars are. <br /> <br /> Like if you think about the settled world vs the Eurasian steppe, in history, only a vanishly small fraction of the settled world indulged in philosophy, learning, moving the world's understanding of the sciences forward. Those small fraction of people could not easily exist in the Eurasian steppe, yet not only that, the Eurasian steppe still proved to be a conduit for knowledge and trade that moved the world forwards.<br /> <br /> (In our world, of course, the &quot;barbarians&quot; were in the centre and &quot;civilization&quot; at the periphery, whatever the Chinese or Romans thought about it, while Exalted inverts this!).<br /> <br /> I do feel like you need an element where the &quot;Lunar strategy&quot; (whatever we might thing about how tight / loose the Lunars are as a people) is working in a way that doesn't purely &quot;diminish&quot; (in some sense) the grandeur and sophistication of the world, and where that isn't the aim of their strategy. Just a preference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T07:51:44-07:00","id":209307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209015#post209015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played a Haltan character traveling in the Scavvy Lands once. He found the cities unfortunately kind of grubby, bleak, uncivilized places. And also strangely two-dimensional.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's awesome! That's certainly a great way of looking at things.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: Halta always came across like an unbelievable twee hippie paradise, a place where people have Weird Hair Just Because and are as dextrous with their feet as with their hands Just Because, kind of like someone took a bucket of Changeling: the Dreaming and dumped it all over a region and turned it into kind of a Disney Princess fantasy setting where animals are on the same level as people and work jobs and make friends with people and can vote. You have a gigantic-beyond-all-scale nation out in the boonies that's a constitutional monarchy (already something very weird in an age of despots, juntas, and absolute monarchs). The size <i>is </i>a problem because it brings up all kinds of logistical issues; you might say &quot;well, only part of that is Halta proper, the rest are protectorates and regions occupied by allied tribes&quot; and that's a cool explanation but that is trying to explain away the pre-existing problem that someone did a bad job on a map. You're saying it makes sense for the greatest military power in Creation, organized in a fashion that is meant to evoke the Han Chinese or Japan, is the same size as something that seems to draw imagery from the Iroquois League With Animals and it doesn't really make that much sense when you look at it closely.<br /> <br /> This was all its own thing well before someone came along and said &quot;you know what, Lunars really haven't done enough, so...Lunars founded Halta.&quot; So anything you found cool about Halta (and there <i>was </i>cool stuff there, don't get me wrong) was probably an established Thing about it before Silver Python and Rain were tacked on. And they were tacked on kind of pointlessly!<br /> <br /> Back in 1e, the Lunar book map (which was kind of a depiction of territories and song lines) had &quot;Tamuz Walks Here&quot; in the area near Chiaroscuro and it's not a huge leap thinking the legendary Ka-Khan of the Delzahn was some kind of Exalt; that retcon wasn't a huge stretch. The Haslanti League was not implied to be a Lunar thing, but Gerd's backstory and taking on the Haslanti as a &quot;project&quot; always seemed better integrated than Halta did. The Lunar parts of Haltsa just seemed like a response to the fandom's &quot;the Lunars never do anything&quot; complaint.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T08:19:26-07:00","id":209323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209307#post209307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's awesome! That's certainly a great way of looking at things.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: Halta always came across like an unbelievable twee hippie paradise, a place where people have Weird Hair Just Because and are as dextrous with their feet as with their hands Just Because, kind of like someone took a bucket of Changeling: the Dreaming and dumped it all over a region and turned it into kind of a Disney Princess fantasy setting where animals are on the same level as people and work jobs and make friends with people and can vote. You have a gigantic-beyond-all-scale nation out in the boonies that's a constitutional monarchy (already something very weird in an age of despots, juntas, and absolute monarchs). The size <i>is </i>a problem because it brings up all kinds of logistical issues; you might say &quot;well, only part of that is Halta proper, the rest are protectorates and regions occupied by allied tribes&quot; and that's a cool explanation but that is trying to explain away the pre-existing problem that someone did a bad job on a map. You're saying it makes sense for the greatest military power in Creation, organized in a fashion that is meant to evoke the Han Chinese or Japan, is the same size as something that seems to draw imagery from the Iroquois League With Animals and it doesn't really make that much sense when you look at it closely.<br /> <br /> This was all its own thing well before someone came along and said &quot;you know what, Lunars really haven't done enough, so...Lunars founded Halta.&quot; So anything you found cool about Halta (and there <i>was </i>cool stuff there, don't get me wrong) was probably an established Thing about it before Silver Python and Rain were tacked on. And they were tacked on kind of pointlessly!<br /> <br /> Back in 1e, the Lunar book map (which was kind of a depiction of territories and song lines) had &quot;Tamuz Walks Here&quot; in the area near Chiaroscuro and it's not a huge leap thinking the legendary Ka-Khan of the Delzahn was some kind of Exalt; that retcon wasn't a huge stretch. The Haslanti League was not implied to be a Lunar thing, but Gerd's backstory and taking on the Haslanti as a &quot;project&quot; always seemed better integrated than Halta did. The Lunar parts of Haltsa just seemed like a response to the fandom's &quot;the Lunars never do anything&quot; complaint.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get people's complaints that it is too big, too prosperous, too successful, not on the verge of implosion like everything else in this setting, and maybe that's reason enough to give it a few problems, but on the whole I really like Halta because it is one of the few mortal places in Creation that actually feels like it belongs in a universe like Exalted. Most of the rest of Creation is just pastiches of different cultures from history. In Halta you suddenly have something completely different. Tree-cities, inter-species enlightenment, an entire field of applied biothaumaturgical science that they use for everything from public lighting to agriculture and waste disposal, etc. etc. It seems like one of the only places where writers were allowed to really explore the possibilities of the setting, and I appreciate that.<br /> <br /> About Lunars, even if you'd never heard of Lunars being involved in Halta, wouldn't you assume they were? I mean look at Halta. Intelligent animals and beastmen, integration between urban centers and ecosytem, 'test of survival'. What about Halta doesn't scream, &quot;Lunars have been here?&quot; If you were asked which of the three Celestial Exalts were behind Halta, which would it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-26-2014, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T09:03:51-07:00","id":209361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209323#post209323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get people's complaints that it is too big, too prosperous, too successful, not on the verge of implosion like everything else in this setting, and maybe that's reason enough to give it a few problems, but on the whole I really like Halta because it is one of the few mortal places in Creation that actually feels like it belongs in a universe like Exalted. Most of the rest of Creation is just pastiches of different cultures from history. In Halta you suddenly have something completely different. Tree-cities, inter-species enlightenment, an entire field of applied biothaumaturgical science that they use for everything from public lighting to agriculture and waste disposal, etc. etc. It seems like one of the only places where writers were allowed to really explore the possibilities of the setting, and I appreciate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, it's seriously only too big because someone did not grok the map scale <i>at all</i>. The fluff doesn't even support its size.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's one of the problems with it. It's a weird, progressive culture in a world that is varying degrees of the Bronze Age. As you put it, it's supposed to be as cosmopolitan as the Realm. It feels a lot like the Tau in the 40k setting: in a universe where the factions include &quot;humans who don't really understand their technology and have ritualized it religiously,&quot; &quot;aliens whose civilization went through apocalypse,&quot; &quot;amoral space bugs drawn to the thing that makes human space travel possible,&quot; &quot;traitors to humanity who consider themselves free but are just as backwards,&quot; and &quot;ancient robots who awaken to find their empire gone and lesser races squabbling over the spoils,&quot; the Tau are a Great White Hope, an up-and-coming race that is progressing technologically rather than regressing, that comes across as Good Socialists who will conquer a human world and let them keep worshiping the Emperor, in a universe of morally-grey autocrats (if the Imperium conquered a Tau world it would torture and then publicly execute anyone professing loyalty to the Greater Good). It feels kind of out of place in the setting milieu, and that's why (I think) the authors started breaking that perfect facade and giving them problems, breakaway factions, and secret morally grey things they do (like secret forced sterilization of Imperial populations) - to make them fit better in the universe they exist in.<br /> <br /> There's something like that in Halta. It's a constitutional republic in a world where the closest thing to that is a confederation of otherwise-autocratic or military-controlled nations (or Nexus, which is basically quasi-anarchic in a way that works). It's cosmopolitan and enlightened, but it's not located on trade routes so the question becomes &quot;why, other than for its own sake?&quot; It has trained sciences without really any explanation for the breakthroughs other than A Lunar Did It: by this I mean, harvesting naturally-existing bioluminescent mushrooms or whatever for light makes sense, as does creating colonies of them for your needs, but it seems like Halta straight-up engineered them from non-glowly fungus or whatever. <br /> <br /> The tree-city conceit is indeed admittedly cool, as is the alliance with the Fair Folk (and the local Fair Folk having their own little internecine issues). The &quot;evergreen versus deciduous&quot; is a great concept for an eternal religious war. But to me an enjoyable Halta should evoke more...I dunno really. You have opportunities for Iroquois vs. Algonquin narratives with the Linowan except it does not really play out that way. The Linowan are made to look particularly brutish and savage compared to the Haltans (in other words, the depiction of the Haltans seems to be written to give them the moral high ground in that war because they're more advanced socially and therefore more worthy of existence).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209323#post209323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Lunars, even if you'd never heard of Lunars being involved in Halta, wouldn't you assume they were? I mean look at Halta. Intelligent animals and beastmen, integration between urban centers and ecosytem, 'test of survival'. What about Halta doesn't scream, &quot;Lunars have been here?&quot; If you were asked which of the three Celestial Exalts were behind Halta, which would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's what bothers me about it. The Delzahn are clearly inspired by Arabian stories, with a cool twist to the modern culture public modesty that is kind of the inversion of Islamic interpretations. The Haslanti make me think about the Vendel/Vesten from 7th Sea - a Norse culture, considered barbarians but with a rather technological twist (hot-air balloon airships reminding me a lot of the dirigibles in His Dark Materials). Halta doesn't have a good real-world parallel for its themes, so it seems alien, but in a kitschy Disney Princess way. <br /> <br /> From the start, Halta had notions that &quot;this couldn't happen on its own, a Lunar Had To Do It&quot; but it never out-and-out said that. And then it made it explicit. Adding Lunars to Chiaroscuro and Haslanti adds a little bit to them but you could see those societies existing as purely mortal, without Exalted interference. Halta doesn't. It doesn't really pan to any real-world society for influence (which is OK I guess). If any Eastern nation feels kind of Lunar-ish in the same way that the Haslanti and Delzahn do, to me it's the Linowan (because it's feasible but doesn't whack you over the head with the implication).<br /> <br /> The Realm is considered cosmopolitan and enlightened because it's like Rome or China or Japan. It's still a brutal military state, but it controls and influences so much that it sees itself as better, and the world kind of has to agree to an extent. It has an internal organization that the places it conquered (which it would consider more primitive) could not match in long-term opposition. The Realm is cosmopolitan because it has the money and the armies and domination. Halta has none of that, but it's still enlightened and cosmopolitan, Just Because? It doesn't really make sense to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T09:48:38-07:00","id":209376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209323#post209323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About Lunars, even if you'd never heard of Lunars being involved in Halta, wouldn't you assume they were? I mean look at Halta. Intelligent animals and beastmen, integration between urban centers and ecosytem, 'test of survival'. What about Halta doesn't scream, &quot;Lunars have been here?&quot; If you were asked which of the three Celestial Exalts were behind Halta, which would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>The test of survival and the beastmen weren't added on until Kingdom of Halta, which was the place that tacked the Lunar influence on in the first place. Also, the test of survival is really kind of dumb. If everything else strained logistics, imagine if there was only one DMV in the US and Canada. Any citizen of either country has to go to that one office to get their license. That is essentially the situation that the Proving Ground sets up, only without someone who might have a car to drive you there faster than you can walk, or buses. It's all on foot, and it's hundreds of miles away from where everyone lives.<br /> <br /> We have plenty of Silver Solar problems, but the countries are Silver Sidereal problems. Yet another instance of Lunars not getting their own thing, with a side of being shat upon courtesy of the complete bastardization of Ten Stripes. Ten Stripes, whose only issue seemed to be that she (or he, Time of Tumult included both pronouns and originally referred to as a male Lunar, likely with a jaguar totem) spent some points on self-awareness that took away from the asskicking quotient that Blossom went into wholeheartedly, to the detriment of everything else. And in 2e, she gets turned into an incompotent Jabberjaw of a politician who can't even anticipate trouble from trying to take in castration-happy demon worshippers who wash up on her island.<br /> <br /> Fuck this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T09:55:17-07:00","id":209377,"title":"","content":"Halta is an elective monarchy, actually, which isn't as out-of-place as it may seem. For one, only a very select group of people may vote, and the potential candidates are likewise, shall we say, not common folk.<br /> <br /> It's less like the democracy you're used to, and more like the papal election.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T12:54:45-07:00","id":209478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209323#post209323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About Lunars, even if you'd never heard of Lunars being involved in Halta, wouldn't you assume they were? I mean look at Halta. Intelligent animals and beastmen, integration between urban centers and ecosytem, 'test of survival'. What about Halta doesn't scream, &quot;Lunars have been here?&quot; If you were asked which of the three Celestial Exalts were behind Halta, which would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ixacoatli cannot come fast enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T12:59:40-07:00","id":209481,"title":"","content":"Just going to leave this here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\"> http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T13:26:42-07:00","id":209495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208948#post208948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would they do this? Why would they <i>not</i> take the wealth and relics instead of smashing them? Are they too stupid to bring a <i>bag</i> with them when they raid places full of artifacts? Could they not perhaps use some of those beastmen they are supposedly so good at churning out to carry their luggage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps they do, on occasion. When the Lunar in question judges it to be something they can reliably keep out of the hands of the enemy, who are still alternately in a better position to make use of it or else so dependent on it for their advantage that there's a serious consideration for removing it from the field altogether, just to remove the threat of it permanently.<br /> <br /> I'd say it would help to look on the scenario as sometimes being akin to destroying the One Ring, except where the conditions are based on military logistics rather than straightforward moralizing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are consistently presented as idiots, the Dumb Brute Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a problem of presentation, not of premise. It's not difficult to make the basis of the Lunar position as projected in Third Edition into something that actually has an intelligent consideration behind it. Or a recognizable cultural bias; at least part of the premise seems to be that Lunars have transformed from what they were in the First Age in response to what's happened to them, and what's happened to them is the violent destruction of everything they owned and loved and being hounded into the wilderness. It's understandable that they're not quite magnanimous about the whole thing; that there's an actual basis for malice and revenge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why <i>should</i> we want to play them or associate with them as anything but raid bosses to be killed if they're this stupid and pointlessly destructive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding the loaded question, I imagine the appeal of Lunars is supposed to be in an embrace of savage fantasy, with a touch of the anthropological basis of violent movements by marginalized people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T13:38:56-07:00","id":209504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209481#post209481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just going to leave this here.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/d...=posts&amp;t=82643</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool stuff, and at least the timetable is right (happening over centuries) as well as some of the consequences. I am just sick to death of &quot;Lunar rape pens&quot; as the best Lunar strategy, or even a common one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T14:32:27-07:00","id":209528,"title":"","content":"Oh, it's worth mentioning that elder Lunar Charms like Frozen Ripple Lair allow for time-dilated pocket dimensions, potentially reducing the time required down to decades rather than centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T16:03:32-07:00","id":209553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209495#post209495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disregarding the loaded question, I imagine the appeal of Lunars is supposed to be in an embrace of savage fantasy, with a touch of the anthropological basis of violent movements by marginalized people.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Exalted are opposed to the Realm and oppressed by it (other than DB's obviously). Infernals have lost everything, Abyssals have lost everything, and sure so have Lunars. Lunars can come from any walks of life. A Lunar could Exalt in Lookshy, Hislanti, Whitewall or any number of other nice places. Lunars are not an oppressed race, they are humans first, and humans can be oppressed or oppressors. Exalted are 'more-than-human' not some kinda fantastical mermaid that detaches itself from its cultural bias and joins a collective identity as 'marginalized peoples'. Lunars can be anyone or anything. They are the splat to just turn their back on that kind of story and take the form of a Guild Prince traveling the land making money and living the good life. Never in one place long enough to be sniffed out, always on the next caravan. *If* they were that oppressed.<br /> <br /> It is not fun stealing heat from the rest of the world and never generating any of your own. Lunars should have plenty of sorcerous works (tons in-fact) and epic stories to tell or show. This only allows other splats material to work with and their own targets to destroy. How else would you tell the story of a Dragonblooded game taking the fight to the Lunars? It would be boring if the PC's could only kill beastmen and never undermine anything significant in the Lunars 'plans' as they were.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T16:06:41-07:00","id":209557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs#post207567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as Lunars have the best tools Creation-side to; locate, collect, and breed the Lost Eggs into a might host to bring down the Realm - one wonders why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, no.<br /> <br /> That would be the Realm. The Realm has the best tools to locate, collect and breed Lost Eggs into a mighty host. They've been doing so for almost a thousand years, and have become rather good at it. Their practical reach spans most of habitable Creation, and their cultural impact rather further - you'd be hard-pressed to find anyone who hadn't heard of the Realm in some form, and while some Outcastes may elect to stay in their near-bordermarch home and alternate between herding and fucking sheep like their fathers before them, rather more will be pushed to seek their fortune, the truth of their parentage, the secrets of their power, or their birthright in the storied Scarlet Island where sits the Throne of the World.<br /> <br /> And once they're there, they discover that it's actually pretty nice to be treated as a living deity with all the comforts of a sophisticated and world-dominating civilization, while also undergoing grueling training that affirms their commitment to and identification with the Scarlet Empire. This is a good model.<br /> <br /> Even without considering its efforts to acquire fresh blood, the Realm has a vast infrastructure dedicated to keeping its families strong, whole circles of Exalted working to determine the best matches to maintain and improve blood purity, manses developed over generations and designed for the sole purpose of enhancing fertility and in-vitro development of elemental chakras, great and storied genealogies eager to be woven together into a potent inheritance.<br /> <br /> A Lunar has, at most, a handful of weak blooded Exalted, who they will need to treat like dumb breeding stock in order to produce any genuinely useful results. Oddly, demigod warriors are not hugely inclined to being treated like dumb breeding stock. And even if the Lunar somehow succeeds in this absurd endeavour, and places himself - and perhaps his Circle! - at the head of a growing Empire populated by Dragon-blooded, his position is not secure. Recall that a full 300 Solars and 300 Lunars could not prevent the Terrestrial Host from rising up and slaughtering them, not with threats or promises or wages or love.<br /> <br /> Precisely what hope do you think a lone Silver Emperor is going to have when his entire nobility - historically the class from whom coups and assassinations spring like slinkies - is comprised of people who can not only shrug off his LOVE ME aura, who can not only take him in combat, but who are demonstrably better-suited to running a country than he is? How long do you think &quot;oh, I'll keep them ignorant of the doctrine of a world-spanning cult sponsored by the greatest civilization in existence, which totally validates their right to rule and casts me as a body-stealing demon (which I kind of look like, let's fucking face it)&quot; is going to last, especially when the Silver Emperor's stated goal is to wage war on aforesaid civilization?<br /> <br /> It's an absurd idea. The Exalted were not created to be slaves, to be led about and bred for good teeth and strong Essence by whatever wanker has the shiniest Caste Mark. They will fucking murder you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T16:25:26-07:00","id":209565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209557#post209557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lunar has, at most, a handful of weak blooded Exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>Says who?<br /> <br /> Seriously, forget the rest of your comment. How can you be sure that a Lunar can have, at most, a handful of Terestrial Exalts under his banner, and that their blood has to be weak?<br /> <br /> Even leaving aside the countless dynastic Lunars who've been played over the years, each of whom are capable of fathering or mothering Dragon-Blooded dynasties of their own, what about the Lunars who find First Age populations of Dragon-Blooded with legendary breeding living on pockets of reality somewhere in the Wyld? What about all the other ordinary ways I can think of for a Lunar to get Terrestrials of good breeding on his or her side?<br /> <br /> How exactly does anyone have the authority to just casually state, &quot;a Lunar can't do that&quot;? Especially when a lot of Lunars actually <i>have</i> done that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T16:38:54-07:00","id":209572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209557#post209557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Precisely what hope do you think a lone Silver Emperor is going to have when his entire nobility - historically the class from whom coups and assassinations spring like slinkies - is comprised of people who can not only shrug off his LOVE ME aura, who can not only take him in combat, but who are demonstrably better-suited to running a country than he is?</div> </div> </div> </div>By trusting them to run said country and treating them like friends, countrymen and family.<br /> <br /> As opposed to attack dogs or cattle. Or..what the fuck ever kind of batshit model you're imposing on the entire thought exercise here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T16:39:14-07:00","id":209573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209361#post209361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, it's seriously only too big because someone did not grok the map scale <i>at all</i>. The fluff doesn't even support its size.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's one of the problems with it. It's a weird, progressive culture in a world that is varying degrees of the Bronze Age. As you put it, it's supposed to be as cosmopolitan as the Realm. It feels a lot like the Tau in the 40k setting: in a universe where the factions include &quot;humans who don't really understand their technology and have ritualized it religiously,&quot; &quot;aliens whose civilization went through apocalypse,&quot; &quot;amoral space bugs drawn to the thing that makes human space travel possible,&quot; &quot;traitors to humanity who consider themselves free but are just as backwards,&quot; and &quot;ancient robots who awaken to find their empire gone and lesser races squabbling over the spoils,&quot; the Tau are a Great White Hope, an up-and-coming race that is progressing technologically rather than regressing, that comes across as Good Socialists who will conquer a human world and let them keep worshiping the Emperor, in a universe of morally-grey autocrats (if the Imperium conquered a Tau world it would torture and then publicly execute anyone professing loyalty to the Greater Good). It feels kind of out of place in the setting milieu, and that's why (I think) the authors started breaking that perfect facade and giving them problems, breakaway factions, and secret morally grey things they do (like secret forced sterilization of Imperial populations) - to make them fit better in the universe they exist in.<br /> <br /> There's something like that in Halta. It's a constitutional republic in a world where the closest thing to that is a confederation of otherwise-autocratic or military-controlled nations (or Nexus, which is basically quasi-anarchic in a way that works). It's cosmopolitan and enlightened, but it's not located on trade routes so the question becomes &quot;why, other than for its own sake?&quot; It has trained sciences without really any explanation for the breakthroughs other than A Lunar Did It: by this I mean, harvesting naturally-existing bioluminescent mushrooms or whatever for light makes sense, as does creating colonies of them for your needs, but it seems like Halta straight-up engineered them from non-glowly fungus or whatever.<br /> <br /> The tree-city conceit is indeed admittedly cool, as is the alliance with the Fair Folk (and the local Fair Folk having their own little internecine issues). The &quot;evergreen versus deciduous&quot; is a great concept for an eternal religious war. But to me an enjoyable Halta should evoke more...I dunno really. You have opportunities for Iroquois vs. Algonquin narratives with the Linowan except it does not really play out that way. The Linowan are made to look particularly brutish and savage compared to the Haltans (in other words, the depiction of the Haltans seems to be written to give them the moral high ground in that war because they're more advanced socially and therefore more worthy of existence).<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe that's what bothers me about it. The Delzahn are clearly inspired by Arabian stories, with a cool twist to the modern culture public modesty that is kind of the inversion of Islamic interpretations. The Haslanti make me think about the Vendel/Vesten from 7th Sea - a Norse culture, considered barbarians but with a rather technological twist (hot-air balloon airships reminding me a lot of the dirigibles in His Dark Materials). Halta doesn't have a good real-world parallel for its themes, so it seems alien, but in a kitschy Disney Princess way.<br /> <br /> From the start, Halta had notions that &quot;this couldn't happen on its own, a Lunar Had To Do It&quot; but it never out-and-out said that. And then it made it explicit. Adding Lunars to Chiaroscuro and Haslanti adds a little bit to them but you could see those societies existing as purely mortal, without Exalted interference. Halta doesn't. It doesn't really pan to any real-world society for influence (which is OK I guess). If any Eastern nation feels kind of Lunar-ish in the same way that the Haslanti and Delzahn do, to me it's the Linowan (because it's feasible but doesn't whack you over the head with the implication).<br /> <br /> The Realm is considered cosmopolitan and enlightened because it's like Rome or China or Japan. It's still a brutal military state, but it controls and influences so much that it sees itself as better, and the world kind of has to agree to an extent. It has an internal organization that the places it conquered (which it would consider more primitive) could not match in long-term opposition. The Realm is cosmopolitan because it has the money and the armies and domination. Halta has none of that, but it's still enlightened and cosmopolitan, Just Because? It doesn't really make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The super magic plants are because of their proximity to the Eastern Wyld. In the Far East, any kind of plant imaginable already exists. Haltan botanists go out into the wilderness for a few months, explore, then come back with several specimens of a newly discovered flower that sings when touched, playing back music it hears. They get sold to specialist thaumaturges, who (working with gods, god-bloods and wood elementals) figure out how to make it grow and breed in Creation. Then when they've got a few nurseries set up, they bring the first cartload of singing vines to a Guild factor, and his beady little eyes pop out of their sockets when he realizes how many dinars they'll be worth in the Scavvy Lands. And that's how Haltans get rich. Pharmaceuticals and plants are a big industry, one of their major exports. And it's how Haltans end up with plants that grow superabundant food, plants that light their streets like lamps, plants that circulate fresh water and carry waste away, etc. It's a bit optimistic, sure, the degree to which they've succeeded in utilizing all of them, but they have had the protection of Lunars (since late first edition) so it makes some sense, and it's nice to have one place in Creation that actually takes the Wyld into account and gives us a look at what a Far Eastern kingdom might be.<br /> <br /> They're not really all that democratic, also, as MG pointed out. I actually think the Haslanesh are more democratic; if memory serves, they're a federal republic. Halta is pretty much a monarchy. Candidates for Queen, IIRC, are chosen from the family of the previous Queen. Is that really such an unusual system, for a people whose laws originated in tribal customs? That's a real question; I'm not sure myself.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, though, I don't disagree. Halta is probably the best place to live in Creation outside the Realm itself. It's pretty much the Tau Empire of Creation. But there are plenty of 40k players who actually like the Tau, may the Emperor shine his blessings upon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-26-2014, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:00:32-07:00","id":209580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209565#post209565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Says who?<br /> <br /> Seriously, forget the rest of your comment. How can you be sure that a Lunar can have, at most, a handful of Terestrial Exalts under his banner, and that their blood has to be weak?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can be sure they're weak of blood because Lost Eggs are, pretty much by definition, the first Dragon-blooded to be Exalted in their families for centuries. They're born to mortals who forgot their great-to-the-power-of-nine grandmother ever so much as worshipfully clasped the robe of a passing demigod, much less bore them an illegitimate child from a one-night stand. Some great need or freak throwback sends that trace of heroic blood surging through their heart, and they are Exalted.<br /> <br /> That is the exact definition of Breeding 1.<br /> <br /> You can argue that maybe some kind of super duper destiny would warrant a given Lost Egg achieving Breeding 5 as a freak accident. I'd say that's absurd, because the Realm's invested incalculable effort in keeping its blood strong, and is barely holding its ground. Handing out inexplicably potent blood to random farmboys is daft.<br /> <br /> I can be sure there aren't many of them because the Realm, as discussed, is really good at snatching up Lost Eggs. Much better than Lunars, in fact. So once you've taken the total population of Lost Eggs, who can be described as &quot;pretty rare&quot;, and subtract the Realm's sizable slice, then subtract those lost to violence, then subtract those poached by Lookshy in the Scavenger Lands, then subtract those who have a pretty sweet gig already and don't want to be used as brood mares by a moon-demon with a grudge, you're left with... oh, look at that, <i>not very fucking many</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209565#post209565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even leaving aside the countless dynastic Lunars who've been played over the years, each of whom are capable of fathering or mothering Dragon-Blooded dynasties of their own, what about the Lunars who find First Age populations of Dragon-Blooded with legendary breeding living on pockets of reality somewhere in the Wyld? What about all the other ordinary ways I can think of for a Lunar to get Terrestrials of good breeding on his or her side?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for the first? Nope. Celestials don't have Breeding. A Solar isn't going to have Dragon-blooded children except by virtue of having a Dragon-blooded spouse.<br /> <br /> For the second, that's the dumbest special snowflake bullshit I've read in a while, and I've been reading the Kingkiller Chronicle. It's like being confronted with the statement &quot;the mighty works of the First Age have vanished from Creation&quot; and responding with &quot;but what about that one time in my IRC game a Sidereal time travelled from the past to drop an entire factory cathedral in my lap complete with instructions&quot;. Hey, maybe an entire regiment of Dragon-blooded with Breeding 6 and First Age sensibilities <i>is</i> drifting out in the Wyld, just waiting for some random Lunar to stumble onto them and lead them to destroy the Realm (for some reason). And maybe the Scarlet Empress is actually Caine in a wig and push-up bra. Who can tell?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209565#post209565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly does anyone have the authority to just casually state, &quot;a Lunar can't do that&quot;? Especially when a lot of Lunars actually <i>have</i> done that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that you are able to do whatever you like at your table. In turn, I hope you'll appreciate that I don't actually give a shit what you do at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:10:42-07:00","id":209581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209580#post209580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for the first? Nope. Celestials don't have Breeding. A Solar isn't going to have Dragon-blooded children except by virtue of having a Dragon-blooded spouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been over this. Even without a dot of Breeding (and I really can't imagine any ST I know ruling Breeding out), the children of someone from a patrician family would still have a 10% chance of Exalting. If any of them Exalt, <i>their</i> children automatically have a ~30% chance of Exalting and it goes up from there. And there are countless reasons a Dragon-Blood of good breeding would ally with a Lunar. The possibilities for it are endless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209580#post209580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the second, that's the dumbest special snowflake bullshit I've read in a while, and I've been reading the Kingkiller Chronicle. It's like being confronted with the statement &quot;the mighty works of the First Age have vanished from Creation&quot; and responding with &quot;but what about that one time in my IRC game a Sidereal time travelled from the past to drop an entire factory cathedral in my lap complete with instructions&quot;. Hey, maybe an entire regiment of Dragon-blooded with Breeding 6 and First Age sensibilities <i>is</i> drifting out in the Wyld, just waiting for some random Lunar to stumble onto them and lead them to destroy the Realm (for some reason). And maybe the Scarlet Empress is actually Caine in a wig and push-up bra. Who can tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2e setting books explicitly say there are islands in the Wyld that have been separated since the Shogunate era, complete with dragonbloods. It's hardly &quot;special snowflake bullshit.&quot; That's what the Wyld is like. That's what's there, along with many other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209580#post209580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate that you are able to do whatever you like at your table. In turn, I hope you'll appreciate that I don't actually give a shit what you do at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nice? I don't care whether you give a shit. I asked on what basis you could say, &quot;Lunars can have, at most, a handful of weak-blooded Terrestrials.&quot; Because in my opinion it's kind of stupid to say a Celestial Exalt can have, at most, a handful of Terrestrial followers and that their blood has to be weak. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:11:24-07:00","id":209583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209572#post209572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By trusting them to run said country and treating them like friends, countrymen and family.<br /> <br /> As opposed to attack dogs or cattle. Or..what the fuck ever kind of batshit model you're imposing on the entire thought exercise here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. Huh.<br /> <br /> See, the thing is, you can <i>either</i> have &quot;this Lunar is breeding his own Dragon-blooded army and accelerating time to get loads of Terrestrial babies and manipulating their blood to get super-DBs and making DB beastmen and etc etc&quot; or you can have &quot;this Lunar's circle of comrades includes his sworn Outcaste friends&quot;. One or the other. You can't treat Terrestrials as breeding stock, as discussed in the OP, and go &quot;oh but I'm respecting them and they're my friends so no betray plz&quot;. You want to play a mixed Circle? Man, go for it. That's not what this thread was about. This thread was about something way fucking dumber.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Also, seriously, no, you don't &quot;just trust&quot; your nobility, that's asinine and has never ever ended well for anyone who's tried it.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:17:56-07:00","id":209590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209583#post209583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the thing is, you can <i>either</i> have &quot;this Lunar is breeding his own Dragon-blooded army and accelerating time to get loads of Terrestrial babies and manipulating their blood to get super-DBs and making DB beastmen and etc etc&quot; or you can have &quot;this Lunar's circle of comrades includes his sworn Outcaste friends&quot;. One or the other. You can't treat Terrestrials as breeding stock, as discussed in the OP, and go &quot;oh but I'm respecting them and they're my friends so no betray plz&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Do your Terrestrial friends, whom you respect, not want to found a dynasty? Do they not want lots of Exalted descendants? Are they not interested in improving the strength of their blood? Would they not welcome the assistance of a proven friend?<br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm used to dynastic households where the young very much are breeding stock and accept that as their duty. The idea of having to <i>force</i> a Dragon-Blooded family to try and improve their bloodline is new to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-26-2014, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:33:26-07:00","id":209603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209293#post209293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please tell me more about things that lack a shred of credibility, Levi. What was the experience of playing or running Halta like for you?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Looking back at this thread, I think you've already made your point and this is starting to look like harassment. </b></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T18:17:08-07:00","id":209645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209553#post209553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All Exalted are opposed to the Realm and oppressed by it (other than DB's obviously). Infernals have lost everything, Abyssals have lost everything, and sure so have Lunars. Lunars can come from any walks of life. A Lunar could Exalt in Lookshy, Hislanti, Whitewall or any number of other nice places. Lunars are not an oppressed race, they are humans first, and humans can be oppressed or oppressors. Exalted are 'more-than-human' not some kinda fantastical mermaid that detaches itself from its cultural bias and joins a collective identity as 'marginalized peoples'. Lunars can be anyone or anything. They are the splat to just turn their back on that kind of story and take the form of a Guild Prince traveling the land making money and living the good life. Never in one place long enough to be sniffed out, always on the next caravan. *If* they were that oppressed.<br /> <br /> It is not fun stealing heat from the rest of the world and never generating any of your own. Lunars should have plenty of sorcerous works (tons in-fact) and epic stories to tell or show. This only allows other splats material to work with and their own targets to destroy. How else would you tell the story of a Dragonblooded game taking the fight to the Lunars? It would be boring if the PC's could only kill beastmen and never undermine anything significant in the Lunars 'plans' as they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars have actually often been presented as Exalted who come from the rougher side of the tracks. While the true reason for this was buried under a lot of cruft in 1e, it did come right out and say that this is probably because being born on the right side of the tracks means that there are more people who want to kill you waiting with sharpened knives upon a hypothetical Lunar Second Breath, and they have a head start over someone who ends up Chosen far, far away from &quot;civilization&quot;, or whatever it is that you want to call it. Someone becoming Exalted in enemy territory is going to quickly pass their heroic legacy on to another in a hurry, in all likelihood.<br /> <br /> So Lunars are likely to come from the oppressed more often than not. At the very least, they are statistically very likely to come from the ranks of those oppressed and/or hemmed in by the Realm, seeing as how that's over 4/5 of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T18:24:48-07:00","id":209646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209557#post209557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, no.<br /> <br /> That would be the Realm. The Realm has the best tools to locate, collect and breed Lost Eggs into a mighty host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Breed, certainly not, Lunars are the only splat with such charms. Collect, that would be a matter of power - so Solars would be best. Locate, Lunars have the following:<br /> <br /> <br /> Fellow Hound Insight: Sniff out other supernatural creatures<br /> Blood-kin Sense: Find one DB and you could find them all<br /> Leaf-falling Scrutiny: Detect any DB's in their territories, which easily spans hundreds of miles. So it would be difficult to slip the noose or meet in secret to rebel.<br /> Inevitable Spoor Discovery: Know when DB travels through the area<br /> Grandfather Spider Majesty: Ping, dragonborn was born<br /> <br /> That's before you look at the whole level of Sorcery they can access above DB's. So naw, Lunars are better at this idea than DB's. The Incarea designed it that way in the Primordial War.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209557#post209557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Precisely what hope do you think a lone Silver Emperor is going to have...</div> </div> </div> </div>Heaven's Reach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-26-2014, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T18:30:59-07:00","id":209648,"title":"","content":"Points are flying over heads like swallows on the dive. Is it spring yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T18:44:28-07:00","id":209653,"title":"","content":"I never liked Lunars as the &quot;breeding Exalted&quot; because it seemed like this unintended side-effect of several factors rather than a specific design decision, and it took them to a weird place.<br /> <br /> Like, okay, the general idea was -- initially where things stood was that Lunars lacked much connection to the world or a strong sense of purpose, but one of the points that was established was that they often used armies of beastmen, and could breed beastmen by accident. Not touching on the whole &quot;beastmen as a metaphor for savage natives from safari stories&quot; thing, because that's a whole kettle of fish, the idea that Lunar Exalted could breed beastmen seemed to be based on their inspirations -- Lunars draw on mythical monsters, and one of the common origins of such characters is weird or transgressive conceptions. So allowing Lunars to breed beastmen sometimes, even accidentally, is a nod to that, and it seems like the kind of thing the Wyld could do, and that's where they live. Okay! Beastmen were mostly an aesthetic thing early on, rather than &quot;super-soldiers&quot;.<br /> <br /> At this point the game was roused to attention about Lunars not having a coherent presentation or role in the setting, and in general not being attractive to players, so it set about working on that. 2e had to find a way to sell Lunars -- to make them feel like they <i>belonged</i> in the setting and also to make them appealing to people who didn't have their money out the moment they saw a loincloth. The whole deal where Lunars are playing a 4X game with experimental puppet nations at the edge of the world grew out of that. Personally I think this was a mistake, because it made them feel a little too much like Sidereals, but it was done under two constraints: it had to be a calculated refutation of 1e Lunars, and it had to be something they could sneak in the back door. (3e's big advantage is that it's tossed those constraints, giving it room to breathe.) So, okay, the Lunars like to engineer experimental societies, and we know they have a bunch of beastmen which are produced in part from people having sex with Lunars, so that makes them into extremely hands-on eugenicists, right? This part was not hugely emphasized in the Lunar book, but it was there.<br /> <br /> Now, 2e Lunars was a huge improvement and made everyone happy initially, but fast forwarding a few years people became dissatisfied with it, because its failings were more obvious when it wasn't being compared directly to 1e Lunars (which, in addition to being genuinely bad, had been blown up into an icon of towering evil by the fandom by that point). At this point people were making an effort to polish up the things that made Lunars feel unique and distinctive, so the &quot;breeding beastmen&quot; bit rose to increased prominence. This happened both in the fandom and in the official line -- if you compare the Lunar charms in Glories: Luna to the ones published in the Lunars manual, you can see that the Glories charms are really trying to push the handful of things that 2e established as &quot;distinctively Lunar&quot; that they're allowed to have Charms for. I don't think this was so much that everyone thought at that point that <i>yeah</i>, <i>Lunars should totally be about this</i>, so much as it was them making the most of what they had. But it further established the idea, and now here we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-26-2014, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T20:32:41-07:00","id":209778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209583#post209583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Huh.<br /> <br /> See, the thing is, you can <i>either</i> have &quot;this Lunar is breeding his own Dragon-blooded army and accelerating time to get loads of Terrestrial babies and manipulating their blood to get super-DBs and making DB beastmen and etc etc&quot; or you can have &quot;this Lunar's circle of comrades includes his sworn Outcaste friends&quot;. One or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>We already have one society in Exalted that disproves this statement thoroughly.<br /> <img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-Rl5aAAXi3Q8/UvXjPzF08cI/AAAAAAAAArQ/p6wYzpauWvY/s1600/Shambler+Bokor.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Dzibilchan is a not-so-soft eugenics project created by a Lunar for the sole purpose of making an army of Terrestrial Beastmen with which to fuck up the Realm. These Terrestrial Beastmen loved his ass up until the point of his death, and still revere afterward. No mini-usurpation, no betrayal. Likely because he elevated him to the ruling class the way the Sidereals did with the Shogunate DBs and later realm.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry bro, I know binary decisions and consequences are comforting, but that's not really the case here. You can make a breed program of Terrestrials while still respecting them enough to not give cute ideas about betrayal and revolution. And without having them wanting to join up with the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 07-26-2014, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T21:04:14-07:00","id":209791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209581#post209581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've been over this. Even without a dot of Breeding (and I really can't imagine any ST I know ruling Breeding out), the children of someone from a patrician family would still have a 10% chance of Exalting. If any of them Exalt, <i>their</i> children automatically have a ~30% chance of Exalting and it goes up from there. And there are countless reasons a Dragon-Blood of good breeding would ally with a Lunar. The possibilities for it are endless.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right until &quot;it goes up from there,&quot; because increasing Breeding is supposed to be really, really hard. It really fucks with game thematics if Lunars are better at creating more &quot;pure&quot; Dragon-Blooded than the <i>actual Dragon-Blooded</i> are. Celestials or not. High Breeding was predominant for much of the First Age because the Dragon-Blooded were only allowed to marry and mate with each other; as the Age went on, you had more and more bastards sprouting up in cities where a DB ship made port or a DB battalion sheltered in the winter. By DotFA you have setting quotes saying the Legendary Breeding is basically gone because of interbreeding with non-DBs. The Shogunate and Contagion hit this even further.<br /> <br /> This narrative is partly reflected in the Breeding rules, which are supposed to show that the Realm cares a lot about marriages in the same way that Pure-bloods from Harry Potter do, that Lookshy cares less and is more focused on having a ton of okay-blooded DBs versus a few super-pure-blooded ones, and that outcastes are pretty much just Exalted out of sheer luck and a drop of Dragon's Blood from their great-grandfather who, like, nabbed a tavern wench while on campaign 400 years ago, or whose family contained DBs before the Contagion but they're all gone until a remote scion Exalts the better part of a millennium later. The mechanical effect of this narrative is that Breeding is cheap for Dynasts, more expensive for the Seventh Legion, and fuck-all ridiculous for outcastes (the outcaste chargen rules are really, really bad, but that's neither here nor there).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209590#post209590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'm used to dynastic households where the young very much are breeding stock and accept that as their duty. The idea of having to <i>force</i> a Dragon-Blooded family to try and improve their bloodline is new to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's your experience? I see the Dynasty focusing on marrying highborn nobles with close family ties to the Empress to each other to try and have that union create more powerful nobles (the Breeding Background being a purely OOC abstract concept). I much prefer the young as acting as political pawns for their elders, as happened often in Roman society through marital alliances, rather than DBs IC getting into the narrative of literally breeding better Exalts. It's not an exact science IC, and it shouldn't be, because it removes the mystical aspects of Exaltation if it is treated that way in-character. Breeding is not an IC thing or quality - I think it would be more like &quot;he has the Sesus chin, definitely&quot; or &quot;she has the Mnemon hairline, bless her.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209581#post209581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and I really can't imagine any ST I know ruling Breeding out)</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? You mean an ST is going to say &quot;well, your backstory is a patrician, but you neither have the Breeding background (which is by RAW for DBs only) nor have the Merit for non-DBs, but I'm going to treat you as Breeding 5 because of your backstory.&quot; I can't imagine any ST actually doing <i>that</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209565#post209565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, forget the rest of your comment. How can you be sure that a Lunar can have, at most, a handful of Terestrial Exalts under his banner, and that their blood has to be weak?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, you might have more. If they're Dynasts, it makes sense for some NPC Dynasts to have strong blood. It doesn't make sense for NPC outcastes to do so, in most circumstances. Usually the high-Breeding outcaste is going to be a PC, and dumping so many of his starting resources into Breeding (because of how fucking terrible it was designed to scale for non-Realm DBs) that the player is basically shouting &quot;ST, I want the fact that I'm super pure-blood but both my parents are dirt farmers (as far as I know) to be really important to my story!&quot; That's a PC's prerogative though. If all outcaste NPCs are running around with high Breeding, it creates big suspension-of-disbelief issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T21:34:04-07:00","id":209809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209791#post209791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right until &quot;it goes up from there,&quot; because increasing Breeding is supposed to be really, really hard. It really fucks with game thematics if Lunars are better at creating more &quot;pure&quot; Dragon-Blooded than the <i>actual Dragon-Blooded</i> are. Celestials or not. High Breeding was predominant for much of the First Age because the Dragon-Blooded were only allowed to marry and mate with each other; as the Age went on, you had more and more bastards sprouting up in cities where a DB ship made port or a DB battalion sheltered in the winter. By DotFA you have setting quotes saying the Legendary Breeding is basically gone because of interbreeding with non-DBs. The Shogunate and Contagion hit this even further.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about increasing the Breeding background. With zero dots of Breeding, going by the errata rules, the child of a Dragon-Blood and an ordinary mortal has a 30% chance to Exalt. The child of a Dragon-Blood and a patrician has a 40% chance to Exalt. The child of two Dragon-Bloods has a 60% chance to Exalt. The Breeding background, as of the errata, only gives additional bonuses on top of these. So as I said, the child of a Dragon-Blood has a 30% chance to Exalt and it goes up from there, without taking Breeding into consideration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209791#post209791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that's your experience? I see the Dynasty focusing on marrying highborn nobles with close family ties to the Empress to each other to try and have that union create more powerful nobles (the Breeding Background being a purely OOC abstract concept). I much prefer the young as acting as political pawns for their elders, as happened often in Roman society through marital alliances, rather than DBs IC getting into the narrative of literally breeding better Exalts. It's not an exact science IC, and it shouldn't be, because it removes the mystical aspects of Exaltation if it is treated that way in-character. Breeding is not an IC thing or quality - I think it would be more like &quot;he has the Sesus chin, definitely&quot; or &quot;she has the Mnemon hairline, bless her.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what exactly you're finding fault with here. The way they're written, every Great House is interested in maintaining and improving the strength of its blood, and every one manages its bloodline with an eye toward having an overall high rate of Exaltation.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209791#post209791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? You mean an ST is going to say &quot;well, your backstory is a patrician, but you neither have the Breeding background (which is by RAW for DBs only) nor have the Merit for non-DBs, but I'm going to treat you as Breeding 5 because of your backstory.&quot; I can't imagine any ST actually doing <i>that</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant I think all the STs I know would open up Breeding to dynastic Celestials at chargen, or work out some other arrangement so that the character's dynastic heritage would have an appropriate mechanical effect ingame.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209791#post209791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh sure, you might have more. If they're Dynasts, it makes sense for some NPC Dynasts to have strong blood. It doesn't make sense for NPC outcastes to do so, in most circumstances. Usually the high-Breeding outcaste is going to be a PC, and dumping so many of his starting resources into Breeding (because of how fucking terrible it was designed to scale for non-Realm DBs) that the player is basically shouting &quot;ST, I want the fact that I'm super pure-blood but both my parents are dirt farmers (as far as I know) to be really important to my story!&quot; That's a PC's prerogative though. If all outcaste NPCs are running around with high Breeding, it creates big suspension-of-disbelief issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are so many ways a Lunar (whether a PC or an NPC, a character in a game or just one in someone's story) could have a large number of Terrestrials following him. Just playing a Dynastic Lunar PC in a game, it's not impossible for you to end up with an entire army (albeit it wouldn't be easy) willing to follow your orders. And there are Lunar creations like Dzibilchan, gods only know how many all over Creation, and beyond it in the Wyld. Exalted is such a huge and dynamic setting, anything is possible. It seems incredible to just say Lunars can't have a large number of Terrestrials under their banner like there's some rule against it in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-27-2014, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:29:01-07:00","id":210075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209778#post209778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We already have one society in Exalted that disproves this statement thoroughly.<br /> <br /> Dzibilchan is a not-so-soft eugenics project created by a Lunar for the sole purpose of making an army of Terrestrial Beastmen with which to fuck up the Realm. These Terrestrial Beastmen loved his ass up until the point of his death, and still revere afterward. No mini-usurpation, no betrayal. Likely because he elevated him to the ruling class the way the Sidereals did with the Shogunate DBs and later realm.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry bro, I know binary decisions and consequences are comforting, but that's not really the case here. You can make a breed program of Terrestrials while still respecting them enough to not give cute ideas about betrayal and revolution. And without having them wanting to join up with the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm, I may be wrong on this, but isn't the Empire of Alligators, well, not canon? So I find it largely immaterial as a counter in the vein of &quot;But you're wrong, because we already have this in canon!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which, by the way, isn't actually that good a defense, given that there is a lot badly written stuff in the books, but just because it's official it doesn't make it better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T07:59:53-07:00","id":210200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210075#post210075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhm, I may be wrong on this, but isn't the Empire of Alligators, well, not canon? So I find it largely immaterial as a counter in the vein of &quot;But you're wrong, because we already have this in canon!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which, by the way, isn't actually that good a defense, given that there is a lot badly written stuff in the books, but just because it's official it doesn't make it better.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't quite say it was canon. And he doesn't need a defense. It's for someone who says it's impossible for something to exist in the setting to explain why it's impossible, and if they can't do that convincingly, there's no reason to expect others to agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:00:26-07:00","id":210251,"title":"","content":"The Empire of Alligators isn't canon, but I do think it's an excellent example of this kind of project done <i>wrong. </i>That is to say, the Lunar did it wrong, not the writer did it wrong. Dzilbilchan is a cautionary tale in designing a vicious and unsustainable society that can't survive the death of its architect, to say nothing of being a distasteful exercise throughout. The basic idea that Dragon-Blooded beastmen are opposed to the Realm by default is a solid one, however. The prejudice of most of Creation against beastmen would not be lessened by their Exalted status.<br /> <br /> There are two components of the plan. First, the Lunar needs a clan of loyal beastmen who can be culturally swayed towards accepting Exalted members of their number. This doesn't seem to be a problem for a lot of Lunars. Use of Fish or Fowl Gestation and Tiger and Sultan's Daughter removes the need for forced bestiality. The clan should be small and relatively isolated (aquatic or flying beastmen are ideal for this) to minimize cultural influence, migration and predation. They should be as stable and sustainable a society as is possible. Locating an out of the way jade mine or other important resources with the assistance of spirits is recommended. Given that this plan will take at least decades, now would be an excellent opportunity to task bind demons to amass resources for your new society's benefit.<br /> <br /> Next, the Lunar needs beastman children with Dragon-Blooded exaltation potential. Using the above mentioned Charms, The Steward need only seduce an Outcaste or Dynast in female form (using Twin Faced Hero if necessary) and imprint the unborn children with beastman traits from any of the species of her heart's blood library. Seducing a dozen randy Dragon-bloods should be no obstacle for a Lunar suited to the task. With Tiger ans Seahorse Dynasty she can guarantee triplets with her clutch of eagle-eggs and repeat the process as many times as is necessary to grow a large stable with which to breed a future beastman gens. To avoid the problem of half-sibling-incest, she can simply wear different human forms during the pregnancy so that her children are born to different biological mothers.<br /> <br /> The Lunar should raise and educate the first generation, her own children, teaching them, in addition to a robust general education, sorcery, the forging of arcane contracts and the working of jade. She should draw up cultural practices calculated to maximise the prosperity of her clan and its new ruling caste, appoint a strong successor, and then depart.<br /> <br /> Within a few short generations, provided the new gens does not collapse to infighting, there should be a strong new faction of dragon-bloods in the world, armed with all a Lunar mastermind can grant them and friendly to the interests of the Children of the Moon.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Wait wait, I forgot you need to have sex in the Wyld to make beastmen without bestiality.<br /> <br /> NEVER MIND, another plan defeated by really stupid Lunar mechanics. This plan only works for E6 elders who have access to Beast Lords of the Blessed Isle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 07-27-2014, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:10:48-07:00","id":210263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210200#post210200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He didn't quite say it was canon. And he doesn't need a defense. It's for someone who says it's impossible for something to exist in the setting to explain why it's impossible, and if they can't do that convincingly, there's no reason to expect others to agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Revlid did explain why he felt such a thing was impossible. He wrote to long posts about it even. On the other hand, TV Head reply felt more like &quot;Well, this thing exists, so you must be wrong!&quot;<br /> Which is not an actual response, or an argument, and is itself subjet to the same &quot;Well, that's just like, your opinion, man&quot; answer you just gave.<br /> <br /> Because you see, what you describe doesn't exist in setting, as it exists right. It just doesn't, no matter what people do at their own tables.<br /> Revlid and others have put forth reasons and arguments as to why such a thing doesn't happen, and it's actually up to those who believe the opposite to put forth reasons why they believe a Lunar breeding program is possible.<br /> IMO, so far I haven't seen anything compelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:19:54-07:00","id":210287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210263#post210263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, so far I haven't seen anything compelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I tried.<br /> <br /> I maintain that the key is <i>beastmen</i> terrestrials, who are immune to the draw of the Realm and its riches because they are despised as the anathema are.<br /> <br /> I also think it is an historic mistake to attempt to <i>rule</i> the resulting Terrestrial dynasty. They must self govern, but you will through circumstance and carefully loaded education have created a strong ally for yourself and other Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 07-27-2014, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:28:38-07:00","id":210292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210263#post210263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Revlid did explain why he felt such a thing was impossible. He wrote to long posts about it even. On the other hand, TV Head reply felt more like &quot;Well, this thing exists, so you must be wrong!&quot;<br /> Which is not an actual response, or an argument, and is itself subjet to the same &quot;Well, that's just like, your opinion, man&quot; answer you just gave.<br /> <br /> Because you see, what you describe doesn't exist in setting, as it exists right. It just doesn't, no matter what people do at their own tables.<br /> Revlid and others have put forth reasons and arguments as to why such a thing doesn't happen, and it's actually up to those who believe the opposite to put forth reasons why they believe a Lunar breeding program is possible.<br /> IMO, so far I haven't seen anything compelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find Revlid's argument compelling, and I've said why. It's based on the assumption that a Lunar can't gain the loyalty of a large number of Terrestrials, which is a very fragile assumption, in my opinion. One should not be so casual about assuming something is impossible for Celestial Exalts to do. If Sidereals and Solars can both get DBs on their side, I see no reason why Lunars can't.<br /> <br /> There are no published examples of Lunar dominions involving a large number of Dragon-Bloods, but that doesn't mean they don't exist in Creation, because the truth is we really have no idea what exists in Creation. What is published of it in all the books is only meant to be a small fraction of the whole. We're never meant to say, as players, &quot;there's nothing like that in the books, therefore it doesn't exist.&quot; Let alone that it can't exist. Pretty much anything can exist in Exalted, it just takes a little imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-27-2014, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:33:43-07:00","id":210297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210292#post210292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't find Revlid's reasons compelling, and I've said why. It's just based on the assumption that a Lunar can't gain the loyalty of a large number of Terrestrials, which is a very weak assumption, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> There are no published examples of Lunar dominions involving a large number of Dragon-Bloods, but that doesn't mean they don't exist in Creation, because what is published of Creation is only meant to be a small fraction of the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Immaculate propaganda was spread to counter this very possibility since the days of the Shogunate, and the Realm took it and ran with it. They've been doubling down on stories of devilish Anathema for eight centuries. Everyone remembers legends of those figures as horrible devils who would have drowned the world in darkness, and which Dragon-Blooded are meant to fight. This is a much bigger obstacle than you're giving it credit for because everyone in the setting just knows that Celestials are dangerous at minimum, and Lunars have been acting the part that propaganda ascribes to them since the fall of the Realm. Establishing anything counter to this world view is going to be an uphill battle among uphill battles, among climbs from the bottom of a sheer cliff to the top of a plateau.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:38:52-07:00","id":210306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210297#post210297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immaculate propaganda was spread to counter this very possibility since the days of the Shogunate, and the Realm took it and ran with it. They've been doubling down on stories of devilish Anathema for eight centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh noes, and I'll bet Lunars don't have charms or powers they can use to counter folk stories and negative propaganda, do they?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:49:53-07:00","id":210314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210306#post210306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh noes, and I'll bet Lunars don't have charms or powers they can use to counter folk stories and negative propaganda, do they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd say Dragon-Blood social magic is quite a bit better than Lunar, but I assume that's a problem of design and not design intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:53:23-07:00","id":210318,"title":"","content":"Besides which, there are, canonically, plenty of parts of Creation where Immaculates and their propaganda are spat upon. I mean look at the Haslanti League. Lunars are viewed overtly as cultural heroes there, and across a large part of the North. Luna herself is widely venerated. Immaculate propaganda isn't something Lunars have to worry about in their own territories. In places where something like this would take place, the folk stories and propaganda should be in favor of Lunars, not against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:59:24-07:00","id":210346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210318#post210318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides which, there are, canonically, plenty of parts of Creation where Immaculates and their propaganda are spat upon. I mean look at the Haslanti League. Lunars are viewed overtly as cultural heroes there, and across a large part of the North. Luna herself is widely venerated. Immaculate propaganda isn't something Lunars have to worry about in their own territories. In places where something like this would take place, the folk stories and propaganda should be in favor of Lunars, not against.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only part of the problem. There are plenty of areas where the Realm doesn't rule. There are <i>very few</i> areas where it isn't known that they hold sway over the majority of the world from the Blessed Isle and enjoy unimaginable wealth, luxury and power by virtue of their birthright. A prospective gatherer of lost eggs is going to have a serious uphill struggle trying to convince his charges that his way is better and more importantly that he can provide them with better prospects than the Realm can.<br /> <br /> Granted the Realm will ship a lost egg off to a military academy or a temple for hard decades in their service before they even have a shot at being part of the real power structure of the Realm, but this isn't nearly as well known, and even if it was, that might still be a better deal than being breeding stock for a Lunar's plans, however well Lunars are viewed by the Haslanti and Haltans.<br /> <br /> I mean, would you rather follow this beast-king to an uncertain fate or make for the Blessed Isle where your birthight is assured? Lunar social Charms might help you here, but it's hardly a sure thing.<br /> <br /> This is why I suggest beastmen Lunars. The siren call of the Realm and Lookshy is lost on them. They face an uncertain world that fears and despises them despite their Exaltation, and they have only their fellow outsiders for guidance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 07-27-2014, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:02:44-07:00","id":210348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210075#post210075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhm, I may be wrong on this, but isn't the Empire of Alligators, well, not canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on whether or not you think the Ink Monkey articles are canon or not. I tend to treat them that way, though I understand that others won't.<br /> <br /> <br /> And it's less about canonicity than demonstrating plausibility. Outside of falling into the classic blunder that all Exalted run societies seem to run into, Dzibilchan worked. It created a society of Terrestrial Beastmen, who did not betray Makar to the Realm and were loyal to their Kingdom. Of course, that society lived in an brutal apartheid, treating non-beastmen as livestock and probably wouldn't be an approach most PCs would want to take.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:06:38-07:00","id":210351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210297#post210297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Immaculate propaganda was spread to counter this very possibility since the days of the Shogunate, and the Realm took it and ran with it. They've been doubling down on stories of devilish Anathema for eight centuries. Everyone remembers legends of those figures as horrible devils who would have drowned the world in darkness, and which Dragon-Blooded are meant to fight. This is a much bigger obstacle than you're giving it credit for because everyone in the setting just knows that Celestials are dangerous at minimum, and Lunars have been acting the part that propaganda ascribes to them since the fall of the Realm. Establishing anything counter to this world view is going to be an uphill battle among uphill battles, among climbs from the bottom of a sheer cliff to the top of a plateau.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Love how 3E is allowed to turn this on its head, as it should, but if anyone wants to borrow some of the primise in the mean time they are a raving lunatic. Lunars have stories too. Lunars have charms and experience in making nations (Blood and Salt specifically calls Lunars out as making nations within the An'Tang region and then we have in Masters of Jade the Three Devil Princes). People throw out Halta, people ignore the direction Exalted is going with 3E, and people ignore Lunar potential.<br /> <br /> I see that about half of the forum has this opinion:<br /> - Lunars should have no themes, the breeding exalted is foolish.<br /> - All the themes they have should be abolished (dream magic, territory magic, breeding magic and more) and most likely end up with the other splats *eye roll*<br /> - Lunars are not allowed to borrow from themes attributed to other splats...btw we've attributed all of them.<br /> - Lunars should not build nations - it steals heat from the Sidereals (what?).<br /> <br /> It's all echo chamber. They have some cool charms, just not a ton, and there is a lot of potential. Lunars just need polish and to move past the 2E mentality that Lunars suck and should suck. Now, I don't like everything that I've heard is going down with Lunars, but it does sound like their perception and reception is going to be a lot better. Not to the whole of Creation, but they will have some ground to stand on and, the forum faction I speak of, won't be able to sweep them off into the Wyld as a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:08:07-07:00","id":210352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210348#post210348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on whether or not you think the Ink Monkey articles are canon or not. I tend to treat them that way, though I understand that others won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a point of order, the thing I posted was unpublished material posted on the forums by Dean Shomshak. Although he <i>was</i> a member of Ink Monkeys, it's not quite the same thing. Otherwise I agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:15:09-07:00","id":210358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210297#post210297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Immaculate propaganda was spread to counter this very possibility since the days of the Shogunate, and the Realm took it and ran with it. They've been doubling down on stories of devilish Anathema for eight centuries. Everyone remembers legends of those figures as horrible devils who would have drowned the world in darkness, and which Dragon-Blooded are meant to fight. This is a much bigger obstacle than you're giving it credit for because everyone in the setting just knows that Celestials are dangerous at minimum, and Lunars have been acting the part that propaganda ascribes to them since the fall of the Realm. Establishing anything counter to this world view is going to be an uphill battle among uphill battles, among climbs from the bottom of a sheer cliff to the top of a plateau.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just means you've got to get your Terrestrial fellows while they're young, so as to imprint them on you.<br /> <br /> I mean, if a bunch of guys who sort of looked like you and are currently oppressing the shit out of nearby village tell you that your adoptive mother is an awful monster and they're here to kill her, how would you react?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 07-27-2014, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:24:59-07:00","id":210385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210346#post210346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is only part of the problem. There are plenty of areas where the Realm doesn't rule. There are <i>very few</i> areas where it isn't known that they hold sway over the majority of the world from the Blessed Isle and enjoy unimaginable wealth, luxury and power by virtue of their birthright. A prospective gatherer of lost eggs is going to have a serious uphill struggle trying to convince his charges that his way is better and more importantly that he can provide them with better prospects than the Realm can.<br /> <br /> Granted the Realm will ship a lost egg off to a military academy or a temple for hard decades in their service before they even have a shot at being part of the real power structure of the Realm, but this isn't nearly as well known, and even if it was, that might still be a better deal than being breeding stock for a Lunar's plans, however well Lunars are viewed by the Haslanti and Haltans.<br /> <br /> I mean, would you rather follow this beast-king to an uncertain fate or make for the Blessed Isle where your birthight is assured? Lunar social Charms might help you here, but it's hardly a sure thing.<br /> <br /> This is why I suggest beastmen Lunars. The siren call of the Realm and Lookshy is lost on them. They face an uncertain world that fears and despises them despite their Exaltation, and they have only their fellow outsiders for guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right that beastman Dragon-Bloods are basically immune to Realm recruiting. But Realm propaganda really has no effect even on humans in much of Creation. When a teenage Haslanti receives Terrestrial Exaltation, and he gets to meet Gerd Marrow-Eater and other Lunars, he's going to see them as celebrated heroes he's known from childhood, basically patron saints of his people, not as the evil anathema a peasant on the Blessed Isle would see them as. And Haslanti have no great affection for the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:37:03-07:00","id":210391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210351#post210351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Love how 3E is allowed to turn this on its head, as it should, but if anyone wants to borrow some of the primise in the mean time they are a raving lunatic. Lunars have stories too. Lunars have charms and experience in making nations (Blood and Salt specifically calls Lunars out as making nations within the An'Tang region and then we have in Masters of Jade the Three Devil Princes). People throw out Halta, people ignore the direction Exalted is going with 3E, and people ignore Lunar potential.<br /> <br /> I see that about half of the forum has this opinion:<br /> - Lunars should have no themes, the breeding exalted is foolish.</div> </div> </div> </div>We disagree about themes you think that Lunars should have, not that they should have no themes. You want to disagree about being the old monster in the wilderness, that's fine, but you don't get to say that it's not a theme. Also, the breeding exalted what? You're breaking up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - All the themes they have should be abolished (dream magic, territory magic, breeding magic and more) and most likely end up with the other splats *eye roll* </div> </div> </div>Of the themes you listed, Lunars barely had any of the first, need some extreme revision for the execution of the second, and the third only really exists so that producing beastfolk doesn't necessarily entail performing bestiality. They aren't really the strongest parts of being a Lunar. That distinction belongs to beast-related shapeshifting. 2e was extremely gunshy about pushing this forward on account of a rather flawed perception that no one wants to see inspiration from Werewolf in Lunars. What people don't want to see in Lunars is a Renown system, or the nonsense of the Storytelling chapter of the first edition book, if you can even call it a storytelling chapter. Wrecking people as a tiger or elephant should be pushed forward as things, not hidden behind a curtain made of even more Silver Solar effects than first edition had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Lunars are not allowed to borrow from themes attributed to other splats...btw we've attributed all of them. </div> </div> </div>The complaint started breaking up at the end. Attributed what?<br /> <br /> Cramming themes into Lunars has gotten out of hand. In the end, they're left looking like an unsuccessful attempt at Frankenstein-type reanimation. Bits and pieces, bits and pieces, weird sorcery!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Lunars should not build nations - it steals heat from the Sidereals (what?). </div> </div> </div>Moreover, it's not consistent with how the world is set up. The Scarlet Empress canonically marched on and destroyed centers of Anathema power, if she couldn't just smite them. A handful of locations that were nondescript can exists in 2e without calling setting integrity into serious question. And, as a 2e complaint, if the Solars have all those nifty Charms, they could bulldoze centuries of Lunar efforts away in the time since Solars have been back, if not sooner. All of the hats that you're complaining that you can't hang on Lunars anymore didn't fit very well in the first place, and it was misguided to try setting things up that way.<br /> <br /> (Heat is credibility. The way that 2e went about trying to build it up for Lunars was full of blunders.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:40:08-07:00","id":210394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210351#post210351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Love how 3E is allowed to turn this on its head, as it should, but if anyone wants to borrow some of the primise in the mean time they are a raving lunatic. Lunars have stories too. Lunars have charms and experience in making nations (Blood and Salt specifically calls Lunars out as making nations within the An'Tang region and then we have in Masters of Jade the Three Devil Princes). People throw out Halta, people ignore the direction Exalted is going with 3E, and people ignore Lunar potential.<br /> <br /> I see that about half of the forum has this opinion:<br /> - Lunars should have no themes, the breeding exalted is foolish.<br /> - All the themes they have should be abolished (dream magic, territory magic, breeding magic and more) and most likely end up with the other splats *eye roll*<br /> - Lunars are not allowed to borrow from themes attributed to other splats...btw we've attributed all of them.<br /> - Lunars should not build nations - it steals heat from the Sidereals (what?).<br /> <br /> It's all echo chamber. They have some cool charms, just not a ton, and there is a lot of potential. Lunars just need polish and to move past the 2E mentality that Lunars suck and should suck. Now, I don't like everything that I've heard is going down with Lunars, but it does sound like their perception and reception is going to be a lot better. Not to the whole of Creation, but they will have some ground to stand on and, the forum faction I speak of, won't be able to sweep them off into the Wyld as a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunars need a complete rewrite, and they need some new themes. The problem is that they started with something fairly weak for a protagonist, and they haven't had a full correction made. There's been a few attempts, but it never really stuck. What do they do? What is their theme? They shouldn't get a theme from someone else, and there's lots of room for what they are, and there's lots of stuff to do with it, but the problem is as always, what we see here:<br /> <br /> If Lunars were badasses and capable of doing the things that they should be capable of doing, like breeding their own DB-Beastman family, why aren't any of these things written about in canon? Instead, we have... not much for thousands of years of work. A couple of societies that are working well, with the Lunar hand only very lightly pushing them at the beginning, and then a little support later. This leaves the Lunars basically sitting down doing nothing for most of their time. Have a look at the following post here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://pixel.quantserve.com/pixel/p-edL3gsnUjJzw-.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history\" target=\"_blank\"> Troubled Lunar History - Chancel Aleph </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history\" target=\"_blank\"> http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Holden and the rest of the writers know that the way Lunars are described is not ok, and that it hasn't been fixed. Even more, they know it CAN'T be fixed with touch ups and a few new parts. They need a complete overhaul and rebuild from scratch. There are some really good ideas in the charmsets, and in some of the story sets, but the Lunars need a narrative that is theirs, and not someone elses. A Lunar playing patron to a DB Beastman culture out past the Threshold, near the edge of the Wyld? That's a cool thing for one or two Lunars to do for a while. Dragon-Blooded live a long time, so several hundred years is not an unreasonable time frame. So what have the others been doing? Eating Solars, killing Fair Folk, not teaching Occult secrets (seriously, half of their occult secrets are only for No-Moons and even those are only for the No-Moons who play well with others in a group of Exalted who are by description, loners who don't play with others who form packs that don't work well), and loving Solars (except when they are eating them. Except, occasionally, both?).<br /> <br /> It's coming. Two more years, maybe? Cross your fingers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:45:43-07:00","id":210401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210391#post210391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, it's not consistent with how the world is set up. The Scarlet Empress canonically marched on and destroyed centers of Anathema power, if she couldn't just smite them. A handful of locations that were nondescript can exists in 2e without calling setting integrity into serious question. And, as a 2e complaint, if the Solars have all those nifty Charms, they could bulldoze centuries of Lunar efforts away in the time since Solars have been back, if not sooner. All of the hats that you're complaining that you can't hang on Lunars anymore didn't fit very well in the first place, and it was misguided to try setting things up that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars have powerful nations and have fought the Realm nearly off the Caul to the point they are being choked out behind their last cities gates. Even in 2E Ma Ha has a huge and threatening empire right out in the open. This junk aboun nondescript hidden nations has been pushed way too far. That's fine, but till the Great Congation, after that Lunars should have a field day in the Boardermarches and then steadily make gains into the Threshold.<br /> <br /> 3E is giving me a mighty fine hat rack so not too worried dude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T11:04:49-07:00","id":210409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210394#post210394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunars were badasses and capable of doing the things that they should be capable of doing, like breeding their own DB-Beastman family, why aren't any of these things written about in canon? Instead, we have... not much for thousands of years of work. A couple of societies that are working well, with the Lunar hand only very lightly pushing them at the beginning, and then a little support later. This leaves the Lunars basically sitting down doing nothing for most of their time. Have a look at the following post here:</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because not everything they do is described, that doesn't we just assume they haven't done anything and have been sitting on their hands for the past 800 years. o_O Are you crazy? They're Celestial Exalts! Of course they've been doing things!!<br /> <br /> Seriously, I sometimes wonder why I visit these forums at all. I like Exalted, I like Exalted 2nd Edition, I like Lunars in Exalted 2nd Edition. But every time I come here, the only thing I hear is that it's broken and sucks and needs a complete rewrite, worst game ever, worst &quot;splat&quot; ever, can't do anything, not enough written, too much, too little, or just,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=209376#post209376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuck this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why more people can't simply enjoy the game. If there are holes in the freaking backstory, assume stuff happened in those holes. What sense does it make to conclude nothing happened? This is Exalted!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T11:36:34-07:00","id":210437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210409#post210409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, I sometimes wonder why I visit these forums at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 'Exalted Forum Echo Chamber' has deafened many and is the contributing factor for the plethora of misinformation we see on the forum. <br /> <br /> In particular I find it funny that people harp on and on about how the Terrestrial DB's should be able to do this and that cause they are &quot;Exalts&quot;. How they should never be oppressed or used, cause they are &quot;Exalts&quot;. Meanwhile the same people saying it want to oppress the hell out of Lunars. Lunars are, in the terms of this forum, rarely even considered &quot;Exalts&quot; or valid in terms of the protections afforded such entities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T11:55:16-07:00","id":210449,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QiZNSzWIaLo\" target=\"_blank\">A dramatic reenactment of how many of us feel about second edition, particularly as it pertains to Lunars.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210437#post210437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 'Exalted Forum Echo Chamber' has deafened many and is the contributing factor for the plethora of misinformation we see on the forum.<br /> <br /> In particular I find it funny that people harp on and on about how the Terrestrial DB's should be able to do this and that cause they are &quot;Exalts&quot;. How they should never be oppressed or used, cause they are &quot;Exalts&quot;. Meanwhile the same people saying it want to oppress the hell out of Lunars. Lunars are, in the terms of this forum, rarely even considered &quot;Exalts&quot; or valid in terms of the protections afforded such entities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You say &quot;echo chamber&quot;, I say, &quot;people dropping by trying to do the same things that won't work over and over again, such that everyone is tired of hearing of them and has a standardized set of responses to conserve energy for other endeavors&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 07-27-2014, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T11:57:02-07:00","id":210451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210409#post210409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because not everything they do is described, that doesn't we just assume they haven't done anything and have been sitting on their hands for the past 800 years. o_O Are you crazy? They're Celestial Exalts! Of course they've been doing things!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing. Sure, we can assume the Lunars have done some epic ambiguous things things. <i>But we have no examples of what</i>. We have nothing to point to and say: &quot;that's what a Lunar can do after 700 years, or after 2000 years.&quot; We have no author who cared enough to lobby something interesting into publication. Lunars as a splat are ridiculously focused on the distant past rather than the present that is the default setting of the game. But despite their obsessive focus on the past, they have nothing to show for it.<br /> <br /> What we have is mostly a bunch of people who alternatively mope or play out revenge porn for an event (granted, a terrible, world-changing event) that happened 2000 years ago, and then we have a ton of them hanging out in the Wyld like losers (fearing probably-described-as-too-competent Sidereals) who eventually just die forgotten and fighting the vanguard of the Balorian Crusade. Sure, a given ST can fill in gaps with whatever he wants to fit his story, and to hell with the rest of the setting. That's an okay tack to take, <i>for one table</i>. But when authors write books and create splat histories, they have to do it with their eye in multiple places: (1) they have to do it with an eye to &quot;this is a thing that someone in this splat did, as an example for the scope of awesome things you can do given enough time and effort&quot;; (2) they have to create big (but coherent and reasonable) plot and story hooks that might influence characters from that splatbook or other splatbooks to hook their backstories on those hooks if they want, or provide hooks for STs to base in-game stories off of; (3) they have to do it in a way where it fits into and does not undermine consistent setting history (basically, the history has to make logical sense).<br /> <br /> In the case of Lunars, authors have have not bothered doing (1), and have put relatively little effort into (2) by making most of the canon Lunars elders and removing them from any contact with the world beyond their fiefdom. They have other splats doing those big things and occupying so much of that narrative space that to simply add some &quot;big things Lunars did&quot; out of categories (1) and (2) to the setting, they might unbalance (3) in ways that make the setting not make sense when viewed from the outside. Instead authors have chosen to keep (3) largely as it was for 2 editions (not radically revising parts of history) and instead spelled out nothing great that Lunars have done, giving prospective players and STs very little to reference about what their Lunar can do, when 300 people like that Lunar have done nothing noteworthy of recording in a book for inspiration.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;the ST can fix it&quot; is a Rule Zero Fallacy event. Of course the ST can fix it, the question is, can he fix it well while the rest of the setting looks somewhat the same? And the answer is, simply, no. Or at least, not easily, and most people won't want to put in that level of effort. The ST can certainly throw in a gigantic overt Lunar kingdom into, say, the Hundred Kingdoms, where 50 Lunars rule, like, states of a confederation evoking the Holy Roman Empire. The question then becomes &quot;why hasn't the Realm attacked it, because this place is openly run by Anathema&quot; and &quot;given 50 Lunars working together, what changes to the political landscape of the world that differentiate from the setting baseline have been made.&quot; If the answer to the second question is &quot;none,&quot; then the Lunars are worthless paper tigers; if the answer is &quot;a lot!&quot; then some of those events have to be detailed, whether it's Lunars basically taking over Nexus and in a cold war with Lookshy and have taken Thorns as a protectorate after 30 out of the 50 Lunars stopped the Mask of Winters in his tracks, at the cost of 20 of them which has caused some successorship issues in the Holy Lunar Empire's component states. But then the question still remains what the other 250 of them are doing and/or have done...<br /> <br /> We know what the DBs did. We know what Alchemicals did in Autochthonia. We know what the Sidereals did (and there are only 100 of them). We know what the Solars did a long time ago, kind of, but they've been out of the picture for so long that it doesn't really matter what the 10 or whatever of them that weren't in the Jade Prison did: mostly get killed, hunted, and killed again. Perhaps we know or can guess what they did because their themes are much more sturdy and established frameworks. With Lunars we have a group of 300 myth-heroes, some of whom are over 2000 years old, and really nothing of note published to show for their lives, and themes that were an antisocial mess in 1e and mayo-on-white-bread in 2e. When the authors can't decide where a splat should be in the world, potential players don't know what to expect from playing that splat, what a default story might be like, what to expect and what is reasonable to reach for. What does that tell a person who is initially interested in the splat?<br /> <br /> Basically you can add a big thing in a vacuum without thinking of larger setting consequences, but if you don't, it looks very tacked on and sloppy. If you go through a ton of setting consequences you may be making more woe for yourself than you intended starting out, and the players may have more trouble recognizing the setting and will have to be brought up to speed or whatever.<br /> <br /> Also it's a problem when so much attention (and word count) is paid to the elder Lunars in the setting (who are about as far away from the PC spectrum as possible) rather than the Lunars who <i>actually might be playable as PCs</i> like Strength-of-Many and Heysha Black-Asp. The other &quot;established&quot; splats (by that I mean &quot;splats with living elders&quot;) don't have this problem: despite Chejop, Sidereals somehow don't have this problem with their NPCs since the young ones get some attention and are interesting (Black Ice Shadow in particular maybe); ditto with DBs. But for some reason everybody just wants to write about fucking Lilith being sulky as an owl for 2000 years as if that's interesting, <i>christ</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210348#post210348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's less about canonicity than demonstrating plausibility. Outside of falling into the classic blunder that all Exalted run societies seem to run into, Dzibilchan worked. It created a society of Terrestrial Beastmen, who did not betray Makar to the Realm and were loyal to their Kingdom. Of course, that society lived in an brutal apartheid, treating non-beastmen as livestock and probably wouldn't be an approach most PCs would want to take.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even that this is an approach most PCs want to take. It's that &quot;brutal apartheid and/or rape pens&quot; is the shtick of like <i>3 existing canon Lunar elders</i>, and now of Dzibilchan too. That shtick is worn out, if it was ever in to begin with.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210437#post210437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile the same people saying it want to oppress the hell out of Lunars. Lunars are, in the terms of this forum, rarely even considered &quot;Exalts&quot; or valid in terms of the protections afforded such entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that is bullshit. If anything Lunars are disrespected because every other Exalt, <i>even the fucking splat invented for 2e</i>, has a more relevant role and &quot;splat goal&quot; in the world-as-described than Lunars do. I haven't seen the ridiculous hyperbole you have gotten to with &quot;they're not even Exalts.&quot; Most people actually say that about DBs because of the nature of their Exaltation (that's bullshit too).<br /> <br /> But as was said, the cure for a narrative problem is not to steal the thunder of others to make yourself look cool. That looks cheap, but it's easy, so that is what has happened. The better (and much harder) question is saying &quot;what themes should this splat have, and what general narratives should it focus on, and what cool examples can we hold up to players as things they can do can we write, based on the themes and the general milieu?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-27-2014, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:31:52-07:00","id":210476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't seen the ridiculous hyperbole you have gotten to with &quot;they're not even Exalts.&quot; Most people actually say that about DBs because of the nature of their Exaltation (that's bullshit too). </div> </div> </div>I haven't heard anyone say anything like this outside of a few IC posts from Sach in the old forum.<br /> <br /> And of course, some of the insane shit from LordLytek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:40:56-07:00","id":210484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not even that this is an approach most PCs want to take. It's that &quot;brutal apartheid and/or rape pens&quot; is the shtick of like <i>3 existing canon Lunar elders</i>, and now of Dzibilchan too. That shtick is worn out, if it was ever in to begin with. </div> </div> </div>And the only Lunar society that <i>doesn't</i> have either of those is more hated than the other three put together. Because of reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:11:46-07:00","id":210494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210451#post210451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing. Sure, we can assume the Lunars have done some epic ambiguous things things. <i>But we have no examples of what</i>. We have nothing to point to and say: &quot;that's what a Lunar can do after 700 years, or after 2000 years.&quot; We have no author who cared enough to lobby something interesting into publication. Lunars as a splat are ridiculously focused on the distant past rather than the present that is the default setting of the game. But despite their obsessive focus on the past, they have nothing to show for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so we don't know what the majority of Lunars have been doing for the past 800 years. That sucks. But because of that, we assume they've not been doing anything? Sorry, but why? How does that make any sense?<br /> <br /> As an ST, I've always just assumed that Lunars have been doing a variety of things in Creation. Raising personal Haltas, fending off armageddons, fighting the star-chosen in a secret war for Creation, building empires beyond the Wyld, whatever. The one thing I would never assume is that they've not been doing anything, because <i>that makes no sense.</i> They're all epic heroes. How could they not have been doing anything? Why would I make such an assumption? Isn't it better to simply say I don't know what most of them have been doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-27-2014, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:03:53-07:00","id":210560,"title":"","content":"what have the Lunars been doing for the last 2000 years???<br /> why, breeding their own army of BD, thats what","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T16:57:01-07:00","id":210646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210476#post210476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't heard anyone say anything like this outside of a few IC posts from Sach in the old forum.<br /> <br /> And of course, some of the insane shit from LordLytek.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Saying x,y, and z can't happen to DB's or Solars or anyone - then saying Lunars die and have done nothing for hundreds of years is the same as saying they are not Exalts and lack any of the prestige and protection of creditability afforded by it.<br /> <br /> What people say about the Lunars would be the same as saying that the Lunars *DO* build come big ass kingdom and the DB's *do nothing*. It's insane that people don't see that - that Lunars are not afforded the same basic *Heroic Status* as the other splats. In so, they are not treated like Exalts. That's my point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:54:31-07:00","id":210671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210494#post210494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so we don't know what the majority of Lunars have been doing for the past 800 years. That sucks. But because of that, we assume they've not been doing anything? Sorry, but why? How does that make any sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the authors had thought of anything good for them, I like to hope that one of them would have written about it. Instead we have nations retconned to be Lunar society-building projects because they &quot;just seem like a kinda Lunar thing to do&quot; rather than have that notion of society design be a baseline splat assumption. Instead it's tacked on at the end as if to say &quot;see, they've been doing something! Or at least 6 of them have!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210494#post210494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an ST, I've always just assumed that Lunars have been doing a variety of things in Creation. Raising personal Haltas, fending off armageddons, fighting the star-chosen in a secret war for Creation, building empires beyond the Wyld, whatever. The one thing I would never assume is that they've not been doing anything, because <i>that makes no sense.</i> They're all epic heroes. How could they not have been doing anything? Why would I make such an assumption? Isn't it better to simply say I don't know what most of them have been doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude it's fucking great that <i>you</i>, as an ST, <i>assume </i>Lunars have been doing things in Creation. The problem is that <i>nobody has actually written about many of them doing anything of note</i>, unless you count retconning &quot;oh these civilizations were actually Lunar projects.&quot; Which I don't, since those elements of the setting existed in the same form before someone said &quot;yeah let's just say a Lunar did that.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is, <i>your assumptions don't matter to the line as a whole.</i> What matters to the line is good portrayals in accessible, published material. And you want to say &quot;sure the Lunars had several Halta-like places with DB beastmen running around.&quot; Let's say this gets picked up and is now a core piece of canon that a writer wants to build something off of. There's things that need to be worked through if that statement becomes canon, the largest being &quot;how does that change history, if at all?&quot; The obvious questions to ask are (1) where is that society now; (2) what happened to it if it's gone; (3) how did it affect the setting in any term of time while it existed; (4) how did the relevant Great Powers at the time the society was formed and grew to power relate to or deal with this place. You can't just say &quot;oh Lunars made a Holy Roman Empire in the Hundred Kingdoms&quot; and leave it at that in the setting we have, because it leaves too many questions unanswered. You can;t just insert giant things into the setting without context; not answering those questions basically means you made assumptions in a white room without considering anything outside the bubble of Lunar Holy Roman Empire, and that itself creates setting consistency issues. Working through those questions shows that the setting has to be tweaked a little, or else all the cool shit Lunars might have done was so far away from the game's main theater that it effectively is irrelevant fluff. Yes, if all that shit happens in the borders of Creation, no matter how cool it is...if it doesn't interact with the rest of the setting, at least its immediate neighbors in some ways...it's not relevant, because it doesn't plug in and try to connect to the world.<br /> <br /> There has yet to be a nation or thing whose base design concept stemmed from &quot;Lunars did this&quot; until the teasers for the Caul in 3e came out. The Lunar NPCs are whiny, uninspiring, and pathetic. Most of the Lunar NPCs that get word count are elders, making them even more unrelatable to the basic player looking for inspiration for a chargen character. Hell most of them just sit around for decades or more just plotting and/or moping. How is that inspiring compared to the NPCs of other splats who are being active instead of sitting in passive stasis? Your assumptions aside, there's nothing about Lunars that makes a player think &quot;this concept should be a Lunar and not something else&quot; unless that concept really revolves around shapeshifting. Because, outside of shapeshifting, Lunars have no theme and nobody has tried to give them a unique theme instead of pulling themes from other splats. Which isn't good for <i>either</i> splat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210646#post210646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying x,y, and z can't happen to DB's or Solars or anyone - then saying Lunars die and have done nothing for hundreds of years is the same as saying they are not Exalts and lack any of the prestige and protection of creditability afforded by it.<br /> <br /> What people say about the Lunars would be the same as saying that the Lunars *DO* build come big ass kingdom and the DB's *do nothing*. It's insane that people don't see that - that Lunars are not afforded the same basic *Heroic Status* as the other splats. In so, they are not treated like Exalts. That's my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see people making that point at all. I see people saying &quot;please, please give Lunars a theme, but also do it without either mirroring the themes of another splat (Silver Solars), or making them so antithetical to other conceits of the setting that playing them is borderline impossible (1e) or without stepping on the toes of another splat (the notion that Lunars might be better at breeding DBs than DBs are).&quot; How is that not a valid request?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 07-27-2014, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T18:04:43-07:00","id":210683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210671#post210671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude it's fucking great that <i>you</i>, as an ST, <i>assume </i>Lunars have been doing things in Creation. The problem is that <i>nobody has actually written about many of them doing anything of note</i>, unless you count retconning &quot;oh these civilizations were actually Lunar projects.&quot; Which I don't, since those elements of the setting existed in the same form before someone said &quot;yeah let's just say a Lunar did that.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a minute. You don't count Halta, the Haslanti, the Delzahn, etc., as Lunars doing anything, because they weren't written as being involved in those things originally, in another Edition, over ten years ago?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean;n210671The thing is, [I</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">your assumptions don't matter to the line as a whole.[/I] What matters to the line is good portrayals in accessible, published material. And you want to say &quot;sure the Lunars had several Halta-like places with DB beastmen running around.&quot; Let's say this gets picked up and is now a core piece of canon that a writer wants to build something off of. There's things that need to be worked through if that statement becomes canon, the largest being &quot;how does that change history, if at all?&quot; The obvious questions to ask are (1) where is that society now; (2) what happened to it if it's gone; (3) how did it affect the setting in any term of time while it existed; (4) how did the relevant Great Powers at the time the society was formed and grew to power relate to or deal with this place. You can't just say &quot;oh Lunars made a Holy Roman Empire in the Hundred Kingdoms&quot; and leave it at that in the setting we have, because it leaves too many questions unanswered. You can;t just insert giant things into the setting without context; not answering those questions basically means you made assumptions in a white room without considering anything outside the bubble of Lunar Holy Roman Empire, and that itself creates setting consistency issues. Working through those questions shows that the setting has to be tweaked a little, or else all the cool shit Lunars might have done was so far away from the game's main theater that it effectively is irrelevant fluff. Yes, if all that shit happens in the borders of Creation, no matter how cool it is...if it doesn't interact with the rest of the setting, at least its immediate neighbors in some ways...it's not relevant, because it doesn't plug in and try to connect to the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2nd Edition books make it very clear that Halta, the Haslanti, the Delzahn, etc., are not the only examples in Creation of societies made by Lunars. They might be the only ones written about, but Creation is supposed to be full of them. That's canon.<br /> <br /> And how has it affected Creation? Well, I imagine that's largely why the Realm (and its patron, the Bureau of Destiny) hasn't succeeded in conquering it, for one thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-27-2014, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T20:35:30-07:00","id":210796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210683#post210683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait a minute. You don't count Halta, the Haslanti, the Delzahn, etc., as Lunars doing anything, because they weren't written as being involved in those things originally, in another Edition, over ten years ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that substantial amounts of 2e just involved filling in open areas left over from 1e, it's far from unreasonable to take this tack. Also, the attempts to &quot;salvage&quot; Lunars by making them hidden puppet masters started in 1e with Kingdom of Halta. It didn't help then, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 2nd Edition books make it very clear that Halta, the Haslanti, the Delzahn, etc., are not the only examples in Creation of societies made by Lunars. They might be the only ones written about, but Creation is supposed to be full of them. That's canon.<br /> <br /> And how has it affected Creation? Well, I imagine that's largely why the Realm (and its patron, the Bureau of Destiny) hasn't succeeded in conquering it, for one thing. </div> </div> </div>2e presented a Keystone Cops version of the Realm. Scavenger Sons laid out that places completely free of its influence, aside from most of the River Province, were the exception to the rule. That's why EX3 is doing a photo-negative version of that volume,in the Realm book that's on the schedule. Else, people, writers included, might be lulled into thinking that the Realm isn't a giant, dangerous empire that still sits astride the world. 2e was generally too busy obsessing over Deathlord dooms and then over the Reclamation. This prevented the Realm from being taken seriously, which devalued the &quot;we're holding on by our fingernails&quot; situation that the Lunars were in because of the Shogunate and then the Realm. It was like 1e's &quot;we don't need the Solars! We can do everything they can!&quot; screed, only worse.<br /> <br /> Compounded with the lacksadaisical approach to critter stat blocks that robbed a lot of forms of potential usefulness or impact, 2e smacked the Lunars around, robbed them, and left them out in the cold with that damned Wyld Keyword and what would be interesting Charms that only worked within the bounds of claimed territory. It said, &quot;Your shtick sucks. Let's try something else that, honestly, we know won't work out. Just look at how much better the Solars are at it than you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T01:39:56-07:00","id":210971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210683#post210683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait a minute. You don't count Halta, the Haslanti, the Delzahn, etc., as Lunars doing anything, because they weren't written as being involved in those things originally, in another Edition, over ten years ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the Edition where Lunars <i>had</i> to be Barbarians or risk losing their Exaltation, if memory serves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T04:41:01-07:00","id":211048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210971#post210971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in the Edition where Lunars <i>had</i> to be Barbarians or risk losing their Exaltation, if memory serves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually presented as merely an in-character myth.<br /> <br /> You absolutely could and would start losing Charms or other supernatural traits if you let yourself &quot;grow soft&quot; like some weak city-dweller, however. There were rule suggestions for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T04:44:16-07:00","id":211049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211048#post211048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was actually presented as merely an in-character myth.<br /> <br /> You absolutely could and would start losing Charms or other supernatural traits if you let yourself &quot;grow soft&quot; like some weak city-dweller, however. There were rule suggestions for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why First Age manses are full of deathtraps. The Lunars built them that way so they wouldn't turn weak and complacent while living there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T04:55:58-07:00","id":211067,"title":"","content":"Oh, incidentally, while I don't really agree with the premise of it that this thread is predicated on, I'm not entirely averse to Lunars having some manner of freaky breeding powers; if they're the Hydra, I don't see much reason why they can't be a bit of Echidna as well. Still wouldn't really work with Dragon Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T07:36:39-07:00","id":211198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211048#post211048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was actually presented as merely an in-character myth.<br /> <br /> You absolutely could and would start losing Charms or other supernatural traits if you let yourself &quot;grow soft&quot; like some weak city-dweller, however. There were rule suggestions for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was presented as an in-character myth. No, there weren't rules suggestions for it in any practical way. It's a vague hack on the last paragraph of page 248, applying chiefly to Lunars living in cities that works by storyteller arbitration, not a system as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T08:37:56-07:00","id":211251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=210683#post210683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2nd Edition books make it very clear that Halta, the Haslanti, the Delzahn, etc., are not the only examples in Creation of societies made by Lunars. They might be the only ones written about, but Creation is supposed to be full of them. That's canon.<br /> <br /> And how has it affected Creation? Well, I imagine that's largely why the Realm (and its patron, the Bureau of Destiny) hasn't succeeded in conquering it, for one thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The portrayal of Creation is not consistent with the idea of 300 Haslanti Leagues crowding out the Realm. That's about the First weakness of the whole Thousand Streams River concept.<br /> <br /> The second weakness is that, despite what Manual: Lunars asserted, the portrayal of Halta, Haslanti and Chiaroscuro aren't really consistent with the idea that there are Lunars running them either; the Lunars were a fairly significant casualty of the general mandate of changing or adding as little to the game as possible across Editions, so you wound up with places that had never been written with the assumption that they were products of some secret Lunar social engineering product looking exactly the same even after they were supposed to be products of some secret Lunar social engineering product.<br /> <br /> That actually wraps around to the first problem, where the setting looks exactly the same between Editions, despite the Second one asserting that they've added in this major game changer. And you can't just say &quot;all the social engineering is happening off screen waiting for you to detail it&quot;, because none of the places that <i>are</i> detailed in the setting are acting as though there are Lunar social engineering projects going on around them, despite how such a thing should be dramatically changing depictions between Editions. Neither the Dragon Blooded Manual nor the Sidereals Manual nor the Blessed Isle book had anything to say on the policies the Scarlet Dynasty nor the Bronze Faction were taking to deal with this thing, that should be near the very top of lists of concerns for those bodies.<br /> <br /> I suppose one could take the cue from Manual: Lunars that the social engineering project was <i>so</i> secretive (and had a tailor made ultimate goal besides) that the Lunars and their influence practically disappear inside a setting portrayal that never assumed the presence of Lunars, but at that point it kind of feels like the invisible dragon who's totally permeable to flour kind of story, which is to say one seems to be trying really hard to convince me of the existence of something one already lacks conviction of. Also, kind of excising anything that might be cool about the presence of an invisible dragon.<br /> <br /> Third Edition looks like it's going to properly reverse this; where the Caul and similar dominions actually are a matter of concern for the Realm and the Sidereals, referenced in their policies. Still, even if the world is big and open enough that among the things you can put into the unmarked spaces are Lunar dominions, the Caul probably forms the high standard for what they can be like; you can't credibly have a place operating on a similar level that isn't being hammered by the enemies of the Silver Pact, or otherwise being inexplicably ignored for Lunars to act with impunity, just because the books never spell out that such a place can't exist.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, such Lunar dominions will help get the dog, the eagle and the snake off the back of places where they don't really belong; let Chiaroscuro be for the Delzhan*, and the Lunars can have other places.<br /> <br /> * I actually am still a bit attached to the idea of Tammuz being focused on Chiaroscuro, just because it's the crown jewel of the South, and a lot of his politics in the Silver Pact concern securing his ultimate entitlement to it. To this purpose, I envision Tammuz feeling that when the revolution comes, most of the Delzhan will be the first up against the wall; they're currently useful for keeping the Realm out of the city, but Tammuz doesn't care for the airs they're adopting just because they managed to take control of the city in a time of major strife and forge a stable and prosperous society out of it. He wants it, and will tolerate it having no other masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T08:48:44-07:00","id":211283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211251#post211251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second weakness is that, despite what Manual: Lunars asserted, the portrayal of Halta, Haslanti and Chiaroscuro aren't really consistent with the idea that there are Lunars running them either; the Lunars were a fairly significant casualty of the general mandate of changing or adding as little to the game as possible across Editions, so you wound up with places that had never been written with the assumption that they were products of some secret Lunar social engineering product looking exactly the same even after they were supposed to be products of some secret Lunar social engineering product.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've set games in the Haslanti League before. I love the Haslanti. They're a tough, hardy, quarrelsome, violent, yet peculiarly democratic and libertarian people. They revere Lunars as embodiments of the traditional Haslanti virtues - chiefly ingenuity, cunning and aggression. They are survivors, descended from survivors, those who learned to prosper in an unforgiving wilderness when Tzatli fell to the ground. They're a supremely pragmatic people, canny opportunists, who worship a pantheon of animal gods and whose religion is based on shamanism and dreams. They're, IMO, very image of what you'd expect a society shaped by Lunars to look like.<br /> <br /> And the Haltans? Oh my god, could you even imagine a more Lunar society?<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211251#post211251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Edition looks like it's going to properly reverse this; where the Caul and similar dominions actually are a matter of concern for the Realm and the Sidereals, referenced in their policies. Still, even if the world is big and open enough that among the things you can put into the unmarked spaces are Lunar dominions, the Caul probably forms the high standard for what they can be like; you can't credibly have a place operating on a similar level that isn't being hammered by the enemies of the Silver Pact, or otherwise being inexplicably ignored for Lunars to act with impunity, just because the books never spell out that such a place can't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't pin my hopes on Third Edition if I were you. It's all well and good when all we have to go on is teasers and promises; you can keep everyone hopeful with those. But I kind of doubt that people who complain so continuously and forcefully about First Edition and Second Edition are going to find themselves suddenly satisfied with Third Edition rolls around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-28-2014, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:26:30-07:00","id":211317,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, back to Outcastes for a bit. There are a few things going on with Outcastes. One is that, yes, there's typically an assumption that they have really poor breeding, partially because this is the connective tissue between what breeding is supposed to mean for Terrestrials and the usual background portrayed for Outcastes, and partially because it's kind of necessary for maintaining consistency in how the setting doesn't look like it would if more Outcaste Dragon Blooded were able to maintain good bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I mean, forget about Lunars, or even the Realm for a moment; if more Outcastes were able to build up Exalted numbers from their own descendents, <i>they'd be doing it for themselves</i>; for their own power and position. Whatever one might think is the big Lunar advantage for locating and uniting them across distances of hundreds of miles, I don't think it's so unsurmountable an obstacle that no Outcastes ever encounter one another without it. And yet, by and large, such encounters do not seem to widely produce new miniature dynasties of Exalted; if they did, the setting would look significantly different. Never mind dozens of Haslanti Leagues, there has to be a reason that several hundred miniature Scarlet Dynasties aren't crowding the Realm off the map.<br /> <br /> If we assume, as things like the preview of the Wyld Hunt imply, that even in places where the grip of the Realm is weaker, the Immaculate dogma of Dragon Blooded spiritual superiority is a pretty far-reaching concept, that would seem to be the thing that most Terrestrials would be more inclined to turn their own families to; not serving the interests of a Lunar, no matter how polite and respectful the Lunar is. Hell, association with a Lunar probably makes their prospects actively terrible, considering that alliance with the Anathema is the one, singular thing upon which the Realm will never budge in its conditions for satrapies, and general diplomatic relations. They'll tolerate failure to pay your taxes in full before they will the idea that you're doing stuff with a Lunar.<br /> <br /> That actually, that's probably worth putting ahead of the idea that the Realm has stronger incentives to recruit Dragon Blooded than Lunars do; like, it's one thing to offer them opportunities and riches, people can accept or reject that as suits them, many people in Creation will dislike the Realm such that they won't accept offers. But throwing in your lot with Lunars will lead to the Realm actively making war on and trying to destroy you, and that's a whole 'nother thing besides. If a Lunar's going to try and recruit some Outcastes, they'll need to make an offer that greatly outweighs what you're sacrificing to become an active target of the Realm.<br /> <br /> Still, one way or another, some Outcastes are likely to end up with Lunars; they're a pretty diverse, but fairly mercenary lot. But if we're going for the idea that a Lunar wants to take these Outcastes and breed a force sufficient to challenge the Realm with them... let's just assume that Outcaste breeding is ever good enough to manage this on a reasonable time scale, does the Realm just... not notice this? Is bringing up a sizable number of Dragon Blooded, especially in service to an agenda based on opposing the most powerful nation in the world, an easy thing to hide? Even if we assume that the Lunar stays around to guard the children, is the Realm not up to overwhelming a priority threat who has to stay in one place? Or is the Lunar continuously on the move to stay ahead of the legions and the Wyld Hunt, and hoping that these are that extremely durable kind of human baby? How do you get away with something like this long enough to pull it off?<br /> <br /> I don't even know what &quot;breeding Charms&quot; Lunars are supposed to bring to the mix to make any kind of difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:35:18-07:00","id":211323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211317#post211317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we assume, as things like the preview of the Wyld Hunt imply, that even in places where the grip of the Realm is weaker, the Immaculate dogma of Dragon Blooded spiritual superiority is a pretty far-reaching concept, that would seem to be the thing that most Terrestrials would be more inclined to turn their own families to; not serving the interests of a Lunar, no matter how polite and respectful the Lunar is. Hell, association with a Lunar probably makes their prospects actively terrible, considering that alliance with the Anathema is the one, singular thing upon which the Realm will never budge in its conditions for satrapies, and general diplomatic relations. They'll tolerate failure to pay your taxes in full before they will the idea that you're doing stuff with a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why would you assume that? That's not true in 2nd Edition, in which Lunars are practically worshipped in places like Haslantiland. And I don't expect it's going to be true in Third Edition either. Immaculate propaganda doesn't carry much weight once you get further into the Threshold than the Inner Sea. Even other Dragon-Blooded states, like Lookshy, spit on Immaculate missionaries and curse the Realm and its dogma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211317#post211317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even know what &quot;breeding Charms&quot; Lunars are supposed to bring to the mix to make any kind of difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar breeding charms are charms like Tiger and Seahorse Dynasty, or Fish and Fowl Gestation, which allows you to assign traits to your offspring based on shapes in your Heart's Blood Library. So you can give your offspring fur, or claws, or a magical third eye, or flame wings, or a body made of thunder, if you so desire.and if you have a shape with the appropriate mutations. There's no charm to explicitly give them dragons' blood, but it wouldn't be much of a stretch at all to create one, since the Terrestrial Exaltation is physiological like anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-28-2014, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:42:26-07:00","id":211329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211283#post211283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've set games in the Haslanti League before. I love the Haslanti. They're a tough, hardy, quarrelsome, violent, yet peculiarly democratic and libertarian people. They revere Lunars as embodiments of the traditional Haslanti virtues - chiefly ingenuity, cunning and aggression. They are survivors, descended from survivors, those who learned to prosper in an unforgiving wilderness when Tzatli fell to the ground. They're a supremely pragmatic people, canny opportunists, who worship a pantheon of animal gods and whose religion is based on shamanism and dreams. They're, IMO, very image of what you'd expect a society shaped by Lunars to look like.<br /> <br /> And the Haltans? Oh my god, could you even imagine a more Lunar society?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say &quot;they don't look like societies that actually have Lunars running them&quot;, I am not talking about a society that has some vaguely connected abstract qualities. Like, I don't see many Lunars as endeavoring to run societies to look like big composite versions of themselves anyway, nor any other Exalted for that matter (with the exception of Alchemicals, and that has more to do with the fact that they literally turn into the environments in which those societies live). Certainly, I think much more of the idea that Exalts come from cultures, rather than the other way around; if you install a Lunar as ruler of Nexus, they're going to have to manage Nexus as it is, not turn it into survivalist Nexus or whatever.<br /> <br /> No, what I mean is that the nations don't seem to be following any policies that seem as though they would be useful to the agendas of Lunars, except insofar as the Manual portrayed that agenda as &quot;make lots of societies in which Lunars have no role whatsoever&quot;. Or even just societies that feel the slightest bit like there's any mechanism or result of Lunars telling people what to do. It's like trying to sell me on the idea that Emperor Norton was actually ruling the United States, or even San Francisco, you can't just point vaguely at the idea that they've got a few adjectives in common. Hell, at least Emperor Norton issued a currency that certain businesses would actually redeem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't pin my hopes on Third Edition if I were you. It's all well and good when all we have to go on is teasers and promises; you can keep everyone hopeful with those. But I kind of doubt that people who complain so continuously and forcefully about First Edition and Second Edition are going to find themselves suddenly satisfied with Third Edition rolls around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pin my hopes on Third Edition because of when I've speculated about where it seems to be going, based on comments of the desires and attitudes of the writers going back several years, going to places that I actually want for it, and when I independently ruminate on things that I think will be in the game and would be good for the game, and then get told by the developer that my thinking's on the right track. I believe the term &quot;unusually keen insight&quot; was used.<br /> <br /> Oh, but I'm sorry, I'm... not supposed to allude to the idea that I think I understand things, am I?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:49:23-07:00","id":211371,"title":"","content":"I don't see how hiding from the Realm is particularly hard, they're centered on the blessed isle and most of their attention is turned inward. Don't you just have to stay out of the way off in the woods somewhere? Hell there's enough woods to do something like that on the Blessed Isle itself! Lunars are crazy good at hiding, even hiding other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:50:12-07:00","id":211372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211329#post211329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pin my hopes on Third Edition because of when I've speculated about where it seems to be going, based on comments of the desires and attitudes of the writers going back several years, going to places that I actually want for it, and when I independently ruminate on things that I think will be in the game and would be good for the game, and then get told by the developer that my thinking's on the right track. I believe the term &quot;unusually keen insight&quot; was used.<br /> <br /> Oh, but I'm sorry, I'm... not supposed to allude to the idea that I think I understand things, am I?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been told I'm not allowed to continue asking about your experience or familiarity with the game, since you've made it clear you're unwilling to answer. So please respect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-28-2014, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T10:40:01-07:00","id":211418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211371#post211371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how hiding from the Realm is particularly hard, they're centered on the blessed isle and most of their attention is turned inward. Don't you just have to stay out of the way off in the woods somewhere? Hell there's enough woods to do something like that on the Blessed Isle itself! Lunars are crazy good at hiding, even hiding other people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much and its about time the Realm got its soldiers out to build Mnemon Hadrian's Wall. Not going to happen, power too scattered over the great Houses, in canon the Realm is just gonna tear itself apart and Lunars can do whatever. <br /> <br /> Even before the Empress poofed - its difficult to march an army 3000 miles through unknown lands, going off rumors, to attack something you know not its capabilities/exact location/allies and so on. Reading 1st Ed. it sounds like they only hunted down Lunars when they made themselves a thorn in the Realms side. Otherwise, left alone. Same with Beastmen like the Snakes that Walk as Men. People harp on 1st Ed. but it reads better than 2E Echo Chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T11:50:30-07:00","id":211511,"title":"","content":"DBs are also notoriously awful at fighting guerrilla wars, especially against celestial exalted. They're good at what they're supposed to be good at, marching a giant army of DB lead troops into a place, but if you can't line up on a field and slug it out they become much much less effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T12:20:20-07:00","id":211550,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's not really the Dragon-Bloods Lunars need to worry about, it's the Sidereals. The Wyld Hunt is guided by Sidereal astrology, and sometimes supported by Sidereal assassins. But the latter can't happen very often, or else there'd hardly be any experienced Lunars or Sidereals alive after 1500 years. Mostly they just fight proxy wars and rarely meet each other face to face.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, Lunars and Sidereals don't like to kill each other in person because the stakes are too high to be worth the risk, and because each ultimately recognizes that Creation needs the other. Hence why Lunars haven't attempted to kick the Sidereals out of Heaven over the past 1500 years, because Sidereals, being bound to the Loom, require access to Heaven in order to serve, whereas Lunars don't. And also because having most of the star-chosen in one place makes it easier to spy on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T12:35:53-07:00","id":211560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211550#post211550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's not really the Dragon-Bloods Lunars need to worry about, it's the Sidereals. The Wyld Hunt is guided by Sidereal astrology, and sometimes supported by Sidereal assassins. But the latter can't happen very often, or else there'd hardly be any experienced Lunars or Sidereals alive after 1500 years. Mostly they just fight proxy wars and rarely meet each other face to face.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, Lunars and Sidereals don't like to kill each other in person because the stakes are too high to be worth the risk, and because each ultimately recognizes that Creation needs the other. Hence why Lunars haven't attempted to kick the Sidereals out of Heaven over the past 1500 years, because Sidereals, being bound to the Loom, require access to Heaven in order to serve, whereas Lunars don't. And also because having most of the star-chosen in one place makes it easier to spy on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why the Lunars haven't tried to kick them out of heaven is first and foremost because they absolutely are not capable of doing this at the moment. Hence the shadow war where the Lunars dismantle First Age devices and infrastructure to deny it to the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals, bit by bit. If they tried to do more than that, they would swiftly bite off more than they can chew. So they kill Sidereals one by one in the field instead, as the number one cause of Lunar mortality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T12:40:18-07:00","id":211563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211560#post211560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why the Lunars haven't tried to kick them out of heaven is first and foremost because they absolutely are not capable of doing this at the moment. Hence the shadow war where the Lunars dismantle First Age devices and infrastructure to deny it to the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals, bit by bit. If they tried to do more than that, they would swiftly bite off more than they can chew. So they kill Sidereals one by one in the field instead, as the number one cause of Lunar mortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about my headcanon for the current edition, the current setting. The anti-infrastructure stuff is supposedly what we'll see in the <i>next</i> edition and in a different version of the setting.<br /> <br /> But yes, even in 2nd edition, I've always assumed Sidereals are the #1 cause of mortality for Lunars, and vice-versa. Even if happens only rarely, they live practically forever until they're killed by something, and what is more likely to be the cause of that death than each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-28-2014, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T12:59:16-07:00","id":211573,"title":"","content":"I got that the other way around. The new edition's details have Lunars being the #1 cause of Sidereal mortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T13:06:31-07:00","id":211581,"title":"","content":"One of the big problems is that the Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion did more to wreck the Realm than 300 Lunars did over 2000 years. That's the actions of like 2 Deathlords - and lazy indirect action at that. Hang around a well, wee just throw that out there. Invite some Fay in (wtf) and sit back and laugh.<br /> <br /> Two sit on their ass Deathlords struck such an insane blow to the Realm while Lunars could not even scratch it (at least by comparison). So it really just overshadows anything Lunars could have done or stories that could have been told in the fight of Lunars against the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-28-2014, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T13:07:10-07:00","id":211583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211573#post211573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got that the other way around. The new edition's details have Lunars being the #1 cause of Sidereal mortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the idea for the next edition (which I've always taken as the idea for 2nd edition) is that the leading cause of death for Lunars is &quot;killed by Dragon-Bloods while Sidereals watch and laugh&quot;, and that the leading cause of death for Sidereals is &quot;eaten by Lunar&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/m...p?title=Exalts</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:25:11-07:00","id":211661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211581#post211581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big problems is that the Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion did more to wreck the Realm than 300 Lunars did over 2000 years. That's the actions of like 2 Deathlords - and lazy indirect action at that. Hang around a well, wee just throw that out there. Invite some Fay in (wtf) and sit back and laugh.<br /> <br /> Two sit on their ass Deathlords struck such an insane blow to the Realm while Lunars could not even scratch it (at least by comparison). So it really just overshadows anything Lunars could have done or stories that could have been told in the fight of Lunars against the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Realm didn't exist then. It was a fractious, chaotic Shogunate that had even more Dragon-Blooded and First Age magic. The Realm came into existence only after 90% of everything that was alive - Lunars included - died and the fae swept in, only to be destroyed when the future Scarlet Empress activated the Sword of Creation. In fact, you could say that the Deathlords inadvertently helped to create the Realm and the threat that it poses to the world by using the Contagion and inviting in the Fair Folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T14:42:49-07:00","id":211672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211581#post211581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big problems is that the Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion did more to wreck the Realm than 300 Lunars did over 2000 years. That's the actions of like 2 Deathlords - and lazy indirect action at that. Hang around a well, wee just throw that out there. Invite some Fay in (wtf) and sit back and laugh.<br /> <br /> Two sit on their ass Deathlords struck such an insane blow to the Realm while Lunars could not even scratch it (at least by comparison). So it really just overshadows anything Lunars could have done or stories that could have been told in the fight of Lunars against the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>A furnace is a 100% reliable way to destroy cancer, but that doesn't mean that doctors are chumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:26:28-07:00","id":211716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211672#post211672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A furnace is a 100% reliable way to destroy cancer, but that doesn't mean that doctors are chumps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunars are not trying to take over the Realm or preserve anything. We've been told that they are trying to rock everything back to the stone age. I hardly see how Lunars have been doctors in this example.<br /> <br /> More so, the Contagion is a disease. Lunars have more claim to a other worldly (World Walkers) and living disease (Deathlords banned from such tools) than some Deathlord. Either that's some Lunar Deathlord mojo or I can shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-28-2014, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:38:31-07:00","id":211728,"title":"","content":"Holden once painted a picture of the Great Contagion that gave me the impression that the Shogunate was only vulnerable because of significant loss of infrastructure and resources over a long term. The source of such losses is being... reattributed. The Deathlords didn't do more, they piggybacked on the work somebody else had been doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:50:03-07:00","id":211757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211728#post211728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden once painted a picture of the Great Contagion that gave me the impression that the Shogunate was only vulnerable because of significant loss of infrastructure and resources over a long term. The source of such losses is being... reattributed. The Deathlords didn't do more, they piggybacked on the work somebody else had been doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this time we're not going to have Lunars whose efforts were ineffectual, but Lunars whose efforts led indirectly to the Great Contagion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:53:29-07:00","id":211763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211716#post211716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lunars are not trying to take over the Realm or preserve anything. We've been told that they are trying to rock everything back to the stone age. I hardly see how Lunars have been doctors in this example.<br /> <br /> More so, the Contagion is a disease. Lunars have more claim to a other worldly (World Walkers) and living disease (Deathlords banned from such tools) than some Deathlord. Either that's some Lunar Deathlord mojo or I can shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what's more important than being World-Walkers? Shapeshifting into beasts. You know what comes before disease? Shapeshifting into beasts. You know what 2e doesn't do well? Shapeshifting into beasts.<br /> <br /> Again, as far as 2e goes for Lunars, reference Obi-Wan at the end of Revenge of the Sith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:57:56-07:00","id":211765,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue Notes\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208760#post208760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No difference in respect to the Moonsilver Doomtrain's meaning. Doing another's bidding without ever knowing, over hundreds of years, just dancing to those strings...still sidelines Dragonbloods and their victories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, that is the exact opposite of my stance.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals never trivialized the Terrestrial Exalted. Never made them irrelevant. They manipulated the Dragon-Blooded and used them for their own ends, but that doesn't mean the Dragon-Blooded have done exactly what the Sidereals wanted.<br /> <br /> At present, I lack exact examples of what the Dragon-Blooded host as a whole have done that the Sidereals would rather they not. I could point to the Scarlet Empress, but the Imperial Manse makes her an outlier.<br /> <br /> Ah. I could instead point to the utter inability of the Sidereals to forestall the civil war resulting from the Empress's disappearance. The Sidereals can manipulate the Terrestrials, and perhaps even get a specific person on the throne, but their control is not nearly great enough to keep the Realm from dissolving into chaos and destruction. The fear and greed and hate of the Ten Thousand Dragons will not be denied by the One Hundred Stars.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two wrongs does not make a right, just frustrates me that everything else does just this<sup>[1]</sup> to Lunars. That even the players oppress them. I remember not so long ago when the Doomtrain carried the banner of Lunars high. I want to see that fire again, passions burning, mighty billows of smoke painting the horizon *sigh* truly we are in an Age of Sorrows. </div> </div> </div>Feh. More like we're past the Primordial War, and the Tornado Wolf is a relic of the raw and distant past.<br /> <br /> For now, Sunder the Gold waits and bides his energies.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:13:38-07:00","id":211828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211757#post211757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this time we're not going to have Lunars whose efforts were ineffectual, but Lunars whose efforts led indirectly to the Great Contagion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I don't find either particularly appealing.<br /> <br /> I don't really see a reason for the Lunars to want to push everything back to the stone age aside from &quot;being stuck in the stone age is a stereotypical barbarian thing&quot;. Given the Lunars are the only one of the Celestial Exalted to have been allied with the Solars during the Usurpation, I would think it would make much more sense for them to want to preserve Solar artifacts than to destroy them. It's easy to establish the capability of Lunars to destroy, they can turn into giant monsters. What I want is more of an emphasis on what Lunars have successfully created than what they've brought down, and why the remaining alliance of Exalted is diminished for their absence<br /> <br /> The Age of Sorrows should not be the way it is purely or even primarily because the Solars are gone and took their super-special magic with them, it should be the way it is because the decision the Sidereals made to destroy the Solars drove the other Exalted apart. If the Lunars were working together with the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded, Creation should have been much more livable without the Solars than it is. Right now the Lunars don't successfully present themselves as offering anything that would have changed the shape of the Shogunate era for the better if they had chosen to ally with the Sidereals, beyond being trained attack dogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:21:52-07:00","id":211837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211828#post211828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I don't find either particularly appealing.<br /> <br /> I don't really see a reason for the Lunars to want to push everything back to the stone age aside from &quot;being stuck in the stone age is a stereotypical barbarian thing&quot;. Given the Lunars are the only one of the Celestial Exalted to have been allied with the Solars during the Usurpation, I would think it would make much more sense for them to want to preserve Solar artifacts than to destroy them. It's easy to establish the capability of Lunars to destroy, they can turn into giant monsters. What I want is more of an emphasis on what Lunars have successfully created than what they've brought down, and why the remaining alliance of Exalted is diminished for their absence<br /> <br /> The Age of Sorrows should not be the way it is purely or even primarily because the Solars are gone and took their super-special magic with them, it should be the way it is because the decision the Sidereals made to destroy the Solars drove the other Exalted apart. If the Lunars were working together with the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded, Creation should have been much more livable without the Solars than it is. Right now the Lunars don't successfully present themselves as offering anything that would have changed the shape of the Shogunate era for the better if they had chosen to ally with the Sidereals, beyond being trained attack dogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asymmetrical warfare demanded more pragmatism than &quot;let's gather and preserve Solar relics&quot;. And this is what allows the Lunars to survive. They didn't have the luxury of sitting on massive repositories of First Age relics like ComStar from BattleTech. They can't really orchestrate Operation Holy Shroud in any manner other than slow, constant erosion of infrastructure and its fruits. They don't need them anywhere near as much as the others do, anyway, so they might kill two birds with one stone and use up some of these, though after they're done, they won't bring it back with them, because that would be long, involved, and likely result in a Sword of Creation smiting. They ruin it, so that it won't be used against them. And because Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals are keen to perform patch jobs by cannibalizing other First Age works, the destruction of the object has to be near-total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T17:35:58-07:00","id":211853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211828#post211828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I don't find either particularly appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite an understatement.<br /> <br /> The thought that in Third Edition, Lunars' anti-Shogunate efforts will have accidentally contributed to the Great Contagion... makes me a little sick in my mouth, actually. I'd rather they were written as ineffectual than as unwitting stooges of the Deathlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-28-2014, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:25:25-07:00","id":211889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211853#post211853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's quite an understatement.<br /> <br /> The thought that in Third Edition, Lunars' anti-Shogunate efforts will have accidentally contributed to the Great Contagion... makes me a little sick in my mouth, actually. I'd rather they were written as ineffectual than as unwitting stooges of the Deathlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the idea is that all three remaining Exalted, were dancing in the Deathlords palm.<br /> The infighting, destruction of civilization, the loss of First Age medicine and defenses cannot be blamed by one single faction, as the Sidereals, Lunars and Dragonblooded are all culpable of it.<br /> <br /> And then the Crusade and Contagion hit. Everything went to hell and for once, in a very long goddamn time, the Exalted Host stopped fighting each other and fought off a common threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T18:46:24-07:00","id":211902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211716#post211716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are not trying to take over the Realm or preserve anything. We've been told that they are trying to rock everything back to the stone age. I hardly see how Lunars have been doctors in this example.</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples you cited that showed up the Lunars were things that were designed to destroy the entire world, and almost did. Lunars really, really do not want the world destroyed. That's where they live!<br /> <br /> The Realm is the centre of the world, and its best-defended redoubt. That means that it's likely to be the least affected and the last to fall to any threat of a global scale, which creates a real risk that if you use such a threat against it, you'll end up hurting everybody else way more than the Realm, thus leaving them in an even stronger position. Note that this is roughly what actually happened with the Contagion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211716#post211716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More so, the Contagion is a disease. Lunars have more claim to a other worldly (World Walkers) and living disease (Deathlords banned from such tools) than some Deathlord. Either that's some Lunar Deathlord mojo or I can shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are...are you saying that Lunars have stronger associations with plague than the Deathlords? Extrapolating from this logic: zombies should not decompose at all, because decomposition is caused by <i>living creatures </i>and is the circle of life and all that shit. And those giant, horse-sized maggots that live in Juggernaut's wounds? Those are babies! It's the miracle of creation!<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, on the subject of the Well, this reminds me of an issue I had with your original post. You're acting like the Contagion was just this lazy half-assed thing that the Dowager stumbled upon while killing time. I don't really think anything in either 1e <i>or</i> 2e bears that out, does it? Drawing something from the well is generally portrayed like inventing something -- it's arduously difficult and you don't know if what you're attempting will ever succeed when you start. The Dowager's work with the Well was like the Manhattan Project -- the fact that we can't <i>understand</i> the nature of what she was doing does not mean that it wasn't hard work or a legendary accomplishment on her part. It's logical to assume it was, and that seems to be the way it's presented in the books, so presuming otherwise comes off like having an agenda. If hauling bespoke apocalypses out of the Well was easy, she'd be doing that all the time like some kind of Power Rangers villain, in addition to her other more serious plans, just because it's easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 07-28-2014, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T20:56:25-07:00","id":212022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211902#post211902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The examples you cited that showed up the Lunars were things that were designed to destroy the entire world, and almost did. Lunars really, really do not want the world destroyed. That's where they live!<br /> <br /> Are...are you saying that Lunars have stronger associations with plague than the Deathlords? Extrapolating from this logic: zombies should not decompose at all, because decomposition is caused by <i>living creatures </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well you sure do twist worlds and argue in a very disingenuous manner.<br /> <br /> 1) It's the same difference. Lunars Exalt from humans. They come from Lookshy, Gem, the Lap, and Whitewall. If they could just as easily walk a Realm legion into a trap (maybe they make a nation with 2-3 Lunars as a honey pot, do some Wyld questing and set up some perception Lunars with communication magic to create a surveillance net and then have 30 Lunars and their armies in the wings) take all their shit. Just rocking stuff to the stone age is no fun. No one want to play that or be that. Lunars can rock the Realm stuff down but they have Elders that helped build up the Age of Wonders, have Lunars with those skill sets, have the ability to train new generations in last technology and magic. I find it ridiculous that they would not build anything themselves. Why have a dam when you can just go be a beaver for a year and build one - then if the Realm rolls in the wood rots and you leave them nothing AWESOME *yawn*. If the Realm an army strong enough 3000 miles to take on a Lunar/Lunars - the Silver Pact comes to their aid for a rofl stomp or they send word to other Silver Pact members on the other side of Creation to cause problems while the army is away. Harry supply lines for 3000 miles. Every single attack on the Lunars would be like attacking Russia in Winter.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, Lunars have stronger association with plague. Making zombies is animating dead flesh. The decomposers are not part of the dead body, they are living organisms, and are outside of the deathly purview. Thus, they can only slow decomposition by killing the decomposers - which is difficult as they thrive on death - so no, the Deathlords struggle to even slow the decomposers. If a Lunar wanted, it could develop a charm that focuses on decomposers and cause issue for the Deathlord in a serious way. I don't get how this logic could be this flawed on your part Gayo...<br /> <br /> 3) &quot;horse-sized maggots that live in Juggernaut's wounds&quot; - could be a lot of different things, they've been kept pretty open to interpretation since 1st Ed. Are they simply part of the dead behemoth? Are they plasmids of something that once preyed on dead behemoths or a lost species? Are they a dream of the Labyrinth? Certainly though, they are not meant to be living maggots but rather a representative and symbolic. Most likely they are part of Juggernaut, as he constantly replenishes and they constantly consume - this tells me that they are intrinsically linked to one another and may infact be part of the same being. Perhaps if one were to kill all of the maggots, which are not so invulnerable as Juggernaut, it would simply die? Who can say but the ST put in that situation. <br /> <a href=\"http://battlerealms.wikia.com/wiki/Infested_One\" target=\"_blank\">http://battlerealms.wikia.com/wiki/Infested_One</a><br /> &quot;He lives in a state of constant suffering, yet identifies, perhaps, with his maggots: from their brutal, swarming life energy, he siphons the strength to continuously regenerate his body.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T23:10:53-07:00","id":212160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212022#post212022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you sure do twist worlds and argue in a very disingenuous manner.<br /> <br /> 1) It's the same difference. Lunars Exalt from humans. They come from Lookshy, Gem, the Lap, and Whitewall. If they could just as easily walk a Realm legion into a trap (maybe they make a nation with 2-3 Lunars as a honey pot, do some Wyld questing and set up some perception Lunars with communication magic to create a surveillance net and then have 30 Lunars and their armies in the wings) take all their shit. Just rocking stuff to the stone age is no fun. No one want to play that or be that. Lunars can rock the Realm stuff down but they have Elders that helped build up the Age of Wonders, have Lunars with those skill sets, have the ability to train new generations in last technology and magic. I find it ridiculous that they would not build anything themselves. Why have a dam when you can just go be a beaver for a year and build one - then if the Realm rolls in the wood rots and you leave them nothing AWESOME *yawn*. If the Realm an army strong enough 3000 miles to take on a Lunar/Lunars - the Silver Pact comes to their aid for a rofl stomp or they send word to other Silver Pact members on the other side of Creation to cause problems while the army is away. Harry supply lines for 3000 miles. Every single attack on the Lunars would be like attacking Russia in Winter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second edition promised a lot on the Lunar front. Unfortunately, it was writing checks that its other setting assumptions couldn't cash. Why can't Lunars make more lost First Age wonders? Because those wonders all relied on Solar Charms to furnish the necessary materials. Why don't they just curb stomp the Realm? Because they haven't got the power to do so. And, incidentally, attacking Russia in the winter is nothing to a group of people who are empowered by raw elemental Essence. So it's cold out? Not after a Dragon Vortex hits, it isn't. The first law of jungle warfare also applies to any other rough terrain. Lunars do not have the odds in their favor. Two other types of Exalted rigged them that way on purpose. So no campaigns, no straightforward battles, here. Just baiting the Realm to expose magic that it can't restore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T00:22:22-07:00","id":212214,"title":"","content":"It's worth mentioning that the Realm was much more effective when the Empress was around, for various reasons. Most notably she had control of the Realm Defence Grid, dooming any invasion of the Blessed Isle to failure. The Wyld Hunt was also considerably stronger during the Empress' reign, and could mobilize quickly to any point in the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T00:31:47-07:00","id":212215,"title":"","content":"In canon she has only fired the grid once and it fucked her own shit up. I'd think Lunars, with the best perception magic in the game, and Wyld questing - would be able to figure out that the Grid is a bluff. If they did go to the Realm, they infiltrate and make them nuke their own cities - not like it's strategic. <br /> <br /> @ &quot;attacking Russia in the winter is nothing to a group of people who are empowered by raw elemental Essence&quot; - was metaphorical, not literally an issue of cold obviously, but that you're going into enemy territory and the land itself is something you must overcome.<br /> <br /> @ &quot;Because those wonders all relied on Solar Charms to furnish the necessary materials.&quot; - Wyld, all the resources you could ever want. Just power quest.<br /> <br /> @ &quot;So no campaigns, no straightforward battles, here&quot; - Pretty lame considering Lookshy gets to be in that boat but the entire Lunar host and all their armies can't compete with one freaking city in the Realms eyes. And the Realm actually wants the East more than any other direction but has allowed Lookshy to bar that for crazy amounts of time.<br /> <br /> @ &quot;Just baiting the Realm to expose magic that it can't restore.&quot; - after nearly 2000 years...that gets tired.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T02:36:17-07:00","id":212261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211828#post211828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I want is more of an emphasis on what Lunars have successfully created</div> </div> </div> </div>An island where fate works by their designs rather than those of Heaven, for one.<br /> <br /> They might also revive the whole songline concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">why the remaining alliance of Exalted is diminished for their absence</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know how in several fictions, there's that one really vicious and brutal character, and on occasions after they do something particularly vicious and brutal their allies quip &quot;glad he's on our side&quot;?<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial and Sidereal Exalted can't say that anymore. Even the returning Solars might not be able to.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a bad thing to build the Lunars around the idea that one of their biggest contributions to the Realm was turning the skills they've been using on the other Exalted throughout the Second Age on the enemies of the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Age of Sorrows should not be the way it is purely or even primarily because the Solars are gone and took their super-special magic with them, it should be the way it is because the decision the Sidereals made to destroy the Solars drove the other Exalted apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Exalted hadn't all turned on each other, then they wouldn't have squandered and ruined the legacy of the Solars. It couldn't have lasted forever, but it wouldn't have been falling apart in a series of disasters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Lunars were working together with the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded, Creation should have been much more livable without the Solars than it is. Right now the Lunars don't successfully present themselves as offering anything that would have changed the shape of the Shogunate era for the better if they had chosen to ally with the Sidereals, beyond being trained attack dogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can make anything sound weak and undignified if you frame it in terms of that kind of hyperbole. There was a time when people were all for Lunar Exalted being some kind of Special Ops Exalted, but now that somehow amounts to being trained attack dogs, and is thus unworthy.<br /> <br /> Hmm, now I'm thinking in terms of the State Alchemists, who are also derided as dogs of the military for their function as living artillery. I guess those guys are pretty lame as well, no wonder that manga was such a failure.<br /> <br /> I don't even believe in it being the limits of what the Lunars are capable of in the next Edition, not with how the Caul seems to be following up on First Edition lines about their creation of songlines or major contribution to the Salinan Working (cue people whinging about how the Lunars only get to do something if working with a Solar, and I bash my head against a wall for the fact that this complaint was about what Lunars cooperate with other Exalted for), even if in their current milieu they're directing such talents ultimately towards destroying the Realm (which doesn't even need to be a hateful act, since by the Realm by its nature sucks everything into its orbit, so any desire for independence is a desire to destroy the Realm).<br /> <br /> My point is, the Lunars absolutely offer themselves as something, you just don't like what they do. What do you actually think they should have been able to contribute?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=211853#post211853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thought that in Third Edition, Lunars' anti-Shogunate efforts will have accidentally contributed to the Great Contagion... makes me a little sick in my mouth, actually. I'd rather they were written as ineffectual than as unwitting stooges of the Deathlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that the fact that the Deathlords inadvertently freed the Solar Essences mean that they're unwitting stooges of the Solars?<br /> <br /> Oh, can I put in some Lunar Elders who look at the Age of Sorrows and think &quot;this is a pretty big win for us&quot; and turn the Deathlords into unwitting stooges of the Lunars as well?<br /> <br /> Or maybe even frame them as unwitting stooges of the Scarlet Empress, since she never would have become the most powerful person in Creation if not for their actions.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I started this off just thinking to mock the idea that ever doing anything that indirectly benefits somebody else is a ridiculous position, but now I think it would be more fun to design elaborate charts tracking who's an unwitting stooge to whom, until absolutely everybody in Creation looks like a comical moron.<br /> <br /> No, no that still seems as though it would deride the very idea, since it's a logic that <i>can</i> only lead to the conclusion that everybody in Creation is a comical moron.<br /> <br /> But no, yeah people complain about the idea that the Deathlords were doing more harm to the Shogunate than the Lunars did, and then somebody gets sickened by the idea that the Deathlords only worked because of the harm the Shogunate had taken from the Lunars. People want the idea to be that Creation is harmed by the disunity and conflict of the Exalted, and then complain over the idea that it actually happened. I wonder if there's a way to wind up with this evocative Dying Earth-style setting in which the remaining Exalted actually were united and cooperative in which people won't complain about how their inability to keep it from becoming an evocative Dying Earth-style setting just undermines their credibility, but I don't particularly care to look for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T02:47:08-07:00","id":212266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212215#post212215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In canon she has only fired the grid once and it fucked her own shit up.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's direct reference to its use against the Seven Tigers and the Manosque rebellion, and indirect reference to its use on other occasions. One of the Aspect books has a fiction piece in which a Fair Folk army on the verge of reaching Paragon was almost certainly destroyed by the Realm's defences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ &quot;Because those wonders all relied on Solar Charms to furnish the necessary materials.&quot; - Wyld, all the resources you could ever want. Just power quest.</div> </div> </div> </div>If power questing undermines the premise of the setting, then it's not a good thing to be in the game.<br /> <br /> This is like saying that the Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick means we should have examples, lots of them, of cities and nations that were destroyed in a single strike by a Sidereal. I mean, maybe some people do want that, but I think the premise that the popular appeal of the setting as it is has been demonstrated to the degree that it doesn't need to be vastly overturned, so the issue in a new Edition is to remove elements that undermine the credibility of the setting, rather than revise the setting wholesale to treat it through the lens of every poorly worked mechanical addition.<br /> <br /> That was the logic they worked with for the Fair Folk errata, and it worked out pretty well. Actually, that's- that's a better comparison than the Oblivion Kick, isn't it? To want the setting to act as though there were ever raksha who could infinitely spawn and had crazy endlessly stacked mutations and have them overrun the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T04:22:23-07:00","id":212331,"title":"","content":"Maybe it does have lots of examples of destroyed cities, but nobody can remember any of them existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T04:33:05-07:00","id":212335,"title":"","content":"If we're going by Lunars Should Be Doing This Because Crunch Says So then power questing isn't even the worst of it (although it's a close second.)<br /> <br /> No, Lunars should be hanging out in the Wyld eating Raksha to max out their Graces and then forming a vast faerie army with undefined magical powers and flying airships using Raksha Charms.<br /> <br /> I guess the reason they don't do that is because <i>they aren't respected enough.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T06:03:08-07:00","id":212372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212261#post212261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I started this off just thinking to mock the idea that</div> </div> </div> </div>Here it comes! The part where you describe the idea of mine you posted this comment to mock! I sure hope it's an accurate description of what I said, not just another pointless strawman!<br /> <br /> Here goes. What was my idea, Levi?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212261#post212261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the idea that <b>ever</b> doing <b>anything</b> that indirectly benefits <b>some</b>body else</div> </div> </div> </div>Curse you, Isator Leviiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiii!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-30-2014, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T07:28:36-07:00","id":212456,"title":"","content":"Reducto ad absurdum is not a strawman. Deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T07:35:23-07:00","id":212472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212215#post212215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In canon she has only fired the grid once and it fucked her own shit up. I'd think Lunars, with the best perception magic in the game, and Wyld questing - would be able to figure out that the Grid is a bluff. If they did go to the Realm, they infiltrate and make them nuke their own cities - not like it's strategic.<br /> <br /> @ &quot;attacking Russia in the winter is nothing to a group of people who are empowered by raw elemental Essence&quot; - was metaphorical, not literally an issue of cold obviously, but that you're going into enemy territory and the land itself is something you must overcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded can resculpt massive areas of terrain on the fly. Whatever advantages which you had can be torn asunder in a matter of moments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> @ &quot;Because those wonders all relied on Solar Charms to furnish the necessary materials.&quot; - Wyld, all the resources you could ever want. Just power quest. </div> </div> </div>On no useful time scale, Also, treasure questing was perhaps the worst addition to the rules regarding the Wyld to the game. No one looked at it, no one seemed to have thought about the repercussions, it just found its way into CoCD: Wyld and created an unrealistic expectation of the setting. If we were still getting 2e errata, I'd expect that it and power questing would have been heavily revised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> @ &quot;So no campaigns, no straightforward battles, here&quot; - Pretty lame considering Lookshy gets to be in that boat but the entire Lunar host and all their armies can't compete with one freaking city in the Realms eyes. And the Realm actually wants the East more than any other direction but has allowed Lookshy to bar that for crazy amounts of time. </div> </div> </div>Lookshy has several thousand Dragon-Blooded and the same trove of ancient magic that the Realm does, including devices that emit The Sound That Kills. Thanks to the foresight of Nefvarin Gilshalos, they ended up in a much better position than the Lunars did, because they were a part of the massive system that inherited all of the Solar-built wonders and managed to get their hands on more than the other parts of the Shogunate. They continue to act as anti-Lunars, finding and storing more as they find it.<br /> <br /> Of course, Lookshy only complicates life for the Realm in the River Province. Lunars complicate its machinations all over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> @ &quot;Just baiting the Realm to expose magic that it can't restore.&quot; - after nearly 2000 years...that gets tired. </div> </div> </div>Again, if that's how you feel, then don't play a Lunar. If you're leaning on what 2e promised, you have a lot of expectations that we can only assume will go unfulfilled. Concentrate on a different shard setting, or just outright play a different type of character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T07:39:29-07:00","id":212477,"title":"","content":"It's not a reducto ad absurdum, because I didn't say that doing something that indirectly benefitted the Deathlords would make the Lunars unwitting stooges of the Deathlords. What I said was that I would rather they were written as ineffectual than they were written as unwitting stooges. The scenario described <b>could</b> make them seem like unwitting stooges, but it could also be written in a way as to avoid it, and we won't know which it is until the books are printed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T07:44:33-07:00","id":212479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212477#post212477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a reducto ad absurdum, because I didn't say that doing something that indirectly benefitted the Deathlords would make the Lunars unwitting stooges of the Deathlords. What I said was that I would rather they were written as ineffectual than they were written as unwitting stooges.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You see. I don't want to kill Lois, I just want her to be..dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T07:49:19-07:00","id":212481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212479#post212479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You see. I don't want to kill Lois, I just want her to be..dead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's actually a world of difference between those two things. Pretending someone who said one had said the other would be pretty unfair. I didn't go so far as to say that it sounded like the Lunars were being written as unwitting stooges, for a reason, because obviously I don't know. All I said was that it makes me a little sick to think about it. Even if I had gone that far, nothing I said indicated that my opinion was based on the premise,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212261#post212261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that <b>ever</b> doing <b>anything</b> that indirectly benefits <b>some</b>body else</div> </div> </div> </div>so it was not a reducto ad absurdum, or any logical criticism, it was just a strawman. And if I seem to be reacting out of proportion, please bear in mind that it's only after several months of replying to the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-29-2014, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T08:45:06-07:00","id":212508,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I wonder if the premise in the setting in which everybody jockeys over position until the sky falls down does unduly favour the Deathlords, if we assume a presentation where they ultimately want the sky to fall down.<br /> <br /> My instinct would be to generally revise the Deathlords such that they're more about wanting to stock up the Underworld that their own armies and societies might swell, but I'm still somewhat attached to the idea that they're kind of standing over the gates of the impending eschaton.<br /> <br /> Maybe they can be both; their conscious desire is to reign in the Underworld, but some of the necromantic warping they've undergone has given them an impulse towards the end of the world in the back of their minds, or a kind of Doom slowly tugging upon them. It's not really part of their motivations or their politics, but it might be influencing them a bit. Could be part of why the Abyssals are ultimately superior.<br /> <br /> That might include the idea that the Great Contagion would have been something beyond the scope of what they even wanted if it hadn't been countered. Maybe the invasion of the Fair Folk is part of that. Hmm, maybe that can even serve as the basis for reconciling those two images I have; the Deathlords want to turn the world into a graveyard, but are distantly frustrated by the idea that sufficient death in Creation might leave it vulnerable to the Wyld, creating an apocalypse on terms that don't really suit them (or the raksha or whatever else, for that matter).<br /> <br /> But yeah, this still all ultimately revolves around the conceit that the politics of <i>everybody</i> at the opening of the setting have the world on the path to ruin. It's their genre appropriate equivalent of peak oil. It's not confined to the Lunars, it... might be able to not benefit the Deathlords, and it's supposed to be the status quo that PCs are saving everybody from. Or gleefully going along with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T11:31:17-07:00","id":212637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212261#post212261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An island where fate works by their designs rather than those of Heaven, for one.<br /> <br /> They might also revive the whole songline concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Y'know how in several fictions, there's that one really vicious and brutal character, and on occasions after they do something particularly vicious and brutal their allies quip &quot;glad he's on our side&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Even the Hulk, who's probably the most iconic instance of such a character, also has the ability to help solve scientific problems as Bruce Banner. I dislike Lunars only contributing fighting power for the same reason I dislike Solars having a gun to the head of Creation by being the only people capable of shaping the Wyld, condemning Creation to a slow death by disintegration without them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Exalted hadn't all turned on each other, then they wouldn't have squandered and ruined the legacy of the Solars. It couldn't have lasted forever, but it wouldn't have been falling apart in a series of disasters. </div> </div> </div>The reason I want more than that is because I don't want it to just be about the legacy of the Solars. I prefer a vision of Creation in which, if the Sidereals had trusted the Lunars enough to approach them and managed to win them over, Creation would be diminished but not doomed, perhaps not possessing the grandeur of the First Age but still quite decent and not at risk of Wyld encroachment. A kind of silver age, if you will. Not only because the Solar equipment wouldn't have been destroyed, although that certainly helps, but because even without Solar equipment the combined efforts and works of the Lunars, Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded should be able to produce a functional Creation, though not as majestic or wondrous as with the Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can make anything sound weak and undignified if you frame it in terms of that kind of hyperbole. There was a time when people were all for Lunar Exalted being some kind of Special Ops Exalted, but now that somehow amounts to being trained attack dogs, and is thus unworthy. </div> </div> </div>If it helps your understanding, I am not one of the people who argued for Lunars as Special Ops Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point is, the Lunars absolutely offer themselves as something, you just don't like what they do. What do you actually think they should have been able to contribute? </div> </div> </div>Honestly this is the part where I start to fall flat, because Lunars don't have an obvious constructive thematic bent. But if we were to extrapolate from what themes they do have, and to go back to the original thread topic for a moment, I could get behind the concept that one of the functions of the Lunars in the First Age was to manage Terrestrial breeding. Not that the Dragonblooded aren't capable of breeding themselves, but that Luna's relationship with Gaia manifests in it being much easier to maintain or restore lost blood purity with the assistance of Lunars. Though this goes back to &quot;Lunars are only good for fighting and fucking&quot;, which is problematic. I'll have to think further on the matter.<br /> <br /> I do feel they should be able to Wyld Shape, though. Maybe not as well as Solars in terms of how Solars are able to produce fully-formed locations, objects and people out of it, but beyond Ritual of Lunar Stability Lunars should be able to at least produce raw, untamed terrain. MoEP: Lunars mentions how they learned something similar by copying the Fair Folk, but I'll admit I have not read much about the fae so I don't know what that translates to in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T11:45:33-07:00","id":212643,"title":"","content":"Regarding &quot;if... then&quot; statements about alternatives to the Usurpation:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wondermark.com/c/2014-07-18-1047regret.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:05:06-07:00","id":212651,"title":"","content":"Now which Division would be responsible for aphorisms: Journeys, Serenity, or Secrets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:10:42-07:00","id":212661,"title":"","content":"Journeys, because it's about the journey and not the destination. But if Journeys and Serenity die in a mysterious accident then it's Secrets because three can keep a secret if two of them are dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:13:27-07:00","id":212665,"title":"","content":"The difference with the Wyld Shaping should be this:<br /> <br /> Solars: They have the power to crush the Wyld down into raw energy and create new matter from that energy - dreaming up their own wonders from it.<br /> Lunars: Have a touch of the Wyld in them, Lunar draws the power of the Wyld and carries it to the Daystar that it might fly across Creation, the Lunars can take what the Wyld offers and give it permanence or subtly shift it. Hence, why Lunars should be able to get Graces but not Solars, they can only crush and reform - not capture and repurpose. In light of this, Lunars can either search the Wyld for something approximating what they need and it takes some time, but if they grab bag and then create stuff from what they find they are much faster than Solars at using the Wyld. Solars can just reach in and create whatever they want but it should be a time consuming and exhaustive process.<br /> <br /> Now in my perfect world:<br /> Sol burns away the Wyld and leaves nothing - Solars should only have holy keywords that destroy it and no further ties.<br /> Luna interacts with the Wyld so her chosen should be the arbiters and the diplomats to the Wyld - the scryers and seers. The Eclipse caste should never have been able to make oaths with the Wyld long term, in its infinite ever changing personas, and it should be a constant struggle for the Lunar host - keeping track of Fairfolk as they shift and become something new, making it a necessity to form new pact and oath.<br /> <br /> <br /> @&quot;Dragon-Blooded can re-sculpt massive areas of terrain on the fly. Whatever advantages which you had can be torn asunder in a matter of moments.&quot;<br /> <br /> And give away their position, leave themselves without cover, piss off the natives/elementals/gods, and get jumped by a hundred Lunars instead of three. The Realm can not afford losses or to be drawn into deathtraps as they chase honey pots. Many Dragonbloods are merchants, politicians and engineers. By canon pretty much every Lunar chews your face off (not a super fan of that - but there it is) and has combat ability through stealth, martial arms, or sorcerous might. Many DB's never serve in the Wyld hunt or the military and then still others only serve their House. So say of 10,000 we have 3k that can be sent abroad. If you sent 500 or less out, the Lunars can kill you. If you send 1000 the Lunars might team up with an army of Fairfolk or a Deathlord (supported by 1st Ed.) and crush you. Send more than that, the Lunars just wasted your time, they move far faster and attack your Satraps while a token force harries and flees. They sneak into the Realm and kill off politicians, teachers of sorcery, and artisans.<br /> <br /> Really, with Lunars being able to swim up Realm rivers as a salmon, fly inland as an insect...I have no idea how they don't just assassinate Dynasts constantly. You can't defense grid one lunar (I mean you could if you wanted to destroy a city with some of the last First Age tech. intigrated into it - maybe a manse or two you can't repair...if you even get the Empress to react that quickly. Then their is popular opinion to worry after - how with this affect her popularity). They are hard as shit to spot, track, detect. Young Dragonbloods on vacation, all dead. Regional governors in satraps, all dead. Dragonbloods stationed in the port cities of the Realm, all dead.<br /> <br /> If you want 3000 years of covert ops (not what I would want) the Lunars would kill you whenever you left the pack - you'd never be able to go out into the Threshold to enjoy the supplication of your Satraps. Lunars would be killing you left right and center. Dragonbloods have a look about them, are loud and proud, they can't hide from the Lunars. The invisible threat would rip them to shreds. Then, you'd be wishing the Lunars were off building nations and more concerned with their own business. Stories about young dragonbloods going to the City of the Steel Lotus to get their party on - whatever - dozen dead Dragonbloods right the hell there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 07-29-2014, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:26:33-07:00","id":212674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212665#post212665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, with Lunars being able to swim up Realm rivers as a salmon, fly inland as an insect...I have no idea how they don't just assassinate Dynasts constantly. You can't defense grid one lunar (I mean you could if you wanted to destroy a city with some of the last First Age tech. intigrated into it - maybe a manse or two you can't repair...if you even get the Empress to react that quickly. Then their is popular opinion to worry after - how with this affect her popularity). They are hard as shit to spot, track, detect. Young Dragonbloods on vacation, all dead. Regional governors in satraps, all dead. Dragonbloods stationed in the port cities of the Realm, all dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits. Spirits are everywhere in Creation. Swim up a Realm river and the luminescent river-god will be swimming invisibly beside you, from beneath every pebble on the riverbed a little god will peek up to look at you, the dryad of every tree you and shrub you fly over, the sprite of every breeze you catch in your wings, every cloud you pass through. Stop in a mortal village and get something to eat, the god of your rice bowl will smile at you, the god of your chopsticks will shiver under your fingers. Sleep in a bed at night and you'll be wrapped between a humble bed-god and a pliant blanket-god while the hospitable god of the inn watches over you. And after you leave and for years to come, the whole lot of them will be gossiping about that glorious Lunar prince who was just here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-29-2014, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:34:19-07:00","id":212678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212637#post212637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even the Hulk, who's probably the most iconic instance of such a character, also has the ability to help solve scientific problems as Bruce Banner. I dislike Lunars only contributing fighting power for the same reason I dislike Solars having a gun to the head of Creation by being the only people capable of shaping the Wyld, condemning Creation to a slow death by disintegration without them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't just contribute fighting power. You're simply so fixated on Solar contributions to non-fighting that you can't see non-Solar contributions to the same. They're not the same. Stop trying to have Lunars match Solar approaches. It won't work/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly this is the part where I start to fall flat, because Lunars don't have an obvious constructive thematic bent. </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do. They're super werewolves. They borrow heavily from WW's earlier contributions to the monsters in question and crank the power dials up. You've got shapeshifting monsters with a spiritual bent. That is going to inform an awful lot about how they work. Just look at the hacking Charm from the recent Ink Monkey Bones additions - it's a digital vision quest. Thankfully, there is no mention of the Wyld anywhere within it..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if we were to extrapolate from what themes they do have, and to go back to the original thread topic for a moment, I could get behind the concept that one of the functions of the Lunars in the First Age was to manage Terrestrial breeding. Not that the Dragonblooded aren't capable of breeding themselves, but that Luna's relationship with Gaia manifests in it being much easier to maintain or restore lost blood purity with the assistance of Lunars. Though this goes back to &quot;Lunars are only good for fighting and fucking&quot;, which is problematic. I'll have to think further on the matter. </div> </div> </div>It wasn't their job. It wasn't anybody's job. Some might take it upon themselves to influence it, but it wasn't a thing that an entire type of Exalted did Just Because.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do feel they should be able to Wyld Shape, though. Maybe not as well as Solars in terms of how Solars are able to produce fully-formed locations, objects and people out of it, but beyond Ritual of Lunar Stability Lunars should be able to at least produce raw, untamed terrain. MoEP: Lunars mentions how they learned something similar by copying the Fair Folk, but I'll admit I have not read much about the fae so I don't know what that translates to in practice. </div> </div> </div>Raw, untamed terrain is one of the things that the Solar Charm does... at low success levels. You really want all Lunar Charms to just be crappy versions of Solar Charms? That's not going to build much in the way of dignity for the splat, to just be second string versions of another character type all the time. The approach has to be re-considered from theory, and in the case of Wyld Shaping Technique, that's not really workable. The theory of it is &quot;make the substance of the Wyld into something formed&quot;, and that's pretty wide open to start. It doesn't brook many alternatives.<br /> <br /> As for learning from the fae, that's another relic of 1e copied over without question. &quot;Lunars can learn Fair Folk Charms&quot; is a persistent artifact of early development that just won't seem to die. But, since EX3 promises to grant Lunars in Creation, there's a good chance that it can be pushed off. No more dealings with raksha that somehow justify a close kinship with them, no more completely open Charm share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T12:46:44-07:00","id":212692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212022#post212022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you sure do twist worlds and argue in a very disingenuous manner.<br /> <br /> 1) It's the same difference. Lunars Exalt from humans. They come from Lookshy, Gem, the Lap, and Whitewall. If they could just as easily walk a Realm legion into a trap (maybe they make a nation with 2-3 Lunars as a honey pot, do some Wyld questing and set up some perception Lunars with communication magic to create a surveillance net and then have 30 Lunars and their armies in the wings) take all their shit. Just rocking stuff to the stone age is no fun. No one want to play that or be that. Lunars can rock the Realm stuff down but they have Elders that helped build up the Age of Wonders, have Lunars with those skill sets, have the ability to train new generations in last technology and magic. I find it ridiculous that they would not build anything themselves. Why have a dam when you can just go be a beaver for a year and build one - then if the Realm rolls in the wood rots and you leave them nothing AWESOME *yawn*. If the Realm an army strong enough 3000 miles to take on a Lunar/Lunars - the Silver Pact comes to their aid for a rofl stomp or they send word to other Silver Pact members on the other side of Creation to cause problems while the army is away. Harry supply lines for 3000 miles. Every single attack on the Lunars would be like attacking Russia in Winter.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, Lunars have stronger association with plague. Making zombies is animating dead flesh. The decomposers are not part of the dead body, they are living organisms, and are outside of the deathly purview. Thus, they can only slow decomposition by killing the decomposers - which is difficult as they thrive on death - so no, the Deathlords struggle to even slow the decomposers. If a Lunar wanted, it could develop a charm that focuses on decomposers and cause issue for the Deathlord in a serious way. I don't get how this logic could be this flawed on your part Gayo...<br /> <br /> 3) &quot;horse-sized maggots that live in Juggernaut's wounds&quot; - could be a lot of different things, they've been kept pretty open to interpretation since 1st Ed. Are they simply part of the dead behemoth? Are they plasmids of something that once preyed on dead behemoths or a lost species? Are they a dream of the Labyrinth? Certainly though, they are not meant to be living maggots but rather a representative and symbolic. Most likely they are part of Juggernaut, as he constantly replenishes and they constantly consume - this tells me that they are intrinsically linked to one another and may infact be part of the same being. Perhaps if one were to kill all of the maggots, which are not so invulnerable as Juggernaut, it would simply die? Who can say but the ST put in that situation.<br /> <a href=\"http://battlerealms.wikia.com/wiki/Infested_One\" target=\"_blank\">http://battlerealms.wikia.com/wiki/Infested_One</a><br /> &quot;He lives in a state of constant suffering, yet identifies, perhaps, with his maggots: from their brutal, swarming life energy, he siphons the strength to continuously regenerate his body.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You are all over the place here, dude. This is kind of stream-of-consciousness, but what I can glean from it is that you have an extremely unconventional and unsupported take on a lot of things and are very angry about it not being conventional and supported. You are probably going to have to deal with that one way or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T13:19:52-07:00","id":212717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212637#post212637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer a vision of Creation in which, if the Sidereals had trusted the Lunars enough to approach them and managed to win them over, Creation would be diminished but not doomed, perhaps not possessing the grandeur of the First Age but still quite decent and not at risk of Wyld encroachment. A kind of silver age, if you will. Not only because the Solar equipment wouldn't have been destroyed, although that certainly helps, but because even without Solar equipment the combined efforts and works of the Lunars, Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded should be able to produce a functional Creation, though not as majestic or wondrous as with the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this follows the premise that the main problem with Creation since the Usurpation was that all the Exalted started viciously fighting each other, but doesn't fully appreciate the reasoning the setting gives for why that kind of conflict happened.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's all well and good to say &quot;with live a diminished world&quot; (and certainly I feel as though the existence of societies in the Age of Sorrows in which people can still have happiness, prosperity and success validates the idea), but to imagine the circumstances of actually living through it...<br /> <br /> Consider my peak oil reference; consider how, while it's obvious that people can exist without the use of technologies reliant on petroleum products, it would be extremely unlikely that a sudden dropoff of such things wouldn't lead to significant disorder and death in societies precariously balanced around the assumption that such technologies will continue to exist. And even if they don't, even if some imposition of order or collective drive towards cooperation took hold, that still wouldn't be enough, not when you've got crops reliant on chemical fertilisers for their yields and combine harvesters for their collection, and vehicles for their transport, how many people are going to starve in a span of twenty or fifty years? Or pharmaceuticals for that matter.<br /> <br /> The idea that the world would have been more stable and secure if the Exalted host had not fallen apart in the wake of Usurping the Solars might be accurate, but I don't think it's particularly useful.<br /> <br /> Although even then, it's probably not accurate; as usual, I forget about the impact that the Great Curse is supposed to have on the Exalted as a whole, and that Holden has cited as necessary for beginning to understand the direction they're taking the Lunars in. Part of the premise that the return of the Solars might be the salvation of the world isn't just in their power and their predilection for righteousness and being disengaged from the politics that have built up over the Second Age, but in the fact that they've had centuries for the greater part of the Curse to have lost momentum.<br /> <br /> My point is, that the world is in a Time of Tumult doesn't really cast an aspersion on the quality of the Exalted, because it's built heavily on a foundation of major complex socio-economic factors, exacerbated by ancient dread magic. The world is bigger than them; if anything, that contributes to the capability for an individual human to have happiness and prosperity more than it does to how the world is basically falling apart.<br /> <br /> Although even with all of that in mind, I'm still just more personally compelled by the idea that Lunars without Solars to distract and restrain them aren't exactly the kind of people many folks want around in any case. Not so much because they're mindlessly destructive, maybe more because they're... intense, passionate, a little bit idiosyncratic...<br /> <br /> I don't know, I think I've reached my limit in trying to think in other terms, because in my own mind I'm just too attracted to the tone of the setting being one in which everybody strives and struggles amidst the ruin, the idea of how they might have avoided that holds little interest to me. I can't really care if the Bronze Age was unavoidable, because I love it so; Dragon Blooded decadence and intrigue, Sidereal frustration and exertion, a Lunar cackling gleefully as yet another fortress of the enemy burns down harmlessly around them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly this is the part where I start to fall flat, because Lunars don't have an obvious constructive thematic bent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though it would help if there were worthwhile nuances in the system to give a sense that part of the fun of construction is how you do it rather than what you produce. If there was some way to make the endeavour of constructing a thing while being in a creative berserker state come across through the mechanics... I mean, for me, I wouldn't even care if the product was unique, or even especially powerful, just so long as the journey felt like how a Lunar would exert themselves. Like a palace that looks as though the architect was on drugs.<br /> <br /> That and some of the stuff the developers have suggested, at putting together useful things while being off the grid.<br /> <br /> And maybe sometimes when they simply shear through the landscape. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could get behind the concept that one of the functions of the Lunars in the First Age was to manage Terrestrial breeding. Not that the Dragonblooded aren't capable of breeding themselves, but that Luna's relationship with Gaia manifests in it being much easier to maintain or restore lost blood purity with the assistance of Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from the other things I've said in this thread, I'm also still averse to the idea based on that time Lea pointed out the comparisons to creepy cult management stuff. And now that I come to think of it... the problematic implications of the idea of a Lunar holding the idea that a Dragon Blood who wants to boost their own power will need to have sex with them over their head...<br /> <br /> Now the idea that Lunars might have a few powers that kind of empower people who have worked or fought alongside them in a manner that represents a certain kind of spiritual affirmation... that sometimes the Terrestrial Exalted will have rode alongside a Lunar of the Wyld Hunt, and the experience had a certain enlightening quality that boosted their Essence expression in their bloodline... I don't know, if it's even not a Solar thing, it feels abstract enough to be Essence 6 or higher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel they should be able to Wyld Shape, though. Maybe not as well as Solars in terms of how Solars are able to produce fully-formed locations, objects and people out of it, but beyond Ritual of Lunar Stability Lunars should be able to at least produce raw, untamed terrain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder... if Lunars might be less suited to transforming the Wyld than they are to having certain ways to harness the Wyld to transform <i>themselves</i>. Or have a distinct capacity for it not to transform them; maybe even a sufficiently small pocket or tendril of the Wyld in Creation is something a Lunar might try to swallow up and contain safely in their body. Maybe they could even vomit it up again somewhere else.<br /> <br /> Actually, if nothing else, I now think a perfectly valid creative effort for a Lunar is to drain an obstructive lake by drinking it in one swallow. <br /> <br /> You've given me a bit to think about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T13:30:36-07:00","id":212721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Really, with Lunars being able to swim up Realm rivers as a salmon, fly inland as an insect...I have no idea how they don't just assassinate Dynasts constantly. You can't defense grid one lunar (I mean you could if you wanted to destroy a city with some of the last First Age tech. intigrated into it - maybe a manse or two you can't repair...if you even get the Empress to react that quickly. Then their is popular opinion to worry after - how with this affect her popularity). They are hard as shit to spot, track, detect. Young Dragonbloods on vacation, all dead. Regional governors in satraps, all dead. Dragonbloods stationed in the port cities of the Realm, all dead.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I imagine the combat system won't really support means of indiscriminately killing enemies from a position of stealth and surprise, and the setting has an idea that Dynasts and several other people are comparatively guarded, and a fish or insect both has a hard time murdering you rapidly, and not giving itself away when it initiates hostilities.<br /> <br /> I'm not actually averse to the idea that sometimes Lunars sneak around the Blessed Isle, and even manage to do some harm while they're there (although I feel it should be a kind of minor legend sort of thing, like Mance Rayder playing songs in Winterfell), but going a bit too far rapidly draws the worst kind of attention.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can only assume that the Wyld Hunt is not easily confounded by Lunars turning into really small animals. Also maybe that such forms can have disadvantages; like a bear probably won't be able to kill you as a salmon, not unless you're already fairly weakened, but the experience might be a bit inconvenient.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T13:41:07-07:00","id":212734,"title":"","content":"Dynasts are often surprisingly unprotected, actually. Because however safe and secure they would be if they stayed within their family manse-fortresses, or in their posts in the legions, Terrestrials, being Exalted, have a hard time doing that. Even those on active duty are disposed to take numerous vacations in order to seek adventure in dangerous places (Yes, that is totally official, it was written in the 2nd Edition core).<br /> <br /> I think a typical Lunar, if he wanted to, could go on a brief blitzkrieg along the coast of the Blessed Isle, maybe for up to a few days, if he was careful, before the Wyld Hunt became an immediate danger. But the star-chosen wouldn't take kindly to the intrusion and it probably wouldn't be worth the heavenly retribution it would incur. Unless the Lunar was immune to astrology (and there are charms for that, but they don't work all the time), I think the whole thing would end badly for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-29-2014, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T14:21:20-07:00","id":212809,"title":"","content":"I actually don't understand this at all either. A Lunar fly can really easily sneak into the tent of a Dynast soldier, snap his neck or slit his throat in his sleep and leave. Even if he's immediately discovered terrestrials really can't give chance, not to mention a small group of DBs isn't much of a match for a Full Moon anyway. That's even assuming a guarded tent, if you were out on a balcony trying to woo another Dynast by moonlight or out hunting in the woods or whatever you're basically Lunar fodder, even on the Isle.<br /> <br /> That's not even counting knacks that let Lunars look like a trusted servant or guard, or charms that let you retain some of your own impressive stats in other forms, ect. With the right charms a lunar wasp can kill a DB instantly, or at least close enough once the poison kicks in. Even without those upgrade knacks and charms though Lunars dominate terrestrials with hit and run tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T14:24:28-07:00","id":212812,"title":"","content":"I realize that you may not have intended it that way, o simian physician, but the image of a silver housefly sneaking up on an armored soldier and snapping his neck is so hilarious that I can no longer take the rest of your post seriously.<br /> <br /> Also judging by what the playtesters have said, going for an immediate kill is a pretty big risk in combat; it can work, obviously, but if you fail to put your opponent in the ground with that one attack, you'll have hemorrhaged all your momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-29-2014, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T14:24:41-07:00","id":212813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212734#post212734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dynasts are often surprisingly unprotected, actually. Because however safe and secure they would be if they stayed within their family manse-fortresses, or in their posts in the legions, Terrestrials, being Exalted, have a hard time doing that. Even those on active duty are disposed to take numerous vacations in order to seek adventure in dangerous places (Yes, that is totally official, it was written in the 2nd Edition core).<br /> <br /> I think a typical Lunar, if he wanted to, could go on a brief blitzkrieg along the coast of the Blessed Isle, maybe for up to a few days, if he was careful, before the Wyld Hunt became an immediate danger. But the star-chosen wouldn't take kindly to the intrusion and it probably wouldn't be worth the heavenly retribution it would incur. Unless the Lunar was immune to astrology (and there are charms for that, but they don't work all the time), I think the whole thing would end badly for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it'd be more an efficient use of time and effort to just find out the various seafaring Terrestrials travel plans in the west, leak them to Leviathan and watch the fireworks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T14:28:25-07:00","id":212818,"title":"","content":"Yes, a chargen Celestial assassin can kill every DB in the world bar an extreme minority that know martial arts capable of reflexive surprise anticipation. <br /> <br /> I think it would be best to chalk this up to being a failure of mechanical execution and not assume that everyone who fights the Realm is just stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T14:33:22-07:00","id":212822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212812#post212812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize that you may not have intended it that way, o simian physician, but the image of a silver housefly sneaking up on an armored soldier and snapping his neck is so hilarious that I can no longer take the rest of your post seriously.<br /> <br /> Also judging by what the playtesters have said, going for an immediate kill is a pretty big risk in combat; it can work, obviously, but if you fail to put your opponent in the ground with that one attack, you'll have hemorrhaged all your momentum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I never said it wasn't hilarious. You'll note no Lunar medicine style charms say they can't be preformed in monkey form. But the neck snap would require a knack, I was more thinking of turning into warform in by the bedside. Assuming no guards creepily watch the dynast in his sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T14:41:54-07:00","id":212832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212818#post212818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a chargen Celestial assassin can kill every DB in the world bar an extreme minority that know martial arts capable of reflexive surprise anticipation.<br /> <br /> I think it would be best to chalk this up to being a failure of mechanical execution and not assume that everyone who fights the Realm is just stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they know sorcery they might have dematerialized spirits watching out for them. or have other defenses. But yeah, I think your solution is best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-29-2014, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:02:29-07:00","id":212844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212818#post212818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a chargen Celestial assassin can kill every DB in the world bar an extreme minority that know martial arts capable of reflexive surprise anticipation. <br /> <br /> I think it would be best to chalk this up to being a failure of mechanical execution and not assume that everyone who fights the Realm is just stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for me it's not just surprise attack=dead. I'm actually okay with a giant burly bearman being able to coup de grace a sleeping dynastic fop. But actually getting there should be hard. Which for literally any Lunar it's just not. I'd also be perfectly fine with it if it was a special charm or combo or something, but it's something inherent to Lunars that they all have. I'd even be cool with that if the setting actually presented Dynasts as putting on a brave face while being secretly terrified that at any moment their guard might whip around and rip their throat out. <br /> <br /> I really want to know if they're going to bring this up, especially with that Realm city in the Caul. How the hell does that place keep it's DB population alive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:02:46-07:00","id":212847,"title":"","content":"I assume that, when it comes to those Dynasts who are adventuring around the Threshold and beyond, a lot survive based off of the basic math; there are lots of them and only a few Lunars, the odds of them running into each other are pretty low, and not all Lunars necessarily have the best means to uncover Dynast travel plans. And even if they do intersect, even adventuring Dynasts often travel with sizable entourages, including a protective detail. Even considering that, I'm all for the idea that the number of Dynasts who don't come back because they encountered Anathema is disturbing to the Realm, even if it's a minority of the overall.<br /> <br /> Even so, that hardly seems like where the story ends; I'd say a fair number of the time, investigators (often Found Eggs) are sent out to find where the last signs of the lost Dynast's movements are end, and a lot of the time they pick up the trail of the Lunar and call in the Wyld Hunt. I can imagine that there are Lunars who spend years dodging the Hunts sent for them, big prolonged campaigns as they all run a merry circuit through some of the more obscure corners of the world. On that note, I'd also say there are Lunars who pick up on lone Dynasts while they're in the middle of other, sensitive projects that can't afford to lose their attention or have heat brought down on them at the moment, and so make the calculated decision to let the Dynast go, unless they're worth the cost. <br /> <br /> Not to mention ones whose strategies against the Realm aren't exactly concerned with killing people in the first place, or who are at least ready to let their fellows take up that side of the campaign. I'd say there are times where a Lunar who sees a Dynast getting too close to something they don't want the Realm knowing about might head a few miles off, do something in an alternate form that catches the Dynast's attention, and redirecting them for a bit, before trailing off.<br /> <br /> And I'd say plenty of Dynasts while they're living on the Isle trust in the defences of their borders and interior, and the difficulties an aggressive Lunar would bring on themselves in the heart of their enemy's power, and the statistical unlikelihood based on the limited number of Lunars, that they can feel secure in their own homeland.<br /> <br /> I think these are conditions that allow for occasions where Dynasts might get killed by Lunars while still being plausible as a thing that is not endlessly happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:08:53-07:00","id":212850,"title":"","content":"Also, I can't help but feel but an insect buzzing around them is something a Dynast would find bothersome and distasteful in a manner that usually ends up with them trying to snatch it from their air with chopsticks and flick it away or crush it, or even just flare their anima at it. Like, it's not as if they're living in farms or abattoirs, where that's just a feature of the landscape; in my experience, people tend to take notice of buzzing insects. It at least seems a good opportunity to give them a check to notice the Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:11:44-07:00","id":212856,"title":"","content":"...<br /> <br /> &quot;This bug has hooves.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;huh, must be a wyld mutant&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;ew.&quot; *squish*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:15:18-07:00","id":212858,"title":"","content":"In the current game, the Wyld Hunt finds Lunars by astrology, spirits, charms and other magical means. When the dice are on their side, they know where and when a Lunar is going to appear <i>well ahead</i> of her actual arrival. When a Lunar Exaltation is going to happen somewhere in the Threshold, both the Wyld Hunt and the Silver Pact usually predict it with enough time to dispatch a party before the Exaltation itself actually happens.<br /> <br /> It's not just a case of Dragon-Bloods physically chasing Lunars around the threshold, following a trail of sightings and rumors. They know where a Lunar is going, often, before than the Lunar himself does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:23:02-07:00","id":212860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212858#post212858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the current game, the Wyld Hunt finds Lunars by astrology, spirits, charms and other magical means. When the dice are on their side, they know where and when a Lunar is going to appear <i>well ahead</i> of her actual arrival. When a Lunar Exaltation is going to happen somewhere in the Threshold, both the Wyld Hunt and the Silver Pact usually predict it with enough time to dispatch a party before the Exaltation itself actually happens.<br /> <br /> It's not just a case of Dragon-Bloods physically chasing Lunars around the threshold, following a trail of sightings and rumors. They know where a Lunar is going, often, before than the Lunar himself does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately for the astrologers, Lunars have both a Knack that lets them assume someone else's fate and a Charm that explicitly makes them undetectable by astrology, makes astrology attempts Obvious to them and <i>lets them track the astrologer.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:25:29-07:00","id":212861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212850#post212850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I can't help but feel but an insect buzzing around them is something a Dynast would find bothersome and distasteful in a manner that usually ends up with them trying to snatch it from their air with chopsticks and flick it away or crush it, or even just flare their anima at it. Like, it's not as if they're living in farms or abattoirs, where that's just a feature of the landscape; in my experience, people tend to take notice of buzzing insects. It at least seems a good opportunity to give them a check to notice the Tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well at that point you really have to choose your insect disguise wisely. Moths and Butterflies are a bit big, but much less likely to attract swatters or draw a second glance for tells, looking pretty damn weird already.<br /> <br /> Or fleas, which are too damned small to check for tells, can't really fly and itch like shit. On the upside you can also use this form to sacred hunt a DB, assuming you survive the first smack after biting it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:34:14-07:00","id":212872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212860#post212860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately for the astrologers, Lunars have both a Knack that lets them assume someone else's fate and a Charm that explicitly makes them undetectable by astrology, makes astrology attempts Obvious to them and <i>lets them track the astrologer.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>True, I mentioned the astrology-blocking charms a few comments ago. And on top of that, all Lunars are innately resistant to astrology (+1 difficulty), due to their slippery Wyld-tainted Exaltations. And there are other charms that grant Lunars immunity to Arcane Fate. But not all Lunars are equipped with the complete anti-Sidereal loadout, sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-29-2014, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T16:04:18-07:00","id":212892,"title":"","content":"I suppose being immune to things is kind of a Lunar theme. Immune to shaping effects, immune to fate, immune to damage. There are charms that make you immune to death while the essence is committed. I think the idea, in keeping with Luna, is throwing off attempts by anything external to yourself to define what you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T16:23:25-07:00","id":212907,"title":"","content":"Hmm, flat immunity, I wonder why <b>no</b> one ever tried to <b>sell</b> that idea before...<br /> <br /> Yeah, this feels like another thing I'd rather not see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T17:14:04-07:00","id":212946,"title":"","content":"I know the conversation has moved on, but this is my obligatory plea for people not to treat the &quot;odds of your child Exalting&quot; table as something that in any way reflects anything about the setting. If it were remotely accurate, the Realm would be hip-deep in Dragon-Blooded - that's what happens when you have a <i>hundred million people</i> with &gt;1% odds of their children Exalting.<br /> <br /> (That's not to say that there shouldn't be statistics for Exaltation rates, or that plans based around said statistics should be impossible, just that <i>these particular statistics</i> are laughably absurd.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T17:27:57-07:00","id":212974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212665#post212665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference with the Wyld Shaping should be this:<br /> <br /> Solars: They have the power to crush the Wyld down into raw energy and create new matter from that energy - dreaming up their own wonders from it.<br /> Lunars: Have a touch of the Wyld in them, Lunar draws the power of the Wyld and carries it to the Daystar that it might fly across Creation, the Lunars can take what the Wyld offers and give it permanence or subtly shift it. Hence, why Lunars should be able to get Graces but not Solars, they can only crush and reform - not capture and repurpose. In light of this, Lunars can either search the Wyld for something approximating what they need and it takes some time, but if they grab bag and then create stuff from what they find they are much faster than Solars at using the Wyld. Solars can just reach in and create whatever they want but it should be a time consuming and exhaustive process.<br /> <br /> Now in my perfect world:<br /> Sol burns away the Wyld and leaves nothing - Solars should only have holy keywords that destroy it and no further ties.<br /> Luna interacts with the Wyld so her chosen should be the arbiters and the diplomats to the Wyld - the scryers and seers. The Eclipse caste should never have been able to make oaths with the Wyld long term, in its infinite ever changing personas, and it should be a constant struggle for the Lunar host - keeping track of Fairfolk as they shift and become something new, making it a necessity to form new pact and oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you keep trying to bend at some parts of the setting that don't yield should clue you in to the viability of the material in MoEP: Lunars, or any attempt to keep pushing &quot;Solars are unnecessary&quot;. You don't set up Eclipses to be diplomats and then suddenly yank part of that back and say, &quot;But not to the Wyld!&quot; That's a terrible way to go. Terrible like the supposed Lunar connection to the Wyld, or the way that chimerae were handled in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T18:11:21-07:00","id":213003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just a case of Dragon-Bloods physically chasing Lunars around the threshold, following a trail of sightings and rumors. They know where a Lunar is going, often, before than the Lunar himself does.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I don't know; I feel it would be consistent with the portrayal of the Wyld Hunt that ran down Arvida of the Crescent Eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T18:30:05-07:00","id":213012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212946#post212946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the conversation has moved on, but this is my obligatory plea for people not to treat the &amp;quot;odds of your child Exalting&amp;quot; table as something that in any way reflects anything about the setting. If it were remotely accurate, the Realm would be hip-deep in Dragon-Blooded - that's what happens when you have a <i>hundred million people</i> with &gt;1% odds of their children Exalting.<br /> <br /> (That's not to say that there shouldn't be statistics for Exaltation rates, or that plans based around said statistics should be impossible, just that <i>these particular statistics</i> are laughably absurd.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree <i>so hard</i>. The numbers for Exaltation rate by Breeding and DB parentage were obviously not written with the intention of falling under obsessive scrutiny, and any model of Creation that tries to use them to justify its existence is going to have some coherency problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The same will occur in just about any attempt to model Creation under the assumption that the game's rules represent the physics of Creation, be it stunts, extras, poisons, falling, or Fair Folk Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T18:37:20-07:00","id":213017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213003#post213003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, I don't know; I feel it would be consistent with the portrayal of the Wyld Hunt that ran down Arvida of the Crescent Eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm sure they rely on such methods sometimes, but I'm equally sure they prefer to have reliable astrological foresight when possible, along with divination charms, spiritual spies and other tools.<br /> <br /> If the Wyld Hunt operated mainly by following sightings and rumors of Anathema from one mortal community to another, Lunars working together could basically toy with them as much as they wanted, flashing an anima to manufacture a sighting 500 miles away from where the Hunt should be, then flying to another area and repeating the process a few days later to lead them around in circles before finally abandoning them in the wilderness. In fact, the 2E Lunars book describes that as one example of tactics a pack uses when extracting a newly Exalted Lunar from territory where the Hunt is operating.<br /> <br /> If that were the limit of their ability, the Wyld Hunt would be a fairly pitiful thing, only a serious threat to dumb or inexperienced Lunars, which is not what I want. I like a Wyld Hunt that is (in better days anyway) competent and effective, something experienced Lunars have to worry about, so I prefer them to use every tool available in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-29-2014, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T21:34:35-07:00","id":213142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213012#post213012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same will occur in just about any attempt to model Creation under the assumption that the game's rules represent the physics of Creation, be it stunts, extras, poisons, falling, or Fair Folk Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but this is not a problem with &quot;use rules to model physics&quot; <i>per se</i>. (There may be problems with that approach - this just isn't one of 'em.) It's possible to write totally serviceable rules for determining the odds of children Exalting - I've taken stabs in that direction before. In fact, if you're going to write up a demographically-reasonable society, you probably <i>need</i> to figure out things like the relative frequency of Dragon-Blooded Exaltation for different parts of the population - and having done that, writing rules for it can be as easy as &quot;Roll your d10000; on a 1-5...&quot;<br /> <br /> If anything, that table demonstrates the problem of writing rules and <i>not</i> thinking about what they say about your world, and why it's a darned good idea that you make your map at least vaguely resemble your territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T22:05:27-07:00","id":213165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=212946#post212946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the conversation has moved on, but this is my obligatory plea for people not to treat the &quot;odds of your child Exalting&quot; table as something that in any way reflects anything about the setting. If it were remotely accurate, the Realm would be hip-deep in Dragon-Blooded - that's what happens when you have a <i>hundred million people</i> with &gt;1% odds of their children Exalting.<br /> <br /> (That's not to say that there shouldn't be statistics for Exaltation rates, or that plans based around said statistics should be impossible, just that <i>these particular statistics</i> are laughably absurd.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The odds I mentioned assumed the character was from one of the Great Houses of the Scarlet Dynasty. Someone whose siblings are all Exalted, parents are both Exalted, grandparents and great-grandparents Exalted. Lunars of less auspicious parentage, those not of the blood, would find the task more difficult, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T05:10:39-07:00","id":213425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213165#post213165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The odds I mentioned assumed the character was from one of the Great Houses of the Scarlet Dynasty. Someone whose siblings are all Exalted, parents are both Exalted, grandparents and great-grandparents Exalted. Lunars of less auspicious parentage, those not of the blood, would find the task more difficult, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still too high, though less so. Consider that there are, by the books, ~10,000 such Dragon-Blooded in the Realm; at a (pretty conservative) 3% reproduction rate, that's 300 kids per year, somewhere between 30 and 270 of whom would Exalt. Split the difference and call it 150.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well,&quot; you may say, &quot;that's not so bad, is it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Okay, now how many <i>un</i>Exalted members of the Great Houses are there? Are they, say, 1% of the population of the Blessed Isle? That would be a million people, having, conservatively, 30,000 children per year. 10% Exaltation rates would mean 3000 new DBs every year, i.e., a population roughly a third the size of the entire host. Even a 1% rate would imply a pretty terrifying mortality rate for the Dragon-Blooded (4.5% is pretty steep), and that 2/3 of the Dragon-Blooded are actually from families where they're the only Exalt, which is not the picture the books paint.<br /> <br /> Then consider that there are ~100 million <i>other</i> people on the Realm, who by that idiotic table still have non-negligible chances of their children Exalting; if even .01% of their 3 million kids per year Exalt, that's another 300 DBs annually - that is, a total of 750, or 7.5% of the total population. To maintain a stable population, that means another 7.5% of the total population has to <i>die</i> every year, which is a terrifying mortality rate.<br /> <br /> Then add Lost Eggs. Then you add the books' claims that most Dragon-Blooded live to retirement age, at around <i>250</i>. It's an impossible hash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T05:22:45-07:00","id":213432,"title":"","content":"If you assume about half the kids of dragonblooded exalt, then obviously the number of unexalted dynasts is going to be the same as the number of exalted ones. Less, because they don't live as long.<br /> <br /> Also people without any terrestrial blood exalt on storyteller fiat alone, so if your estimate of the percentage produces numbers too high then it's <i>too high itself.<br /> <br /> Also</i>, a good chunk of realm dragonbloods are in the order and don't breed. And they <i>are</i> noted to have a bonkers mortality rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 07-30-2014, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T05:27:52-07:00","id":213436,"title":"","content":"In order for Dragon-Blooded populations to stay stable with any kind of reasonable Exaltation rate, reasonable enough that children who don't Exalt are considered a disappointment rather than the norm (so let's say 50% and let confirmation bias take care of societal expectations), the collective 10,000 Realm Dragonblooded need to have 80 children a year if we assume that there is <i>no possibility whatsoever</i> of non-Dragonblooded bearing Dragonblooded children. In other words, 3% reproduction rate is incredibly huge, it needs to be about 0.8% to maintain a steady population if we assume that Lost Eggs are not a thing. MoEP: Dragonblooded cites the insane rate of the average Dragonblooded female having a child every twelve years, which translates to about a 10% reproduction rate.<br /> <br /> There is almost no way that Creation should not be overrun with Dragonblooded under the constraints that some significant percentage of Dynasts Exalt and that Dynasts have large families. I'm not sure there's a viable solution to this other than to not think about it too hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T05:33:17-07:00","id":213440,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Bloods tend to die.<br /> <br /> <i>A lot.</i><br /> <br /> Seriously. Consider that it is not extraordinary for a Dragon-Blood to reach 50 or even 100 without having married or birthed any children. Consider that in that time, they will be fighting wars in the Threshold, playing a lethal games of politics at home, or riding out into crazy adventures like the Wyld Hunt. Consider that a significant portion of Dragon-Blooded - including most Outcastes or Lost Eggs - are pushed towards the (celibate) Immaculate Order, which was in part<i> specifically designed</i> to remove them from the reproduction pool. <br /> <br /> The lethality rate of Dragon-Bloods is kind of astonishing. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T05:46:59-07:00","id":213445,"title":"","content":"Again to go by numbers, the only one I can find is a 50% mortality rate before retirement age. That still means the average Dynast lives to about 150 and pumps out about ten kids in that time, five of which Exalt. Plenty of them die without having kids, certainly, but between the ones that do, the ones that join the Immaculate Order, and the ones that live 300-500+ years pumping out kid after kid, that's the average.<br /> <br /> This means entire family lines are getting wiped out all the time, certainly, but this doesn't matter much when the ones that survive branch out as much as they do. More to the point, even if we assume the 50% mortality rate, that is to say half of all Dynasts die a violent death before retirement age, Dragonblooded <i>still</i> need to have an annual reproduction rate of less than 1.6% to not undergo exponential population growth. You can have a shocking percentage of your population dying young and still have your population increasing if that population never becomes infertile, lives for a long time, and is having a large number of kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T05:59:39-07:00","id":213450,"title":"","content":"10000 dragons on the blessed isle, say about 1/5 are IO, that leaves 8000. Half of those are female, so that's 4000 potential mothers. 8 kids a century each means 320 a year, assume about half of those exalt so we get about 160 new terrestrials a year.<br /> <br /> Huh. that's 1.6% of 10000. whaddya know.<br /> <br /> Of course the patricians and unexalted dynasts throw this off a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T06:09:21-07:00","id":213453,"title":"","content":"Also if the DB mortality rates get to be too high, then distinctions like House Cynis or House Mnemon, et cetera, become meaningless, because the idea of establishing a &quot;Great House&quot; when the DBs are being mass-force-fed through meat-grinders is <i>laughable</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T06:11:37-07:00","id":213455,"title":"","content":"It's pruning. The great houses are great because anyone born in them who is not great doesn't last long enough to cause them embarrassment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T06:25:23-07:00","id":213476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213425#post213425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, now how many <i>un</i>Exalted members of the Great Houses are there? Are they, say, 1% of the population of the Blessed Isle? That would be a million people, having, conservatively, 30,000 children per year. 10% Exaltation rates would mean 3000 new DBs every year, i.e., a population roughly a third the size of the entire host.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, the Second Edition core says that for the patricians (who are mostly descended from unExalted Dynasts and regularly have them married in, so they've got better blood than most mortals with no direct Exalted relatives), about one child in every 30,000 Exalts. I'd say the rate for commoners and peasants in the Realm is significantly lower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you add the books' claims that most Dragon-Blooded live to retirement age, at around <i>250</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nono, a <i>third</i> live to retirement, and that number is skewed by how many find major financial success young and retire early, so it's an even lower percentage who live to old age.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T06:33:48-07:00","id":213483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213453#post213453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if the DB mortality rates get to be too high, then distinctions like House Cynis or House Mnemon, et cetera, become meaningless, because the idea of establishing a &quot;Great House&quot; when the DBs are being mass-force-fed through meat-grinders is <i>laughable</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, when a Great House is established, they get significant protections, benefits and dispensations. The Empress shields them from the usual dangers of Dynastic competition until they're entrenched enough to successfully serve the purpose of keeping the Houses at each others' heels.<br /> <br /> Part of V'Neef is that they're a new House in the unique and unenviable position of lacking this safety net.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T06:51:52-07:00","id":213505,"title":"","content":"Safety net or no, if any day a Lunar can zip into your tent and kill you <i>as a housefly</i>, it matters little to which House you belong.<br /> <br /> Also since DBs only live for ~300 years (barring exceptions), having them only able to retire at 250 is asinine.<br /> <br /> The notion that two DB parents are going to have DB children more often than not before Breeding even factors in can go bye-bye if we don't tie DB Exaltation rates to a ridiculous death-rate.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That's not to say that I <i>want</i> Lunars cartoonishly snapping the necks of Dragon-Blooded while in a form that weighs less than a flicked booger - that's outrageously stupid, duh - but if people here are going to argue in favor of literally exactly that, of course it's going to make for a ridiculous, incoherent mess of a setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-30-2014, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T07:09:51-07:00","id":213515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213505#post213505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Safety net or no, if any day a Lunar can zip into your tent and kill you <i>as a housefly</i>, it matters little to which House you belong.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I don't think I understand what point you're making.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also since DBs only live for ~300 years (barring exceptions), having them only able to retire at 250 is asinine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying they should retire later or earlier? :s<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T07:19:23-07:00","id":213523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213515#post213515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... I don't think I understand what point you're making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dr. LoveMonkey literally described this exact scenario perhaps two pages ago. This is, or was, being argued for, a world where, even guarded and on the Blessed Isle, a sleeping Dynast will be easy prey for a Lunar, and his sworn brotherhood can consider themselves lucky they &quot;only&quot; drive the Lunar off afterward instead of being butchered themselves.<br /> <br /> Thing is, if this is a thing that happens, if DBs more often than not join the list of &quot;vanished by Lunar,&quot; then things like House affiliation probably won't have that much meaning even on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213515#post213515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying they should retire later or earlier? :s</div> </div> </div> </div>If, <i>if</i> we want to give DBs ridiculous death-rates to justify the ridiculous Exaltation-rates (I don't, but apparently some do), they should retire <i>way</i> earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-30-2014, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T07:50:33-07:00","id":213589,"title":"","content":"I've just come up with a really simple system tweak that I think puts the numbers closer to what is described in the books and/or is sensible.<br /> <br /> What we do is keep the target numbers as-is, but instead of rolling just one die, we roll a variable number based on the parents involved, and need to get at or below the target on all of them. Dragonbloods add a die to the pool each, mortals with terrestrial bloodline add 2 and regular mortals add 3. This has the advantage of only dropping the dragonblooded odds a bit whilst really kicking the ones involving mortals in the balls. For comparison it makes the kid of two dragonblooded of breeding 3 or lower have a 36% chance of exalting instead of 60, but makes the kid of two good blooded patricians have a 0.16% chance of exalting instead of 20%.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:14:53-07:00","id":213645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213476#post213476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nono, a <i>third</i> live to retirement, and that number is skewed by how many find major financial success young and retire early, so it's an even lower percentage who live to old age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to request you to double-check this; I'm away from my books at the moment, but I have a pretty firm recollection that, no, half live to retirement, a third live to die of old age. Couch seems to have found the same statistic. If you've got a citation that I'm just misrecalling, by all means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 07-30-2014, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:39:59-07:00","id":213663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213432#post213432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you assume about half the kids of dragonblooded exalt, then obviously the number of unexalted dynasts is going to be the same as the number of exalted ones. Less, because they don't live as long.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that simple - you have to consider what kids the mortal kids are more likely to have. More to the point, the books have always presented the Dragon-Blooded as the elite of the elite of dynast society, not a half-and-half mix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also people without any terrestrial blood exalt on storyteller fiat alone, so if your estimate of the percentage produces numbers too high then it's [I]too high itself. </div> </div> </div>When describing <i>the world</i>, rather than a game, it's not helpful to talk about storyteller fiat: in general, if we wanted to summarize the way Realm society works, what are the numbers? That's the question of interest here. And the answer to it <i>matters</i>, because a Realm where 10% of non-DB Dynast children Exalts is, shall we say, rather different from one where one in 30,000 Exalt, and your Exalted kid is the most important person that anyone in your social circle will ever know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a good chunk of realm dragonbloods are in the order and don't breed. </div> </div> </div>This is also true of human society; average birth rate figures take that kind of thing into account. (Real world birth rates range from .7% in Japan, which is &quot;SHOOT SHOOT EVERYBODY PANIC&quot; low even given modern lifespans, to about 5% in less-developed countries. If you're going to take the book's numbers on DB pressure to have children, you actually get a birth rate quite a bit higher than 3% - so again, you have to throw out <i>something</i>.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And they <i>are</i> noted to have a bonkers mortality rate. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Bloods tend to die.<br /> <br /> <i>A lot.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>In the example I gave earlier, I worked my way up to 750 DBs/year; for a balanced population, that implies a 7.5% mortality rate. I'm going to run with that number for what follows, because I have to run with <i>some</i> number; if you think this is the wrong one, that's fine, but treat it as a rebalancing point to figure out what number <i>does</i> make sense. From the fact that people are objecting, I'm going to assume that, on the surface, 7.5% doesn't sound that bad to at least some folks.<br /> <br /> So, let's talk about bonkers mortality rates. Africa has a pretty bonkers mortality rate, wouldn't you say, of modern countries? South Africa has the highest - and it's <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortality_rate\" target=\"_blank\">1.9%</a>. Iraq, if we want to add an active war zone to the picture, has a mortality rate of 0.4%.<br /> <br /> 7.5% is <i>stupidly</i> higher than that. Let's talk about what 7.5% mortality rate means: it means that every nine years, half of everyone you know is dead. The time from entering high school, to shortly after graduating college? Half of everyone you know is dead. Your ten-year college reunion? Half of your graduating class is dead. Reached age thirty? You're a lucky guy, because <i>90%</i> of your fellows won't. This is a mortality rate that might make you envious of the longevity of <i>your mortal peasants</i>.<br /> <br /> The Black Death, in Europe, was a time of pretty bonkers mortality, wouldn't you say? Wikipedia estimates that maybe 45% of Europe died during the Black Death, over the course of several decades. If we concentrated all of those deaths into just the 7 years when the plague was worst, <i>that's</i> a 7.5% mortality rate.<br /> <br /> Is that the mental image we have of the Realm: seven hundred years of Black Plague-level mortality? Because <i>that's where these numbers go</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 07-30-2014, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:40:28-07:00","id":213664,"title":"","content":"Hmmm what if only a small percentage of DBs get married? With most dying in the threshold or living out their days without having kids? It might be an okay explanation if you ignore all the dynastic pressure to get a husband and start cranking out children.<br /> <br /> Or we could just go with half of all dynasts are found dead in their bedchambers, often with a lingering aura of moon essence. All it would take is 5-10 psycho killer Lunars. Actually that's a high percentage of mental illness, even for the moon-mad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T09:56:09-07:00","id":213682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213664#post213664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm what if only a small percentage of DBs get married? With most dying in the threshold or living out their days without having kids? It might be an okay explanation if you ignore all the dynastic pressure to get a husband and start cranking out children.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Realm society was rewritten so that most Dynasts are basically sex-averse and birth rates are closer to modern Japan, sure, we could probably make this work, as long as we also are all clear that non-Exalts have teeny-tiny fractions-of-a-percent chances of having Exalted kids. That would be a <i>huge</i> rewrite to Realm society, though.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> Look, the big thing is: don't try to headspace this. Don't just think about numbers and go, &quot;Eh, that sounds right&quot;; as humans, we're really really terrible at statistics. Run a model! Figure out which of the given population figures you have to ignore (the sizes? the longevity? the birth rate? the Exaltation rate?), what real-world benchmarks those things correspond to, and then how the Realm <i>has</i> to look different as a result. You can run the Realm as &quot;Black Death Europe,&quot; but how does it shape society when you're probably going to be dead in ten years? How does it shape things if most DBs are born to unExalted patricians? To peasants? How are things different if you had a graduating class with <i>two</i> Exalts, as opposed to (as the books seem to presume) several hundred?<br /> <br /> But you can't just uncritically take the book's figures and go with them. That way lies madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T11:02:22-07:00","id":213750,"title":"","content":"I understand that not everyone sees it this way, but I don't really feel any compulsion to make the numbers make sense. Exalted is a world that operates on drama. An arrow fired from a bow will literally fly in a straighter trajectory if released in a dramatic fashion. An object at rest will remain at rest until drama acts upon it. An object in motion will continue in motion until acted upon by drama.<br /> <br /> The numbers given are only there for the purposes of story. The real reason there are supposedly 10,000 Dragon-Bloods in the Realm is because someone thought 100,000 would make the game too difficult for Solar PCs. The reason there are 11 Great Houses is because (I assume) someone decided that roughly two houses for each element was a good number. And the rate of Exaltation is pretty much dictated by the story. But the actual numbers in various books don't really add up when you look at them and to my knowledge they never have, so I pretty much just disregard numbers entirely. How many Dragon-Bloods are in the Realm? &quot;A lot.&quot; A more precise estimate? As many as the story demands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-30-2014, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T11:06:26-07:00","id":213751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213750#post213750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that not everyone sees it this way, but I don't really feel any compulsion to make the numbers make sense. Exalted is a world that runs not on math, but on drama. An arrow fired from a bow will literally fly in a straighter trajectory if released in a dramatic fashion. An object in motion will continue in motion until drama acts upon it. The numbers in various books don't add up to any kind of sense, and I tend to disregard them pretty much entirely. How many Dragon-Bloods are in the Realm? &quot;A lot.&quot; A more precise estimate? As many as the story demands.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's a fine way to play - but then you can't really make plans that depend on demographic information - like, say, &quot;Can I breed up an army of DBs given thus-and-such resources&quot; - because you're building a world that <i>has no demographics</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T11:14:07-07:00","id":213753,"title":"","content":"Well, you can have a rough idea of the demographic information. In a Ream legion, you can assume, every officer above the rank of Talonlord will be Exalted. There will be a large number of Exalted officers in supporting roles. Every scale of troops must at least have some officers trained to work essence. And so on. But in terms of population, I don't think you can really make a science out of it, considering the numbers given in various books are contradictory and often kind of ridiculous, with nations populated by millions fighting with armies of thousands in bronze-age style warfare. How far would you have to go to make it all add up? I really don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T11:54:36-07:00","id":213802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, if this is a thing that happens, if DBs more often than not join the list of &quot;vanished by Lunar,&quot; then things like House affiliation probably won't have that much meaning even on the Blessed Isle.</div> </div> </div> </div> Explain how. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, if we want to give DBs ridiculous death-rates to justify the ridiculous Exaltation-rates (I don't, but apparently some do), they should retire way earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which will accomplish what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T12:02:31-07:00","id":213812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213802#post213802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain how.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an earlier poster noted, the numbers are on par with the Black Death in Europe at its peak. Admittedly, I'm<i> not</i> an expert on these things, or anything really, but I imagine it's inordinately difficult to maintain a rigid, controlled dynastic structure when half a generation is killed off before they get to the point where they are capable of making the next generation.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which will accomplish what? </div> </div> </div><i>Any DBs at all surviving to retirement age under these ridiculous models, let alone a third of them.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-30-2014, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T14:06:16-07:00","id":213954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213753#post213753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you can have a rough idea of the demographic information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! Then we're using numerical ranges rather than specific numbers. It's still math!<br /> <br /> (I don't think knowing, you know, the <i>exact singular</i> number of Dragon-Blooded in the Realm is particularly helpful - but having workable approximations is nice! And it's really handy to have workable approximations that make sense with each other, because it avoids the problem where you realize that two different numbers you've pulled out of the air conflict. So, for instance: I don't much care whether there are 30 or 50 new Dragon-Blooded born in a given year, but knowing whether the mortality rate is more like 0.5% or 5% - which necessarily depends on the general answer I give to &quot;How many kids?&quot; - <i>does</i> matter to me, quite a bit. I don't want to describe the setting with 500 new kids a year and then realize I've written myself into a corner.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in terms of population, I don't think you can really make a science out of it, considering the numbers given in various books are contradictory and often kind of ridiculous, with nations populated by millions fighting with armies of thousands in bronze-age style warfare. How far would you have to go to make it all add up? I really don't know. </div> </div> </div>You can definitely make a science of it - you just can't do so while <i>also</i> honoring all the numbers in the books. So, again, it comes down to &quot;Which parts of the books do you want to ignore for your particular vision of the Realm?&quot; I recommend ignoring Exaltation rates and the number of new DBs per year (both way too high), at which point the rest of the world mostly falls into place, but there are lots of workable answers. It's just important not to take things like the Exaltation rate table as meaning <i>anything</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T15:03:34-07:00","id":213974,"title":"","content":"I wonder... if you took a family like the Rockefellers, and assumed that, say, a third of all members from the past 150 years were still alive, how many would there be?<br /> <br /> I think at least one thing keeping the numbers in the Realm down is how families have periodically lost all of their assets and benefits and thus lost their inroad to marriages with other well-bred Dragon Blooded, meaning that their own Exalted numbers drop off dramatically while they become lesser Houses, at the same time as new Houses have to start up from individual couples or otherwise small numbers. One House is sterilised as another has to start from scratch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T15:35:09-07:00","id":213991,"title":"","content":"I think it is a very rare thing when a Great House of the Dynasty falls. Mortal families, we know, come and go with regularity and are hardly noticed. Patrician families in whom one finds thin traces of the Blood Terrestrial multiply and divide. But when a Great Family falls, nations change hands in the balance, lines are redrawn across Creation. And I don't think any dynasts enjoy the thought of a Great House descending into the status of a patrician family, even if it should be their enemies, any more than they like the thought of a patrician family being elevated to the status of a Great House. Because either event subtly erodes the class solidarity on which Realm society depends. So from that point of view, it's preferable to the Empress and to all dynasts that a Great Family is destroyed utterly, than allowed to sink into the status of patricians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T17:19:38-07:00","id":214060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the numbers are on par with the Black Death in Europe at its peak</div> </div> </div> </div> What about the Kennedy Curse? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's preferable to the Empress and to all dynasts that a Great Family is destroyed utterly, than allowed to sink into the status of patricians.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's preferable to the Empress that the Dynasty fear her inflicting the things they wouldn't prefer upon them. Twelve Houses have fallen, in a Realm that is supposed to have been stable in a manner that doesn't fit with them all being as dramatic as Jerah or Manosque, and were likely replaced under conditions like what V'Neef is getting up to now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T17:23:22-07:00","id":214079,"title":"","content":"Actually, still considering the numbers, of the eleven families that the Great Houses are, one has spent about three hundred years being dismatled, forcing their members underground or into the Threshold (that can't help their marriage prospects), one has maybe ten people in total, and one is the infamously low-bred Nellens. How many Dynasts does that leave for the other Houses... 1,100 each?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T17:40:52-07:00","id":214092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=214079#post214079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, still considering the numbers, of the eleven families that the Great Houses are, one has spent about three hundred years being dismatled, forcing their members underground or into the Threshold (that can't help their marriage prospects), one has maybe ten people in total, and one is the infamously low-bred Nellens. How many Dynasts does that leave for the other Houses... 1,100 each?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, was the &quot;Ten Thousand Dragons&quot; thing actually said at some point to be a <i>literal</i> (even rough) count for Dragon-Blooded on the Blessed Isle (or in Creation as a whole), instead of just a poetic expression for how there are a helluva lot of them? I was sure it was the latter...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T17:51:49-07:00","id":214115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=214092#post214092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, was the &quot;Ten Thousand Dragons&quot; thing actually said at some point to be a <i>literal</i> (even rough) count for Dragon-Blooded on the Blessed Isle (or in Creation as a whole), instead of just a poetic expression for how there are a helluva lot of them? I was sure it was the latter...</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2E core book (page 43) says, &quot;Perhaps 10,000 Dragon-Bloods pledge their loyalty to the Realm.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I also prefer the poetic interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T19:55:07-07:00","id":214218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=214092#post214092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, was the &quot;Ten Thousand Dragons&quot; thing actually said at some point to be a <i>literal</i> (even rough) count for Dragon-Blooded on the Blessed Isle (or in Creation as a whole), instead of just a poetic expression for how there are a helluva lot of them? I was sure it was the latter...</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed it was. Ten thousand sounds like a lot, but when you look at an empire the size of USSR Russia and Asia combined...it's just doesn't make sense. Also Isator, don't forget all the minor houses, there are several and they all have Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T09:12:22-07:00","id":214730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=214092#post214092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, was the &quot;Ten Thousand Dragons&quot; thing actually said at some point to be a <i>literal</i> (even rough) count for Dragon-Blooded on the Blessed Isle (or in Creation as a whole), instead of just a poetic expression for how there are a helluva lot of them? I was sure it was the latter...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's used as the basic reference point in basically everything that discusses the number of Dragon Blooded in the Realm.<br /> <br /> Urrgghh, this whole subject just makes me want to see that House Mnemon genealogy being written up for Scarlet Manual of Upright Bearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T09:27:32-07:00","id":214736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213753#post213753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a Ream legion, you can assume, every officer above the rank of Talonlord will be Exalted. There will be a large number of Exalted officers in supporting roles. Every scale of troops must at least have some officers trained to work essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's stated that most legions can expect to have the winglords and the general be Exalted, and that's it; they occasionally get fifty or sixty officers in a legion, but that's really weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">with nations populated by millions fighting with armies of thousands in bronze-age style warfare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by Bronze-Age style. Also, are you saying the armies are too small, or too big?<br /> <br /> I'm personally totally on board with the idea that Second Edition was far too cavalier with portraying nations as having professional standing armies of recruits, rather than raising levies in times of war or retaining the services of mercenaries.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T14:42:31-07:00","id":215078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=213812#post213812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an earlier poster noted, the numbers are on par with the Black Death in Europe at its peak. Admittedly, I'm<i> not</i> an expert on these things, or anything really, but I imagine it's inordinately difficult to maintain a rigid, controlled dynastic structure when half a generation is killed off before they get to the point where they are capable of making the next generation.<i>Any DBs at all surviving to retirement age under these ridiculous models, let alone a third of them.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Very few DBs living to retirement is an idea that might make some sense in the culture of the more martial houses. I mean, dying in a sickbed, that's no way for a Tepet to die. Not while you can die swinging a daiklave, your anima pouring scorn on the Empress's enemies, a virtuous and noble death, preferably atop a heap of Lookshyans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=214736#post214736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's stated that most legions can expect to have the winglords and the general be Exalted, and that's it; they occasionally get fifty or sixty officers in a legion, but that's really weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legion organization goes: Legion, dragon, wing, talon, scale, fang.<br /> <br /> Winglords, dragonlords and generals are, of course, Exalted. Talonlords too, sometimes, depending on the circumstances. But whatever any book says, I think Terrestrials are also valued as engineers, artificers, geomancers, spies, intelligencers and assassins, physicians, alchemists and medics, sorcerers, logistics officers, military investigators, architects, diplomats, bureaucrats and plenty of other positions other than battlefield command roles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=214736#post214736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by Bronze-Age style. Also, are you saying the armies are too small, or too big?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, I think the armies are too small for the cities/countries they belong to. But in other cases they're probably too big. The numbers are just all over the place. The books don't really seem to agree on what constitutes a big city, either. And I agree with you about standing armies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 07-31-2014, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T15:28:29-07:00","id":215152,"title":"","content":"Oh, wait, I made a mistake; I mixed up wings and dragons again. I'm always doing that.<br /> <br /> The average legion has eleven Dragon Blooded in total.<br /> <br /> I have to reread the Thousand Correct Actions and see if the Realm organizational doctrine allows for high ranking officers to serve certain other roles, but even so...<br /> <br /> I wouldn't think it's much of a stretch for a legion deployed for war to typically have another dozen Terrestrials to serve vital auxilliary roles. In my mind, they're not quite formal units in the military organization (but then, neither are the rank and file; most of their cavalry, archers and skirmishers, say, or drawn from subject populations, even probably sometimes mercenaries; recruits and commissions are in the medium and heavy infantry phalanxes, which form the heart of their tactical doctrine). Like, I've said before how I think most retired Dynasts have engaged in some form of military service at one time or another even when it's not the focus of their career and lifestyle, I imagine that most engage in such by lending their actual talents to various support roles (with an understanding that they'll possibly get in a scrap while on the march, or if a camp is struck during a flanking action, or the whole legion is overrun a bit). It's a bit of a voluntary thing; like, Dynasts who hear that a legion is being deployed for war will usually volunteer their support services for the prestige or adventure, and when they don't there'll be somebody in the legion command structure tasked to go recruiting.<br /> <br /> But they're not a permanent fixture, not career soldiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think the armies are too small for the cities/countries they belong to.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't know, from what I gather, the sizes of armies have usually derived mostly from the bureaucratic apparatus to gather and manage them, economic development that gets them funded, and the surrounding cultural ideal for service in and use of militaries.<br /> <br /> That... can actually lend itself to one standard or the other; you've got societies where regularly deploying 12,000 is pretty extreme, largely because they're all farmers fulfilling a feudal or national duty who need to be home by harvest, or ones that can manage fifty to sixty thousand because they're all mercenaries from a militant culture that is a client state.<br /> <br /> It helps that numbers in armies don't usually matter as much as one might think.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, I meant to say, part of my attitude about specialists is that I wouldn't want it to imply that mortal experts don't have their value to Dragon Blooded commanders, including them being in their own positions of command.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 07-31-2014, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T00:44:33-07:00","id":215654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215152#post215152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The average legion has eleven Dragon Blooded in total.<br /> <br /> I have to reread the Thousand Correct Actions and see if the Realm organizational doctrine allows for high ranking officers to serve certain other roles, but even so...<br /> <br /> I wouldn't think it's much of a stretch for a legion deployed for war to typically have another dozen Terrestrials to serve vital auxilliary roles. In my mind, they're not quite formal units in the military organization (but then, neither are the rank and file; most of their cavalry, archers and skirmishers, say, or drawn from subject populations, even probably sometimes mercenaries; recruits and commissions are in the medium and heavy infantry phalanxes, which form the heart of their tactical doctrine). Like, I've said before how I think most retired Dynasts have engaged in some form of military service at one time or another even when it's not the focus of their career and lifestyle, I imagine that most engage in such by lending their actual talents to various support roles (with an understanding that they'll possibly get in a scrap while on the march, or if a camp is struck during a flanking action, or the whole legion is overrun a bit). It's a bit of a voluntary thing; like, Dynasts who hear that a legion is being deployed for war will usually volunteer their support services for the prestige or adventure, and when they don't there'll be somebody in the legion command structure tasked to go recruiting.<br /> <br /> But they're not a permanent fixture, not career soldiers.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, I meant to say, part of my attitude about specialists is that I wouldn't want it to imply that mortal experts don't have their value to Dragon Blooded commanders, including them being in their own positions of command.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither would I. The dynastic Lunar I mentioned on this thread was a heroic mortal talonlord before Exalation, and most of his family are in legion posts. So this is something I've thought about a lot, and I would never say mortal soldiers don't have value in Realm legions when obviously they do; they're most of the legion's strength and skill. So no problem agreeing with you there. But just on the basis of arithmetic, I think it's better to just take what the books say about the number of DBs in a legion and throw it in the garbage. Because - at least in the more martial Houses - if there are 11 Dragon-Bloods in a legion, and maybe 60 or 70 in all the family's legions combined, then what the heck are all the rest of them doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-01-2014, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T00:48:56-07:00","id":215655,"title":"","content":"Running the country?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T01:00:19-07:00","id":215660,"title":"","content":"Ugh, no. Running the country? What do we have patricians for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T01:26:01-07:00","id":215668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215654#post215654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what the heck are all the rest of them doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same thing any aristocrat spends their time doing - having their way with the maids and anyone else who catches their eye.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=StJS51d1Fzg\" data-code=\"StJS51d1Fzg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/StJS51d1Fzg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-01-2014, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T04:04:37-07:00","id":215731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215654#post215654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because - at least in the more martial Houses - if there are 11 Dragon-Bloods in a legion, and maybe 60 or 70 in all the family's legions combined, then what the heck are all the rest of them doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd first think the more martial Houses are a bit smaller than the other ones; Cathak particularly is described as having a problem with their members dying glorious deaths.<br /> <br /> I'd say that when it comes to the more martial Houses, they provide the majority of career officers for the Imperial legions, but the majority of actual House members prefer to go off on their own military ventures, where they can be their own bosses and fight for their own glories rather than the advantages of the state. They take relatively small companies of of the family troops around to pillage beyond the edge of the Threshold or act as elite troops in foreign wars, in contrast to typical House legions who basically just do security detail on the collection of tribute.<br /> <br /> Then this makes for House legions that are a bit too elite and experienced, and need to be taken down a peg.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">EDIT: Wait, I think I came up with the numbers for this once...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If I assume that it's reasonable for about a thousand Exalted to typically serve in the legions at once, then that means you can get 20 legions with the usual complement of eleven Exalted, four particularly elite ones with sixty, and the remaining eight are somewhere in between, varying according to legion...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Then if it's about... Cathak, Tepet and Sesus are liable to provide 250 each at any one time, the other Houses make up a hundred between them, and the rest are Found Eggs who accepted the coin...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you average about a thousand per House, but assume that the militant ones are a bit smaller, then that means ones serving in the Imperial legions make up better than a quarter of all members of the House? Combine that with assumptions that many of the others engage in more private enterprise forms of military venture, and that not every member of those Houses can be a soldier, and...<br /> <br /> I think that's consistent, at least.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-01-2014, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T04:09:42-07:00","id":215733,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that not all the prestigious Realm academies cater to military careers. Although the Realm is a martial society, many Dynastic scions become bureaucrats, spies or artists instead.<br /> <br /> The only reason I can think of that the Realm isn't better suited for producing larger populations of Dragon-Blooded than it is is that the Empress designed it to stabilize at a limited population for her to better keep it under control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-01-2014, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T05:36:31-07:00","id":215785,"title":"","content":"That was actually mentioned somewhere, I think, but I cannot remember the source - essentially that the Scarlet Empress\u00b4 policies are geared towards a stable number of Dragon-blooded in the Empire, not a growing one. The high First Age had how many, a million? In a sense, it\u00b4s a shame how much the Exalted of the Dragons had fallen, even as they rose in political power.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I\u00b4d expect the Realm with Her Redness on the throne could fairly easily pseudo-draft dragonblooded if it needs them, for example if it is expecting a serious war. Nowadays, this power lies with the noble houses who can pressure the kids to pitch in for their house legions, so a lot of DBs are essentially reservists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T05:57:03-07:00","id":215790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=208815#post208815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're quite welcome. And there are reasons for the endemic problems to Lunars that go back so far that it's not surprising many of them were carried forward.<br /> <br /> Some reading on the subject that I believe to be accurate, from Holden:<br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:the-lunar-factions\" target=\"_blank\">The Lunar Factions</a><br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:fixing-the-lunars\" target=\"_blank\">Fixing the Lunars</a><br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/troubled-lunar-history\" target=\"_blank\">Troubled Lunar History</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to thank you for the links. I'm only partway though the rest of them, but I really like what Holden's been saying here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T08:33:02-07:00","id":215897,"title":"","content":"Maybe Lunars would have been better off if their shards had gotten trapped in the Jade Prison with the solars, or if they had wandered off into the wyld on some sort of quest and just returned prior to the standard start point.<br /> <br /> Basically anything that gives them a concrete reason to have vanished for a millennia and a half. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T08:39:06-07:00","id":215899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215733#post215733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that not all the prestigious Realm academies cater to military careers. Although the Realm is a martial society, many Dynastic scions become bureaucrats, spies or artists instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends... part of the reason for their post-school sabbaticals is supposed to be picking up skills they didn't get in school. Plus, even before secondary school, every young Dynast is expected to at least know the rudiments of fighting and warfare.<br /> <br /> I'd say the majority of them are at least good enough to help out in a scrap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only reason I can think of that the Realm isn't better suited for producing larger populations of Dragon-Blooded than it is is that the Empress designed it to stabilize at a limited population for her to better keep it under control.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215785#post215785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was actually mentioned somewhere, I think, but I cannot remember the source - essentially that the Scarlet Empress\u00b4 policies are geared towards a stable number of Dragon-blooded in the Empire, not a growing one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently you'll get higher taxes on the land you need to accomodate and increasingly large family, as a disincentive.<br /> <br /> Mostly though, I think even my ideas about the likelihood of them dying is a bit excessive. The books seem to generally assume that their long life spans account more for them taking longer to do everything than fitting more things into their full span. It's like, sure, if a well-bred Exalted Dynast, you're going to live a long time and have descendent who will as well, but it still seems to generally assume that you're only around to see your great-grandchildren, maybe a single generation after that at best*. And whatever the importance they place on children, they still don't seem to have a particularly extreme attitude to it just as a matter of being people; I mean, who <i>really</i> wants twenty or so children?<br /> <br /> So I mean, if you're about eighty before you even have your first child, and don't really want to have more than six or seven, ten at an extreme, and your own children carry that same attitude, how many descendants will be around before you and everybody in your generation dies of old age (even if they won't)?<br /> <br /> * If they're Exalted, of course; if you live 300 years, you'll be around for your mortal grandchildren who are about fifteen generations away from you. The fact that, being a line that persists in mortality for so long means you don't really acknowledge them as relatives at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T08:52:45-07:00","id":215905,"title":"","content":"There are exceptions to that in canon too, especially in Lookshy where it's stated that they go for numbers. Karal Linwei would have been about 30 at the oldest when her daughter Fire Orchid was born, and I don't think she's her eldest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T09:01:39-07:00","id":215913,"title":"","content":"Personally I find the idea that Dynasts are generally slow about having children, but aren't dying in a meat grinder, preferable to the idea that they're suffering Black Death mortality rates while making up for it by pumping out absurd numbers of children.<br /> <br /> I mean, if a Dragonblooded lives to around 300, they can wait until they're sixty to have their first child and still be around to see three generations of descendants assuming some of their lineage Exalts. They can take their time about it, maybe have three or four children at sixty and then another batch a hundred years down the road. Instead we have this bizarre situation where if people tend to treat Dragonblooded as being baby factories, it's because their own society does <i>exactly that</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T09:10:23-07:00","id":215916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215790#post215790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wanted to thank you for the links. I'm only partway though the rest of them, but I really like what Holden's been saying here.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome; glad to share ideas around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T09:28:12-07:00","id":215922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215913#post215913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I find the idea that Dynasts are generally slow about having children, but aren't dying in a meat grinder, preferable to the idea that they're suffering Black Death mortality rates while making up for it by pumping out absurd numbers of children.<br /> <br /> I mean, if a Dragonblooded lives to around 300, they can wait until they're sixty to have their first child and still be around to see three generations of descendants assuming some of their lineage Exalts. They can take their time about it, maybe have three or four children at sixty and then another batch a hundred years down the road. Instead we have this bizarre situation where if people tend to treat Dragonblooded as being baby factories, it's because their own society does <i>exactly that</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, exactly. You could write a Realm where Dragon-Blooded just don't have kids that often (but when they do, the kids usually Exalt) -<br /> <br /> - though to do so, you'd need to address <i>why</i> their society works this way, when a new Exalt is just about the most potent resource you/your family/your house could desire, and so it's in their interests to encourage it -<br /> <br /> - but in any event, that's the exact opposite of the Realm presented, because, basically, nobody ever sat down and worked out the numbers.<br /> <br /> (You can tell that the author of MoEP: DBs thinks there are hundreds of new Dragon-Blooded every year, because he claims that there are, like, half-a-dozen secondary schools, several of which are <i>primarily</i> Dragon-Blooded in their populations.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T09:48:32-07:00","id":215941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215913#post215913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they're suffering Black Death mortality rates</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this concept is entirely sound... I'm pretty sure there's a meaningful difference between 14% of several million people dying in two or three years and 14% of a few thousand people, or whatever the percentages are.<br /> <br /> That and considerations for the other circumstances, like the difference between everyday society in general and what's basically a subculture of a dangerous lifestyle. How does that percentage compare to gang related murder rates in one of the more violent American cities? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T10:01:57-07:00","id":215949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215922#post215922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could write a Realm where Dragon-Blooded just don't have kids that often</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't only a few hundred new children per year when there are probably several thousand Dragon Blooded couples already them not having kids that often?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">though to do so, you'd need to address <i>why</i> their society works this way, when a new Exalt is just about the most potent resource you/your family/your house could desire, and so it's in their interests to encourage it -</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's the expense and the time investment...<br /> <br /> I've also got my own idea that a lot of Dragon Blooded only try for children in coordination with other Dragon Blooded whose kids they want their own to be socially tied to, including being marriage prospects. Like, you don't want to have a kid who'll go through their school years with a bunch of undesirables.<br /> <br /> Plus, not all people are more interested in the vague nebulous benefits of having an Exalted child to serve as a political pawn or whatever than in pursuing their own achievements and enjoyments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- but in any event, that's the exact opposite of the Realm presented</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it though?<br /> <br /> I mean, Exalted: the Dragon Blooded almost seems to suggest that even more Dynasts would delay having children for longer than thirty or fifty years if it weren't for the fact that doing the former causes people to gossip about your fertility, and the latter leads to summary dissolution of your marriage.<br /> <br /> I don't think the book has ever portrayed them as obsessed with reproduction as the fans seem to assume they would be...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T10:07:36-07:00","id":215953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215941#post215941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this concept is entirely sound... I'm pretty sure there's a meaningful difference between 14% of several million people dying in two or three years and 14% of a few thousand people, or whatever the percentages are.</div> </div> </div> </div>14% is 14% regardless of whether it's several million or a few thousand people. That is literally what a percent means. For the upper class of Realm aristocracy to have the breeding habits described in MoEP: DB, you have to be five times as likely to die as one of the elite of Realm society than you are to die as someone in Somalia or the Congo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That and considerations for the other circumstances, like the difference between everyday society in general and what's basically a subculture of a dangerous lifestyle. How does that percentage compare to gang related murder rates in one of the more violent American cities? </div> </div> </div>Let's take World War I, one of the bloodiest conflicts in all of human history. 9 million soldiers dead. Trench warfare basically defines the meat grinder in how long it takes to play out and how many casualties it racks up per battle, there is virtually no bloodier way to fight a war.<br /> <br /> 70 million soldiers were mobilized in World War I. That means across the four years of that war, 12% of the participants died. Meaning <i>even that</i> was a 3% mortality rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T11:47:55-07:00","id":216059,"title":"","content":"Waaait waitwaitwait, I'm sure I've done the numbers on this before...<br /> <br /> Assuming the &quot;ten thousand&quot; figure refers primarily to graduated adults, if we assume there are something like 4800 married couples at any given time, we take the numbers said to attend secondary school and apply them across the board to get 2400 children between the ages of one and eighteen at any given time, so about half the Dynasts have school-aged children at any given time, if about 200 graduate and enter secondary school each year, round that up to about 300 to fit a number somebody else said and assume a whole bunch drop out or burn out, that seems fairly consistent, so...<br /> <br /> I don't know, every year 300 are born, 300 die to keep the overall number from growing, that seems like a lot of deaths per year without being ridiculous, and enough births to be consistent with the setting portrayal.<br /> <br /> It's definitely no Black Death, I'll tell you that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T12:24:07-07:00","id":216081,"title":"","content":"Long time reader first time poster yadda yadda. Anyway, I took a look at those numbers and while I'm no math-expert, something seems very off.<br /> <br /> Assume for a moment that the 300 deaths come purely from the oldest year of dragon-bloods around. Each DB could then be said to advance in the &quot;queue&quot; by 300 slots per year. I went through it and my numbers came out to ~33.3 years of life before reaching the end of the line - which is a rather low expected lifespan for anyone, let alone the long-lived dragon-blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3630-cuddlefission","name":"Cuddlefission","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:15:43-07:00","id":216108,"title":"","content":"300 dying each year out of 10,000 is 3% mortality, which as I said is about the mortality rate of World War I and considerably higher than the worst countries in the entire world to live in from a longevity standpoint. It's considerably higher than the mortality rate of most wars. So every single Dragonblooded is partaking in trench warfare for their entire lives.<br /> <br /> 3% mortality rate means that by the time you're twenty-four, half the people you grew up with are dead. By forty-seven, another half. Five Dragonblooded out of every 10,000 will make it to retirement age and only one will die of old age.<br /> <br /> Numbers that &quot;feel&quot; right almost never are when it comes to statistics. You have to actually go and do the math. The math comes out to a society of long-lived people needing to have very low birth rates, not the typical Dragonblooded woman putting out a baby every twelve years. That in turn means you can't have the kinds of schools described where Dragonblooded are most or all of the students. It's simply not plausible. Either the Dragonblooded population is undergoing growth over time, Dragonblooded die at a rate equivalent to the bloodiest wars in human history and thus have shorter lifespans than their mortal peasants, or Dragonblooded are comparably sex-averse to modern Japan and only a tiny fraction of them end up actually bearing children at all. All of these require rewriting chunks of Realm culture and politics, because the current arrangement is impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:24:43-07:00","id":216112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215941#post215941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this concept is entirely sound... I'm pretty sure there's a meaningful difference between 14% of several million people dying in two or three years and 14% of a few thousand people, or whatever the percentages are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure there isn't; I'd imagine peasants in a village in France didn't care how many millions were dying, just how many of the couple of thousand of people they interacted with were dying. To go personal, I'd for darn sure sit up and take notice if 7.4% of, say, my graduating college class were dying every year.<br /> <br /> And again, these are <i>worse</i> than Black Death rates: these are rates as if all those who died of the bubonic plague were compressed into a period of seven years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That and considerations for the other circumstances, like the difference between everyday society in general and what's basically a subculture of a dangerous lifestyle. How does that percentage compare to gang related murder rates in one of the more violent American cities? </div> </div> </div>A quick bit of Googling doesn't turn up any definite numbers, but let's go with <a href=\"http://www.nationalgangcenter.gov/survey-analysis/measuring-the-extent-of-gang-problems\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a benchmark: 782,500 gang members, with ~2000 gang-related homicides reported. If all of those deaths are gang members, that's, uh, a 0.25% death rate for <i>actually being in a gang</i>, so.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps you meant &quot;what percent of people are dying to gang violence, in violent cities.&quot; Again, hard to say, but let's overestimate: the city with the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_cities_by_crime_rate\" target=\"_blank\">highest murder rate in America</a> is (surprising no one) Detroit. Suppose all of those murders are gang-related; that's still only 54 out of every 100,000 people, or a 0.054% murder rate.<br /> <br /> Or let me give another perspective for a &quot;high risk&quot; population: the Soviet Union took pretty appalling losses during World War 2, right? They lost something like 14% of their population during that time, which is horrific. Of course, that was the total over <i>six years</i>; on average during WW2, the Soviets only suffered about 2.5% mortality rates due to war, famine, and disease. To get the kinds of numbers we're talking about in this thread, you have to <i>triple</i> those rates.<br /> <br /> <i>Stop defending this number.</i> Its only function in this thread is to make everyone go, &quot;Well, <i>that</i> can't be right.&quot; Find an assumption to relax that doesn't require 90% of the fifteen-year-olds who Exalt as Dragon-Blooded to be dead by 45.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 08-01-2014, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:25:47-07:00","id":216114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216108#post216108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">300 dying each year out of 10,000 is 3% mortality, which as I said is about the mortality rate of World War I and considerably higher than the worst countries in the entire world to live in from a longevity standpoint. It's considerably higher than the mortality rate of most wars. So every single Dragonblooded is partaking in trench warfare for their entire lives.<br /> <br /> 3% mortality rate means that by the time you're twenty-four, half the people you grew up with are dead. By forty-seven, another half. Five Dragonblooded out of every 10,000 will make it to retirement age and only one will die of old age.<br /> <br /> Numbers that &quot;feel&quot; right almost never are when it comes to statistics. You have to actually go and do the math. The math comes out to a society of long-lived people needing to have very low birth rates, not the typical Dragonblooded woman putting out a baby every twelve years. That in turn means you can't have the kinds of schools described where Dragonblooded are most or all of the students. It's simply not plausible. Either the Dragonblooded population is undergoing growth over time, Dragonblooded die at a rate equivalent to the bloodiest wars in human history and thus have shorter lifespans than their mortal peasants, or Dragonblooded are comparably sex-averse to modern Japan and only a tiny fraction of them end up actually bearing children at all. All of these require rewriting chunks of Realm culture and politics, because the current arrangement is impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, given <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zarataylor/ExaltedNumbers\" target=\"_blank\">this set of detail</a>s, that would be more like 2% mortality, most of which is soaked up by the five to six thousand Lost Eggs that the Realm has. That's a rather generous cushion, with more Lost Eggs coming in every year regardless of the Realm's birth rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:36:00-07:00","id":216121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216114#post216114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, given <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zarataylor/ExaltedNumbers\" target=\"_blank\">this set of detail</a>s, that would be more like 2% mortality, most of which is soaked up by the five to six thousand Lost Eggs that the Realm has. That's a rather generous cushion, with more Lost Eggs coming in every year regardless of the Realm's birth rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Lots of Found Eggs come in every year&quot; makes the problem <i>worse</i>, because it means the total population growth is higher - you have to either raise mortality or lower birth/Exaltation rates to compensate.<br /> <br /> Edit: Yeah, Couch has the better point here - adding an additional population doesn't change the problem for <i>this</i> population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 08-01-2014, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:39:11-07:00","id":216122,"title":"","content":"The Lost Eggs don't come into consideration here because, as we've established, they overwhelmingly don't breed and more importantly, aren't counted as part of the 10,000 we're trying to keep constant. 300 births among Dynasts requires 300 deaths among Dynasts, which gives you World War I death tolls.<br /> <br /> A more reasonable number would be 1%, which is higher than most developed countries but gives you an expected lifespan of closer to 70. 0.5%, that is to say the expected mortality rate of modern Mexico, gives you 140. To match &quot;half die before retirement at 250&quot;, there need to be only 0.3% birth and death rates among Dragonblooded, which is about how many people die each year on the Cayman Islands. When you're trying to keep someone alive for that many years, they need to have a <i>very</i> low chance of dying each year because they're rolling the dice so many times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T13:42:15-07:00","id":216124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=215949#post215949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't only a few hundred new children per year when there are probably several thousand Dragon Blooded couples already them not having kids that often?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! And a few hundred children per year is <i>still too high</i>, as demonstrated. That's my point: you have to push the numbers freakishly low, to something like 30 kids/year, unless you want the All Trench Warfare, All the Time version of the Realm.<br /> <br /> (The simplest change to enable this rate is to make Exaltation rates really, really low, in the range of 1-10% of their kids for most Dragon-Blooded couples, and maybe 50% for the really exceptionally high-Breeding parents. Maybe 80-90% for, like, V'neef, and probably <i>just</i> V'neef. Alternative #2 is to let the DB population have increased over time to, like, a million, but it plays against the &quot;Realm in decline&quot; image if they have more Dragon-Blooded than ever in their history.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well there's the expense and the time investment... </div> </div> </div>Cultural pressure, dude. The Realm as written now acknowledges the value of Dragon-Blooded heirs for the empire - that's why the Great Houses push their families to reproduce so much.<br /> <br /> Plus, pfft, time investment? Not like you're going to have to raise the kid yourself if you don't want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it though?<br /> <br /> I mean, Exalted: the Dragon Blooded almost seems to suggest that even more Dynasts would delay having children for longer than thirty or fifty years if it weren't for the fact that doing the former causes people to gossip about your fertility, and the latter leads to summary dissolution of your marriage. </div> </div> </div>Um, yes, it is. The fact that the Realm has institutions to punish you for not having children is precisely the thing I'm talking about, here.<br /> <br /> Who cares whether any particular couple wants children? Their society is built to <i>require</i> it, and the books are explicit on how relatively frequently you're expected to comply. This is a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 08-01-2014, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T14:06:05-07:00","id":216139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216108#post216108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">300 dying each year out of 10,000 is 3% mortality, which as I said is about the mortality rate of World War I and considerably higher than the worst countries in the entire world to live in from a longevity standpoint. It's considerably higher than the mortality rate of most wars. So every single Dragonblooded is partaking in trench warfare for their entire lives.<br /> <br /> 3% mortality rate means that by the time you're twenty-four, half the people you grew up with are dead. By forty-seven, another half. Five Dragonblooded out of every 10,000 will make it to retirement age and only one will die of old age.<br /> <br /> Numbers that &quot;feel&quot; right almost never are when it comes to statistics. You have to actually go and do the math. The math comes out to a society of long-lived people needing to have very low birth rates, not the typical Dragonblooded woman putting out a baby every twelve years. That in turn means you can't have the kinds of schools described where Dragonblooded are most or all of the students. It's simply not plausible. Either the Dragonblooded population is undergoing growth over time, Dragonblooded die at a rate equivalent to the bloodiest wars in human history and thus have shorter lifespans than their mortal peasants, or Dragonblooded are comparably sex-averse to modern Japan and only a tiny fraction of them end up actually bearing children at all. All of these require rewriting chunks of Realm culture and politics, because the current arrangement is impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't all this fixed if you just assume there are way more than 10,000 Dragon-Bloods in the Realm? 10,000 is a purely arbitrary number anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T14:20:40-07:00","id":216148,"title":"","content":"That'd work fine if you kept the birth count the same (thus decreasing relative birth rate substantially), but if you kept the birth rate the same you'd have a much larger population influx that you'd need to cancel out, creating the same problem again.<br /> <br /> Trying to have both a static overall population and culturally mandated high birth rates at the same time -requires- a massive population sink to balance the equation. You can do either of them fine without it, but trying to do both at once, not so much.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, considering we're talking only about the actual dragon blooded in that number, you could keep the high birth rate but just plummet the actual rate of exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3630-cuddlefission","user":"Cuddlefission","date":". 08-01-2014, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3630-cuddlefission","name":"Cuddlefission","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T14:26:58-07:00","id":216150,"title":"","content":"We're told the Empress has for whatever reason made an active effort to keep the number of Realm Dragonblooded, aside from Lost Eggs, at exactly 10,000. It's just that whoever wrote the books seems to have thought that meant she had to try to keep their numbers up, rather than what she should be doing which is trying to keep them down. If the population of Realm Dragonblooded is allowed to grow, then there's no issue because it grows.<br /> <br /> Grows at a rate of about 7.2% annually, to go by the &quot;child every twelve years&quot; thing, meaning if there were 10,000 Dragonblooded at the start of the Realm there are now about 1.34*10^28 Dragonblooded no wait that doesn't work either. Maybe this &quot;child every twelve years&quot; thing is just stupid.<br /> <br /> Modern US birth rates of 1.2%, with a 0.3% death rate, give you about 13 million Dragonblooded today from a starting population of 10,000. Isn't compounding wonderful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T14:35:45-07:00","id":216156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216150#post216150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're told the Empress has for whatever reason made an active effort to keep the number of Realm Dragonblooded, aside from Lost Eggs, at exactly 10,000. It's just that whoever wrote the books seems to have thought that meant she had to try to keep their numbers up, rather than what she should be doing which is trying to keep them down. If the population of Realm Dragonblooded is allowed to grow, then there's no issue because it grows.<br /> <br /> Grows at a rate of about 7.2% annually, to go by the &quot;child every twelve years&quot; thing, meaning if there were 10,000 Dragonblooded at the start of the Realm there are now about 1.34*10^28 Dragonblooded no wait that doesn't work either. Maybe this &quot;child every twelve years&quot; thing is just stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the thinning of the blood means the host is in decline and...<br /> <br /> Yeah, (most) writers can't do math.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:01:49-07:00","id":216187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216150#post216150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're told the Empress has for whatever reason made an active effort to keep the number of Realm Dragonblooded, aside from Lost Eggs, at exactly 10,000. It's just that whoever wrote the books seems to have thought that meant she had to try to keep their numbers up, rather than what she should be doing which is trying to keep them down. If the population of Realm Dragonblooded is allowed to grow, then there's no issue because it grows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember reading that. The 2E core book doesn't give it as an exact number. It says there are, &quot;Perhaps 10,000&quot; Dragon-Bloods in the Realm.<br /> <br /> Anyway, what I'm saying is why not just ignore that number? If you forget the idea that there are only 10,000, then the birth and death statistics could make sense. 10,000 Dragon-Bloods has always seemed like a totally arbitrary figure to me, and it seems to make a mess of a lot of things, so I always just pass it off as a figure of speech in my games.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cuddlefission</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216148#post216148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'd work fine if you kept the birth count the same (thus decreasing relative birth rate substantially), but if you kept the birth rate the same you'd have a much larger population influx that you'd need to cancel out, creating the same problem again.<br /> <br /> Trying to have both a static overall population and culturally mandated high birth rates at the same time -requires- a massive population sink to balance the equation. You can do either of them fine without it, but trying to do both at once, not so much.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, considering we're talking only about the actual dragon blooded in that number, you could keep the high birth rate but just plummet the actual rate of exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also suggest just tossing out the idea that the Realm's Dragon-Blooded population remains fixed at some arbitrary number. What sense does that make? Do the Realm's enemies obligingly decline to multiply as well? The Empress is supposed to be an astute ruler, surely she can handle something as basic as &quot;there are more of my subjects than there used to be.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not to mention, with houses rising and falling, keeping the number of Dragon-Bloods fixed at some number would be an incredible feat all by itself and even if it succeeded probably the only thing it would accomplish would be creating several times as many bastards outside the dynasty.<br /> <br /> NOT TO MENTION, Terrestrials are nothing if not fecund. The libido of the Dragon-Blooded is the subject of plays throughout Creation. It's in their very essence to multiply. The idea of a Dragon-Blooded population that stagnates at a certain level is unnatural and hard to believe, possibly blasphemy against the elemental dragons themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-01-2014, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:19:34-07:00","id":216197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216187#post216187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, what I'm saying is why not just ignore that number? <br /> ...<br /> I would also suggest just tossing out the idea that the Realm's Dragon-Blooded population remains fixed at some arbitrary number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, right, as Couch notes, if you toss out the idea of a balanced population, you can make this work. If you're fine with there being tens of millions of Dragon-Blooded in the Realm, then cool. Making this statement is going to change the way you portray Realm society in a pretty major way, though, so it's one that needs to be thought through; it also, as noted above, is somewhat problematic to the idea that the Wyld Hunt is understaffed and at a fraction of its former strength. The Realm should have more raw power now than ever in its history; the story of the Realm should be one of ever-increasing might and territory as its Exalted population grows.<br /> <br /> But yes, you can do it! The constraints are: birth rate, Exaltation rate, death rate, starting population size, with population growth and final population size falling out of these. You can solve the problem by changing any of these constraints - you just have to change <i>something</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:23:25-07:00","id":216202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216197#post216197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, right, as Couch notes, if you toss out the idea of a balanced population, you can make this work. If you're fine with there being tens of millions of Dragon-Blooded in the Realm, then cool. Making this statement is going to change the way you portray Realm society in a pretty major way, though, so it's one that needs to be thought through; it also, as noted above, is somewhat problematic to the idea that the Wyld Hunt is understaffed and at a fraction of its former strength. The Realm should have more raw power now than ever in its history; the story of the Realm should be one of ever-increasing might and territory as its Exalted population grows.<br /> <br /> But yes, you can do it! The constraints are: birth rate, Exaltation rate, death rate, starting population size, with population growth and final population size falling out of these. You can solve the problem by changing any of these constraints - you just have to change <i>something</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's probably <b>some </b>number between &quot;ten thousand&quot; and &quot;tens of millions&quot;, isn't there?<br /> <br /> And the Wyld Hunt is understaffed largely because, in the last five years, the number of Anathema in Creation has doubled, and because a political crisis has thinned its ranks still further. You don't need that much to explain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:43:16-07:00","id":216214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216202#post216202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's probably <b>some </b>number between &quot;ten thousand&quot; and &quot;tens of millions&quot;, isn't there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends - how low do you want to set the growth rate? Couch gave a (birth*exaltation - death) rate of 0.9%, and while my numbers for that calculation aren't quite the same as his, they still give you a population of ~10 million. If you want something more like 100,000 over 768 years, you're talking about a (birth*exaltation - death) rate of ~0.3%.<br /> <br /> &quot;Growth rate&quot; is a dependent variable, of course, so the question is really, &quot;Where do you want to set the birth, Exaltation, and death rates?&quot; If the total difference is only 0.3%, you still can't justify the books' seeming opinion of &quot;Children of Dragon-Blooded are likely to Exalt, and Dragon-Blooded have <i>lots</i> of kids.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the Wyld Hunt is understaffed largely because, in the last five years, the number of Anathema in Creation has doubled, and because a political crisis has thinned its ranks still further. You don't need that much to explain it. </div> </div> </div>Right, which works fine with a stable DB population, but less well when there are a thousand times more Dragon-Blooded now than at the Realm's founding. That's what I mean - the presentation of an empire in decline gets harder to justify when the DBs are increasing and the Celestials are a static number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 08-01-2014, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:55:00-07:00","id":216230,"title":"","content":"I never thought the Realm was an empire in decline. It's an empire in crisis, but unquestionably the most powerful state in Creation.<br /> <br /> And do we need to know the growth rate over the last 768 years? The Realm has fought some massive wars over that time, do we know what effect they've had on the population? Do we need to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T16:30:53-07:00","id":216285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216230#post216230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And do we need to know the growth rate over the last 768 years? The Realm has fought some massive wars over that time, do we know what effect they've had on the population? Do we need to?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really - averages have a lovely way of swallowing up that kind of thing. The point is that you want averages that are workable approximations to a much more complex reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T22:41:28-07:00","id":216494,"title":"","content":"It was my boyfriend who first introduced me to Exalted, years ago. It wasn't long before I started noticing that the numbers given in the books for various things didn't add up, and didn't agree with each other from one book to the next. His advice, quite helpful, was to just ignore any number I read. That approach has worked pretty well ever since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-02-2014, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T07:47:29-07:00","id":216753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216187#post216187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not to mention, with houses rising and falling, keeping the number of Dragon-Bloods fixed at some number would be an incredible feat all by itself and even if it succeeded probably the only thing it would accomplish would be creating several times as many bastards outside the dynasty.<br /> <br /> NOT TO MENTION, Terrestrials are nothing if not fecund. The libido of the Dragon-Blooded is the subject of plays throughout Creation. It's in their very essence to multiply. The idea of a Dragon-Blooded population that stagnates at a certain level is unnatural and hard to believe, possibly blasphemy against the elemental dragons themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is never a good idea to have a larger aristocracy than your state can support, and Dynastic Dragon-Blooded are nothing if not aristocracy. And it is not like you cannot have more children, you just need to pay extra... which may accidentally give an edge to certain houses and disadvantage others, but definitely will help the Imperial coffers, and limit exactly the houses most keen to expand their numbers and thus power.<br /> <br /> As for bastards? Oh sure, whenever the Dragonblooded are somewhere in the Threshhold, you can bet your last obol that, sure enough, there will be a few kids born in about a year\u00b4s time whom the Dragons will take a fancy to - whether simply born to local women or &quot;orphans&quot; surreptitiously raised near the Vacation villas that the Princes/ses of the Earth frequent. It is the <i>legitimate </i>heirs of the Great Houses that are limited . In case, you might even wonder if it wasn\u00b4t intended by someone to work just that way in order to provide the Empire with a ready supply of fresh blood eager to join in, without any ties to the established houses and willing enough to certain positions in the Dragon-Blooded host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T10:35:15-07:00","id":216800,"title":"","content":"Actual aristocratic families, historically, limit their own reproduction, because you don't want too many heirs, family members you can't support and won't inherit. Those who don't have any titles to inherit are given to the church. But Dynastic families are very different. Their wealth and noble status isn't based on titles, being the Earl of Something or the Duke of Whatever, and so, having a finite number of titles doesn't impose any restrictions on their growth. And for the same reason, their growth does not pose such problems to the monarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-02-2014, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T11:13:29-07:00","id":216810,"title":"","content":"I can't find offhand a reason why the Empress would try to keep the number of Dragonblooded in the Realm static, though I'm sure one has been provided somewhere. Regardless, if they actually followed the policies described in the books, the structure of the Realm would collapse in that there would be no mortals anymore, everyone would be Dragonblooded. This is something I have considered as a method of defeating the Celestial Exalted, starving the Exaltations of hosts, but I'm pretty sure it's not supposed to be what the Realm is <i>actually doing</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T12:43:15-07:00","id":216824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216800#post216800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actual aristocratic families, historically, limit their own reproduction, because you don't want too many heirs, family members you can't support and won't inherit. Those who don't have any titles to inherit are given to the church. But Dynastic families are very different. Their wealth and noble status isn't based on titles, being the Earl of Something or the Duke of Whatever, and so, having a finite number of titles doesn't impose any restrictions on their growth. And for the same reason, their growth does not pose such problems to the monarch.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Empire, the pressure actually comes from the Empress rather than the great ouses themselves. I think the idea was a purely selfish one - the Empress did it in order to limit the power base of her potential rivals and keep them easier to control or at least keep tabs on. Left to themselves, the great houses would surely want to expand, but those who do so beyond a limit the Empress set would have to pay for it... either fees or no further subsidies, I don't remember which one at the moment, but either are good for the Imperial treasury. If you are not worried about an external foe - and the Empire during its heyday had no reason to be - then ensuring internal stability and safety becomes a top priority for the ruler. It definitely sacrifices a fair bit of the possible effectiveness of the Dragon-Blooded host, but I think from the standpoint of someone who made the working of the empire pretty much contingent on herself it makes sense.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the two avenues open to Found Eggs - and the system, by making it undesirable to have a large number of legitimate heirs, tacitly encourages at least some extramarital procreation - herd them into the organisations that the Great Houses would (at least imo) have the hardest time controlling. The Immaculate order is strictly neutral but the Empress is probably the outsider with the most sway, and Pasiap's Stair prepares them to be officers loyal to the Realm, not to a great house. To me, this is a further indication that the system was planned in a way to limit those whom the Empress saw as the most likely potential rivals and solidify her own power base. It does mean sacrificing the overall potential of the Empire against an external threat, but for the vast majority of the Realm's history, there simply was no (credible) outside threat to its existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 08-02-2014, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T14:50:45-07:00","id":216956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216824#post216824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of the Empire, the pressure actually comes from the Empress rather than the great ouses themselves. I think the idea was a purely selfish one - the Empress did it in order to limit the power base of her potential rivals and keep them easier to control or at least keep tabs on. Left to themselves, the great houses would surely want to expand, but those who do so beyond a limit the Empress set would have to pay for it... either fees or no further subsidies, I don't remember which one at the moment, but either are good for the Imperial treasury. If you are not worried about an external foe - and the Empire during its heyday had no reason to be - then ensuring internal stability and safety becomes a top priority for the ruler. It definitely sacrifices a fair bit of the possible effectiveness of the Dragon-Blooded host, but I think from the standpoint of someone who made the working of the empire pretty much contingent on herself it makes sense.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the two avenues open to Found Eggs - and the system, by making it undesirable to have a large number of legitimate heirs, tacitly encourages at least some extramarital procreation - herd them into the organisations that the Great Houses would (at least imo) have the hardest time controlling. The Immaculate order is strictly neutral but the Empress is probably the outsider with the most sway, and Pasiap's Stair prepares them to be officers loyal to the Realm, not to a great house. To me, this is a further indication that the system was planned in a way to limit those whom the Empress saw as the most likely potential rivals and solidify her own power base. It does mean sacrificing the overall potential of the Empire against an external threat, but for the vast majority of the Realm's history, there simply was no (credible) outside threat to its existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize this is the official explanation but I'm not buying it. In the first place, the Empress comes off as weak if she can't manage a growing number of subjects and has to try and keep them from reproducing. In the second place, forbidding them to reproduce, or charging money for it? Surely that's going to make enemies of her subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T15:09:11-07:00","id":216983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216956#post216956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realize this is the official explanation but I'm not buying it. In the first place, the Empress comes off as weak if she can't manage a growing number of subjects and has to try and keep them from reproducing. In the second place, forbidding them to reproduce, or charging money for it? Surely that's going to make enemies of her subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>She kept power in spite of several attempted coups. I doubt that she would care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T16:04:24-07:00","id":217021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216956#post216956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realize this is the official explanation but I'm not buying it. In the first place, the Empress comes off as weak if she can't manage a growing number of subjects and has to try and keep them from reproducing. In the second place, forbidding them to reproduce, or charging money for it? Surely that's going to make enemies of her subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm gonna get in trouble for this, but: Is it nice in your world? Do the unicorns fart golden rainbows?<br /> <br /> Administration is tough. That's in this world. Right now. With enough tech and modernization to choke a behemoth. The number one reason empires have fallen in our world is simply getting too big and complicated to handle with the bureaucracy. Best example of that? The British Empire. Ran itself right into the crapper by becoming too big to not waste money and administrators on useless stuff.<br /> <br /> Even with all the Charms and other magic, the Realm has never been presented as having an administrative apparatus equivalent to even modern Greece. So, it simply cannot handle population over a certain amount. Especially when that population has tons of Charm-slinging self-entitled yahoos. And that's presuming the administration of the Realm was meant to be clear and efficient. Which the Empress explicitly did not design it to be. To say she can't handle an infinitely growing number of Charm-slinging aristos isn't calling her weak. A Solar couldn't handle an infinitely increasing empire of Charm-slinging aristos. If she could handle it, then your idea of a Silver Emperor is crap, because she already has a progrram in every small dort-farmer village in Creation to capture and imprison each new Lunar in her Lunar-proof detention facility where they spend the millenia staring at a blank wall, drugged to the gills, because them roaming around was just too disruptive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T17:51:42-07:00","id":217081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>phalamir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217021#post217021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna get in trouble for this, but: Is it nice in your world? Do the unicorns fart golden rainbows?<br /> <br /> Administration is tough. That's in this world. Right now. With enough tech and modernization to choke a behemoth. The number one reason empires have fallen in our world is simply getting too big and complicated to handle with the bureaucracy. Best example of that? The British Empire. Ran itself right into the crapper by becoming too big to not waste money and administrators on useless stuff.<br /> <br /> Even with all the Charms and other magic, the Realm has never been presented as having an administrative apparatus equivalent to even modern Greece. So, it simply cannot handle population over a certain amount. Especially when that population has tons of Charm-slinging self-entitled yahoos. And that's presuming the administration of the Realm was meant to be clear and efficient. Which the Empress explicitly did not design it to be. To say she can't handle an infinitely growing number of Charm-slinging aristos isn't calling her weak. A Solar couldn't handle an infinitely increasing empire of Charm-slinging aristos. If she could handle it, then your idea of a Silver Emperor is crap, because she already has a progrram in every small dort-farmer village in Creation to capture and imprison each new Lunar in her Lunar-proof detention facility where they spend the millenia staring at a blank wall, drugged to the gills, because them roaming around was just too disruptive.</div> </div> </div> </div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The Realm is the most prosperous empire in Creation. It doesn't seem like it's anywhere near its carrying capacity in terms of population.</li> <li>We're not talking about the population of the Realm anyway, but the number of Dragon-Blooded.</li> <li>If the Realm's administrative apparatus is so inadequate, doesn't that just make it even less plausible that the Empress, somehow, keeps the Dragon-Blooded population from growing beyond 10,000?</li> <li>Even if she could do it, it seems like a terrible, self-defeating policy, to me, if the idea is that it's supposed to ensure her safety. Because forbidding Dragon-Bloods from reproducing, charging fees, removing subsidies, licensing them to breed like they're animals, however it's supposed to work? That can't possibly sit well with them. I'm pretty sure dynasts don't enjoy being treated like chattel.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-02-2014, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T18:59:36-07:00","id":217116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217081#post217081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure dynasts don't enjoy being treated like chattel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Said in a thread about Lunars breeding Dragon-Blooded like chattel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T20:12:34-07:00","id":217129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217116#post217116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Said in a thread about Lunars breeding Dragon-Blooded like chattel.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UD9WiTTE6FU\" data-code=\"zehSKo5CJWY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zehSKo5CJWY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-02-2014, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T21:19:16-07:00","id":217153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217116#post217116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Said in a thread about Lunars breeding Dragon-Blooded like chattel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think the thread was about enslaving Dragon-Bloods, much less enslaving dynasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-03-2014, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T06:12:32-07:00","id":217337,"title":"","content":"What the crap else are you going to call it? They're certainly not <i>free</i>. Some furry psycho is breeding them, like Pok\u00e9mon in reverse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And to those of you who, pages ago, said, &quot;Well, the Lunar and DBs can be friends!&quot;, well, maybe it's just reservations born out of modern-day sensibilities, but I like to think that if a person in my social in-group started dictating that some of us will have to get to baby-making with each other, and that he or she was going to oversee it, dictating all such pairings for a dozen or a hundred generations to ensure it culminates in some grand vision of his or hers, <b>I would not think of that person as my friend.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why does this need explaining?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-03-2014, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T07:11:47-07:00","id":217381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217337#post217337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the crap else are you going to call it? They're certainly not <i>free</i>. Some furry psycho is breeding them, like Pok\u00e9mon in reverse.<br /> <br /> And to those of you who, pages ago, said, &quot;Well, the Lunar and DBs can be friends!&quot;, well, maybe it's just reservations born out of modern-day sensibilities, but I like to think that if a person in my social in-group started dictating that some of us will have to get to baby-making with each other, and that he or she was going to oversee it, dictating all such pairings for a dozen or a hundred generations to ensure it culminates in some grand vision of his or hers, <b>I would not think of that person as my friend.</b><br /> <br /> Why does this need explaining?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're exaggerating. There was nothing in the OP about dictating who ruts with who over a dozen or a hundred generations. Why would anyone need to do that, when Dragon-Blooded families do that on their own? Do you think dynasts get to choose who they marry? Not in my reading of it. Those decisions are made by their parents and elders, and every Great House of the Realm manages its bloodline with an eye toward, above all, increasing their rate of Exaltation (which is another problem for the idea that the Empress keeps the number of Dragon-Bloods at exactly 10,000).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T08:01:29-07:00","id":217401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217381#post217381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're exaggerating. There was nothing in the OP about dictating who ruts with who over a dozen or a hundred generations. Why would anyone need to do that, when Dragon-Blooded families do that on their own? Do you think dynasts get to choose who they marry? Not in my reading of it. Those decisions are made by their parents and elders, and every Great House of the Realm manages its bloodline with an eye toward, above all, increasing their rate of Exaltation (which is another problem for the idea that the Empress keeps the number of Dragon-Bloods at exactly 10,000).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call house heads &quot;friends&quot; to the offspring they use as game pieces, either. On their own, outside of any giant breeding project, Dragon-Blooded don't necessarily always pair with other Dragon-Blooded. There's no inborn drive for Dragon-Blooded to act in a manner far different from &quot;get together with someone you are fond of&quot;, which is quite possibly means that the Terrestrial's prospective spouse in the Threshold is mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T08:05:22-07:00","id":217406,"title":"","content":"The only places where a Terrestrial is even likely to have another Terrestrial to decide to be in a relationship with are places like the Realm and Lookshy, anyway, but let's say a Lunar starts collecting DBs, again, like some sort of reverse Pok\u00e9mon. What happens when the two DBs he gets are gay, or just plain aren't attracted to each other? What if one's already got a wife?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T08:07:56-07:00","id":217407,"title":"","content":"I think if the lunars wanted to encourage terrestrials in an area to pair up subtle matchmaking is probably the way to go. <br /> <br /> Eg, turning into a crab and singing &quot;Kiss de girl&quot; during boat rides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T08:09:49-07:00","id":217409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217407#post217407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if the lunars wanted to encourage terrestrials in an area to pair up subtle matchmaking is probably the way to go.<br /> <br /> Eg, turning into a crab and singing &quot;Kiss de girl&quot; during boat rides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a stunt, it's really only subtle if you do it just once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T09:00:50-07:00","id":217424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217381#post217381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're exaggerating.</div> </div> </div> </div>No shit, really?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There was nothing in the OP about dictating who ruts with who over a dozen or a hundred generations. </div> </div> </div>Not in those terms, but yeah, it's there - without the Lunar performing some ludicrous feats of matchmaking, the Dragon's blood is going to peter out in generations. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would anyone need to do that, when Dragon-Blooded families do that on their own? </div> </div> </div>You don't have a &quot;Dragon-Blooded family,&quot; you have perhaps a handful of Outcastes that have a dozen or more generations separating them from any other Exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think dynasts get to choose who they marry? Not in my reading of it. Those decisions are made by their parents and elders\u2026 </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing you haven't been in an arranged marriage - please correct me if I'm wrong - but let's go ahead and try and pretend for a minute. If your family pairs you up with someone you're not attracted to, that's gonna put a strain on your relationship with them, yes? Being engaged to someone you loathe, what's that gonna do? Now, instead of your family deciding this, it's the furry psycho who dragged you out of your home and family in the Hundred Kingdoms because he wants to summon an army out of your vagina.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>What the fuck is wrong with people, thinking people will just be okay with this?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T09:03:33-07:00","id":217426,"title":"","content":"Surprise, surprise, forcing arranged marriages on people regardless of their preferences isn't that far divorced from slavery. That your family sells you into slavery also doesn't particularly make it better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Additionally, even if my Lunar &quot;friend&quot; tells us that we're free to micromanage our children's marriages ourselves, as long as we pop out an obedient army of Exalts for him, as opposed to him being the decider, <b>that still makes him a not-friend.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No relationship the Lunar possesses with his cadre of DBs can be equal or amicable, let alone be described as &quot;friendship&quot;, as long as it's his intent to use them to breed an army.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-03-2014, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T09:42:46-07:00","id":217468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217401#post217401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call house heads &quot;friends&quot; to the offspring they use as game pieces, either. On their own, outside of any giant breeding project, Dragon-Blooded don't necessarily always pair with other Dragon-Blooded. There's no inborn drive for Dragon-Blooded to act in a manner far different from &quot;get together with someone you are fond of&quot;, which is quite possibly means that the Terrestrial's prospective spouse in the Threshold is mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded who are interested in having a family naturally prefer to pair with other Dragon-Blooded. And it's in their interest to pair with somone with good blood, because they want their children and grandchildren to be Exalted, like them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217406#post217406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only places where a Terrestrial is even likely to have another Terrestrial to decide to be in a relationship with are places like the Realm and Lookshy, anyway</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, why? Terrestrials live hundreds of years, they inevitably learn of each other and have freedom to travel and opportunities to meet. They certainly do meet outside of the Realm and Lookshy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217406#post217406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but let's say a Lunar starts collecting DBs, again, like some sort of reverse Pok\u00e9mon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not say that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217406#post217406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when the two DBs he gets are gay, or just plain aren't attracted to each other? What if one's already got a wife?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember Nellens Malakai and Mnemon Tirhon? For a prince of the blood, there are responsibilities. Being gay doesn't excuse you from doing your duty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217424#post217424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing you haven't been in an arranged marriage - please correct me if I'm wrong - but let's go ahead and try and pretend for a minute. If your family pairs you up with someone you're not attracted to, that's gonna put a strain on your relationship with them, yes? Being engaged to someone you loathe, what's that gonna do? Now, instead of your family deciding this, it's the furry psycho who dragged you out of your home and family in the Hundred Kingdoms because he wants to summon an army out of your vagina.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Are we kidnapping Dragon-Bloods now?<br /> <br /> But no, I don't think arranged marriage is an offensive concept to nobles in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-03-2014, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T09:51:27-07:00","id":217475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217426#post217426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprise, surprise, forcing arranged marriages on people regardless of their preferences isn't that far divorced from slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, my wife worked with an Indian lady who was in an arranged marriage and who felt, basically, that it was a vastly superior institution in all ways: benefited from the wisdom and experience of older family members, wasn't swayed by the foolish vagaries of young people, etc. &quot;You learn to love your husband,&quot; she said; in her view (which, I gather, was pretty typical for her background), love marriages were kind of irresponsible and selfish.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying she's right, and I'm certainly glad that I got to pick my own spouse - but &quot;slavery&quot; is maybe a little bit of an overstatement re: arranged marriage. I can definitely believe in a society where Dragons-marrying-Dragons was what everyone understood to be the &quot;responsible&quot; thing to do and objecting to it was the weird, childish thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T10:20:45-07:00","id":217495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217475#post217475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, my wife worked with an Indian lady who was in an arranged marriage and who felt, basically, that it was a vastly superior institution in all ways: benefited from the wisdom and experience of older family members, wasn't swayed by the foolish vagaries of young people, etc. &quot;You learn to love your husband,&quot; she said; in her view (which, I gather, was pretty typical for her background), love marriages were kind of irresponsible and selfish.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying she's right, and I'm certainly glad that I got to pick my own spouse - but &quot;slavery&quot; is maybe a little bit of an overstatement re: arranged marriage. I can definitely believe in a society where Dragons-marrying-Dragons was what everyone understood to be the &quot;responsible&quot; thing to do and objecting to it was the weird, childish thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference that needs to be teased out in this conversation between an 'arranged marriage' (which has the consent of all involved and is realtively morally unproblematic) and a 'forced marriage' (which doesn't and is problematic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":978,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","user":"Iozz-Sothoth","date":". 08-03-2014, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T10:20:50-07:00","id":217496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217475#post217475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, my wife worked with an Indian lady who was in an arranged marriage and who felt, basically, that it was a vastly superior institution in all ways: benefited from the wisdom and experience of older family members, wasn't swayed by the foolish vagaries of young people, etc. &quot;You learn to love your husband,&quot; she said; in her view (which, I gather, was pretty typical for her background), love marriages were kind of irresponsible and selfish.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying she's right, and I'm certainly glad that I got to pick my own spouse - but &quot;slavery&quot; is maybe a little bit of an overstatement re: arranged marriage. I can definitely believe in a society where Dragons-marrying-Dragons was what everyone understood to be the &quot;responsible&quot; thing to do and objecting to it was the weird, childish thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about people going from other institutions to the one mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T10:56:00-07:00","id":217525,"title":"","content":"Are we? When did that happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T11:01:22-07:00","id":217528,"title":"","content":"If they're Outcastes, they do not come from a Dynastic background, so arranged marriages are not a given.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If they're not Outcastes, a Lunar isn't going to be able to get them to be part of this sick fucking thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T13:27:34-07:00","id":217568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217528#post217528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're Outcastes, they do not come from a Dynastic background, so arranged marriages are not a given.<br /> <br /> If they're not Outcastes, a Lunar isn't going to be able to get them to be part of this sick fucking thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither of those statements is necessarily true. You\u2019re just not using your imagination here, Alucard.<br /> <br /> Take, for instance, the Myriarchate of Tethys, an autonomous province in the far north. In centuries past, the region was a tributary of the Realm, and over time, the blood of dragons found its way into the local aristocratic families, many of whom received the Grace of the Air Dragon. When the Great House to which the Myriarch paid tribute fell out of favor with the Empress, their wealth and power was broken, and their legions and garrisons withdrew, leaving their former tributaries to fend for themselves.<br /> <br /> Into this tableau, in RY 522, came Masuda Storm-Thrush, an outcaste from the coastal states. The bastard daughter of an exceptionally well-bred Mnemon, Storm-Thrush was not permitted adoption into the house of her Exalted kin because of her relatively low birth to a serving woman, and because, in their judgment, she represented only contamination, being, unusually, an Aspect of Air. Filled with scorn for her dynastic relatives, she led a tempestuous and bloody life as a mercenary, hacking her way around the battlefields of Creation before one day finding herself a dragonlord, leading the forces of then-Myriarch Tarsios IV Tzymenides in defense against the fae.<br /> <br /> Rewards and honors followed her victories, and it was around this time that she met, or rather became re-introduced, to the man who would in later years be her husband, a wealthy townsman who was, in fact, the Chosen of Luna called Rain Falls in Silence.<br /> <br /> The two were a perfect match, and in centuries to come rarely left each other\u2019s side. Rain\u2019s wealth and Masuda\u2019s rising prominence ensured that their children (of whom several Exalted) married well, integrating their blood into that of the local Dragon-Blooded aristocracy. Two centuries later, their children, grandchildren and great-great grandchildren have become a minor dynasty in the region. And with no slavery or rape required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T13:57:20-07:00","id":217576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217496#post217496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're talking about people going from other institutions to the one mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to be a bit of an assumption that they're necessarily coming in from other institutional systems, to me. &quot;Not all Outcastes practice arrange marriage&quot; vs. &quot;All Outcastes do not practice arranged marriage&quot; are very different - even in our world, I wouldn't be surprised if arranged marriage is the more common option.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't really change whether or not arranged marriage is basically slavery, even if so. (I agree with Iozz-Sothoth that there's some ambiguity of language going on here, though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 08-03-2014, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T16:26:48-07:00","id":217635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217568#post217568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two were a perfect match, and in centuries to come rarely left each other\u2019s side. Rain\u2019s wealth and Masuda\u2019s rising prominence ensured that their children (of whom several Exalted) married well, integrating their blood into that of the local Dragon-Blooded aristocracy. Two centuries later, their children, grandchildren and great-great grandchildren have become a minor dynasty in the region. And with no slavery or rape required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather tangential to the situation in the OP.<br /> Rain seems to have looked at the Lunars who want to bring down the Realm and said &quot;lol! good luck with that&quot;. I'm sure he holds to some vague Silver Pact obligations such as sheltering other Lunar Exalted from the Wyld Hunt if one of them Exalts on his doorstep but I can't imagine he's viewed as a dependable ally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T17:50:31-07:00","id":217690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217635#post217635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather tangential to the situation in the OP.<br /> <br /> Rain seems to have looked at the Lunars who want to bring down the Realm and said &quot;lol! good luck with that&quot;. I'm sure he holds to some vague Silver Pact obligations such as sheltering other Lunar Exalted from the Wyld Hunt if one of them Exalts on his doorstep but I can't imagine he's viewed as a dependable ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as his name suggests, he works quietly. But he has built up Tethys as a power in the north. And has established a dynasty of Terrestrial Exalts to wield that power.<br /> <br /> The characters I made up for that example, but Tethys is a city-state I've used before in games. It's hardly on good terms with the Realm. The local nobility has no interest in seing a return to foreign rule, and the ordinary people would hardly stand for it either. Tethys is a center of industry, the north's Nexus or Gem; they do good business with the Realm's enemies and their gods, the Diadocton, take a dim view of Immaculate meddling.<br /> <br /> And certainly no one in the burgeoning House Masuda wants to see the Realm back, unless it's for a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-03-2014, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T19:00:12-07:00","id":217760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217426#post217426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprise, surprise, forcing arranged marriages on people regardless of their preferences isn't that far divorced from slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think that alone will stop an entire civilization from practicing it, I've got an unpleasant dose of reality for you to swallow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T20:15:07-07:00","id":217834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217760#post217760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think that alone will stop an entire civilization from practicing it, I've got an unpleasant dose of reality for you to swallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but his objection isn't &quot;Lunars wouldn't do this because it's immoral&quot; it's &quot;people are handwaving the immoral aspects of this plan.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T20:27:53-07:00","id":217839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217834#post217834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but his objection isn't &quot;Lunars wouldn't do this because it's immoral&quot; it's &quot;people are handwaving the immoral aspects of this plan.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's &quot;This is impossible because Dragon-Bloods won't go along with this plan, it being immoral.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I've been trying to show that there's really no reason it has to be immoral. The OP suggested Lunars could breed Dragon-Bloods the way they breed beastmen. Lunar beastmen are generally their own descendants. If you're simply starting your own dynasty, there's no reason you have to be immoral about it. At least no more immoral than the heads of the Great Houses are, and no one complains what they do is impossible, because it's not.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not going to keep arguing the point forever. If you think it's impossible, fine. But my view is, there aren't many things that are impossible in Exalted, and this is by far not the hardest thing a Lunar can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T21:56:36-07:00","id":217881,"title":"","content":"Put words in my mouth again, TSk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T01:19:19-07:00","id":217966,"title":"","content":"So, some Lunar finds some Dragon Blooded, somehow makes friends with them, brings them together, looks over their lineages and ancestral histories as best she can in order to figure out which individuals have the highest chance to produce Dragon Blooded offspring, makes sure that they get together and have children, then figures out whom those children should marry in order to have the highest chance to produce Exalted offspring, and continues this process until she has a large force of Dragon Blooded...<br /> <br /> ... wait, that's sounding familiar. Maybe <i>exactly</i> like what the heads of the Realm and Lookshy and every other nation-state with Dragon Blooded have been doing since the First Age? Seriously, Dragon Blooded in Lookshy and the Realm don't get married to people they fall in love with - they get married to people their families tell them to get married to. Moreover, arranged marriage is probably the norm throughout most of Creation, just as it was the norm in our world for much of our history.<br /> <br /> Why would it be so horrifically monstrous that they'd need to kill the poor Lunar who is, at best, just making them a little more efficient at something that they already do anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-04-2014, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T04:56:55-07:00","id":218031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you think it's impossible, fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nooo, I\u2019m questioning the morality and so far you\u2019ve given me Beastmen breeding and Great House leaders.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T05:23:55-07:00","id":218041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=216810#post216810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find offhand a reason why the Empress would try to keep the number of Dragonblooded in the Realm static, though I'm sure one has been provided somewhere. Regardless, if they actually followed the policies described in the books, the structure of the Realm would collapse in that there would be no mortals anymore, everyone would be Dragonblooded. This is something I have considered as a method of defeating the Celestial Exalted, starving the Exaltations of hosts, but I'm pretty sure it's not supposed to be what the Realm is <i>actually doing</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm about 90% sure that she, before she vanished into the magic of the backround history of the game, explictly didn't want the number static, instituting a number of rules about &quot;All ya'll be making babies. Yes, even you. I don't care if you don't like men/women, you doin' it anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exagerated for effect, yes, but some rather strict rules about dragonblood being expected to breed.<br /> <br /> ...funny. That sounds...rather familure...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3444-revan058","name":"Revan058","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T05:30:17-07:00","id":218043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217834#post217834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but his objection isn't &quot;Lunars wouldn't do this because it's immoral&quot; it's &quot;people are handwaving the immoral aspects of this plan.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>His objection is based on interpreting said plan (which is vague enough to allow for it) in the absolute most negative way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T06:55:19-07:00","id":218115,"title":"","content":"To clarify, I'm not saying it's strictly impossible - it's just a really bad idea, both in the sense of being detestable <i>and</i> a 9.6 on the 10-point scale &quot;Will This Shit Blow Up In My Face?&quot;, all for a benefit that is dubious at best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, Exalted are the grandmasters of championing bad ideas, so, please, feel free to breed people like animals with the intent of stabbing the heart of the Realm with a sword made of its own blood. It may even work. But be <i>at least as</i> prepared for a glorious, hilarious failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T07:10:26-07:00","id":218124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=218115#post218115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify, I'm not saying it's strictly impossible - it's just a really bad idea, both in the sense of being detestable <i>and</i> a 9.6 on the 10-point scale &quot;Will This Shit Blow Up In My Face?&quot;, all for a benefit that is dubious at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, specifically, about the example I gave is detestable? I went to the trouble of creating two characters and a backstory just to serve as an example for you of how it might work without being detestable, and so far you haven't replied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-04-2014, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T08:07:58-07:00","id":218178,"title":"","content":"I seem to have either skimmed or missed your example, because I don't recall it. Mind reposting it, or at least telling me what page it is on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T08:21:00-07:00","id":218188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217568#post217568\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217568#post217568\"> Lunars, Breeding Projects and Lost Eggs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217568#post217568\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217568#post217568 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Seeing as Lunars have the best tools Creation-side to; locate, collect, and breed the Lost Eggs into a might host to bring down the Realm - one wonders why not? Beastmen are a thing that is used and Lunars are the unparalleled masters of all things, &amp;quot;breed that supersoldier&amp;quot;. With the Lunar </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T08:29:02-07:00","id":218198,"title":"","content":"Oh, that - yeah, I'd skimmed it after seeing words like &quot;Myriarchate.&quot; Also, it doesn't fit our argument - I'm complaining about cats, you showing me a picture of a dog and say, &quot;What about this one?&quot; is not going to sway me from my hatred of the fuzzy little Hitlers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:White\">Actually, I am reasonably fond of cats, even despite being allergic to them, but that's tangential to this discussion.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T08:33:46-07:00","id":218201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=218198#post218198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that - yeah, I'd skimmed it after seeing words like &quot;Myriarchate.&quot; Also, it doesn't fit our argument - I'm complaining about cats, you showing me a picture of a dog and say, &quot;What about this one?&quot; is not going to sway me from my hatred of the fuzzy little Hitlers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer cats to dogs.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://nedroid.com/imagesb/comicsaboutdogs.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T08:42:34-07:00","id":218205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=218198#post218198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that - yeah, I'd skimmed it after seeing words like &quot;Myriarchate.&quot; Also, it doesn't fit our argument - I'm complaining about cats, you showing me a picture of a dog and say, &quot;What about this one?&quot; is not going to sway me from my hatred of the fuzzy little Hitlers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:White\">Actually, I am reasonably fond of cats, even despite being allergic to them, but that's tangential to this discussion.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a word, I swear. <a href=\"http://www.thefreedictionary.com/myriarch\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.thefreedictionary.com/myriarch</a><br /> <br /> What doesn't fit about it? It concerns a Lunar who has bred a dynasty of Dragon-Bloods in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> I've been saying that there are more ways of doing it than being a furry psycho who abducts outcastes and forces them to breed. So if I can't give examples of other ways, I'm not sure what I can actually say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:01:43-07:00","id":218226,"title":"","content":"No, he hasn't. Breeding implies a deliberateness, a degree of micromanagement, that's just not in your example. If he hasn't been the one choosing mates, et cetera, <i>he hasn't bred them</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you throw out your leftovers onto a heap outside, and a rose-bush starts miraculously growing out of the refuse, it would be severely misleading, at best, to say that you &quot;grew&quot; the rose-bush.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, &quot;myriarch&quot; is an awkward as hell word, and notably a Greek one, which seems particularly out of place in the North.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-04-2014, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:33:41-07:00","id":218263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=218226#post218226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, he hasn't. Breeding implies a deliberateness, a degree of micromanagement, that's just not in your example. If he hasn't been the one choosing mates, et cetera, <i>he hasn't bred them</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was implied that he has been. I mean I did say they married their offspring to members of the local Dragon-Blooded aristocracy and built a dynasty out of it. Presumably that involves the same kind of decision-making that any Great House engages in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=218226#post218226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, &quot;myriarch&quot; is an awkward as hell word, and notably a Greek one, which seems particularly out of place in the North.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are indeed Greek elements to Tethys, including the name Tethys itself. Edit: and you pronounce it like <i>myriad.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 08-04-2014, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T18:38:16-07:00","id":219715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=218226#post218226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, he hasn't. Breeding implies a deliberateness, a degree of micromanagement, that's just not in your example. If he hasn't been the one choosing mates, et cetera, <i>he hasn't bred them</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've spent how many pages raging against this thread because of one single fucking word in the title?<br /> <br /> I'm at a loss for words. There are not enough images of Tommy Lee Jones staring disapprovingly on the internet to convey what I'm feeling right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Jesus tap dancing Christ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T05:50:23-07:00","id":220081,"title":"","content":"Pressuring your children for a certain kind of marriage is something that has happened pretty much throughout our history, even when the prizes on the line were much lower than a chance of your children becoming elemental demigods or members of a world-spanning aristocracy. How strict it is and what forms it will take may vary, but seriously, a desire for some sort of control over your family is only to be expected. And of course the patriarch or matriarch of a family will want to be obeyed and think s/he knows best, even when their desires are not universally shared by the descendants. This should be typical for many corners of Creation... though of course it may backfire every now and then. Plans do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I\u00b4d consider any serious long-term plan backed by concrete actions to improve the strength of a dragon-blooded bloodline as breeding, especially where an exalt has devoted time, resources and motes to beat the odds. Sure, it may sound crass, but if it quacks like a duck, walks like a duck and looks like a duck...<br /> <br /> (It\u00b4s an ANATHEMA!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","user":"4uk4ata","date":". 08-06-2014, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T06:48:27-07:00","id":220116,"title":"","content":"Well, this went downhill while I wasn't looking.<br /> <br /> Probably a bad time to talk about vivisecting dynasts to make Neomah babies, huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T07:16:46-07:00","id":220150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/207567-lunars-breeding-projects-and-lost-eggs?p=217475#post217475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying she's right, and I'm certainly glad that I got to pick my own spouse - but 